4667,start-x5-mipt-competition,"# Description

Ticks can be carriers of other microorganisms, which, in turn, can cause various diseases in humans, including encephalitis, lyme disease, monocytic ehrlichosis, granulocytic anaplasmosis. 


Most people are only aware of tick-borne encephalitis, so they turn to laboratories for analysis for tick-borne encephalitis, without conducting tests for other possible diseases.


How many ticks are a vector in the population depends on various factors, which in turn depend on the time of year, place, geographical location, time.


In order to take preventive measures in advance, it is important to know how the activity and population of ticks will change, the probability of their infection with other microorganisms.


It is possible to determine this from the historical data of the analysis results. 

You are invited to build a model that predicts the number of visits to clinics according to the 'Borrelia miyamotoi' tests
----------------------
# Evaluation

MAE (mean absolute error) will be used as a metric.","# Dataset Description

""date"" - ""You will be provided with data for 2 years based on the results of the tests. (Date of capture in the format yyyy-mm-dd hh:mm:ss)""

""region"" - ""The name of the region in which the test was conducted, a total of 67 unique values""

""invitro_count"" - ""Number of invitro clinics in the region""

""population"" - ""The population of the region""

""endemicity"" - ""The endemicity of the region (0 - a small probability of catching a tick, 3 - a large probability of catching a tick)""

""§£§Ú§â§å§ã §Ü§Ý§Ö§ë§Ö§Ó§à§Ô§à §ï§ß§è§Ö§æ§Ñ§Ý§Ú§ä§Ñ §²§¯§¬"" - ""The number of '§£§Ú§â§å§ã §Ü§Ý§Ö§ë§Ö§Ó§à§Ô§à §ï§ß§è§Ö§æ§Ñ§Ý§Ú§ä§Ñ' tests at the invitro clinic""

""Ehrlichia muris/chaffe§Önsis §¥§¯§¬"" - ""The number of 'Ehrlichia muris/chaffe§Önsis' tests at the invitro clinic""

""Anaplasma Phagocytophillum §¥§¯§¬"" - ""The number of 'Anaplasma Phagocytophillum' tests at the invitro clinic""

""Borrelia burgdorferi s.l §¥§¯§¬"" - ""The number of 'Borrelia burgdorferi s.l' tests at the invitro clinic""

""Borrelia miyamotoi §¥§¯§¬(target)"" - ""The number of 'Borrelia miyamotoi' tests at the invitro clinic""",True,True
4668,matrix-completion-summer-challenge,"# Description

This is our summer coding challenge. Find a quickstart notebook in the data section.
----------------------
# Evaluation

The evaluation is the RMSE over all three (25%, 50% and 75% removed) arrays.

The public leaderboard shows the results for the training arrays. The final scoring on the private leaderboard will be done on the three test arrays.","# Dataset Description

There are six three-dimensional data arrays in total. The dimensions of each are [time, lat, lon]. Each of them consists of 11 consecutive, distinct years of global monthly-average 2m-temperature reanalysis fields. For each of them a random set of values (25%, 50% or 75%) were set to NaN. Your job is to reconstruct the missing values as best as possible. The submission with the lowest reconstruction error, measured using the RMSE, wins. Follow the getting-started notebook to see how to create a submission that can be submitted to Kaggle.",True,True
