4682,machine-learning-regression-and-regularization,"# Description

Now that we're familiar with some basic regression and classification tasks, it's time to apply our knowledge. We have with us a dataset for video game sales for multiple consoles.
Your task is to predict the global sales for video games.
You are expected to perform EDA and data analysis based on your existing knowledge of statistics and visualisation, and engineer variables and manipulate to get the best MAE possible. You will check for missing values, categorical values, outliers and deal with them as you see fit.
You will split the data into training and testing (80:20).
May the force be with you and data always be in your favor.
----------------------
# Evaluation

The metric we will be chasing is mean absolute error, but feel free to present other values as well.
##Mean Absolute Error
Prediction Error ¡ú Actual Value - Predicted Value
This prediction error is taking for each record after which we convert all errors to positive. This is achieved by taking the absolute value for each error as below;
Absolute Error ¡ú |Prediction Error|
Finally, we calculate the mean for all recorded absolute errors (Average sum of all absolute errors).
MAE = Average of All absolute errors","# Dataset Description

##Content
Alongside the fields: Name, Platform, YearofRelease, Genre, Publisher, NASales, EUSales, JPSales, OtherSales, Global_Sales, we have:-

* Critic_score - Aggregate score compiled by Metacritic staff  
* Criticcount - The number of critics used in coming up with the Criticscore  
* User_score - Score by Metacritic's subscribers  
* Usercount - Number of users who gave the userscore  
* Developer - Party responsible for creating the game  
* Rating - The ESRB ratings",True,True
