4685,pjjda2021,"# Description

**LATIHAN MACHINE LEARNING PJJ DAS 2**

<p>
Dataset Information

This dataset contains information on default payments, demographic factors, credit data, history of payment, and bill statements of credit card clients in Taiwan from April 2005 to September 2005. </p>

<p></p> Content

There are 25 variables:

    ID: ID of each client
    LIMIT_BAL: Amount of given credit in NT dollars (includes individual and family/supplementary credit
    SEX: Gender (1=male, 2=female)
    EDUCATION: (1=graduate school, 2=university, 3=high school, 4=others, 5=unknown, 6=unknown)
    MARRIAGE: Marital status (1=married, 2=single, 3=others)
    AGE: Age in years
    PAY_0: Repayment status in September, 2005 (-1=pay duly, 1=payment delay for one month, 2=payment delay for two months, ¡­ 8=payment delay for eight months, 9=payment delay for nine months and above)
    PAY_2: Repayment status in August, 2005 (scale same as above)
    PAY_3: Repayment status in July, 2005 (scale same as above)
    PAY_4: Repayment status in June, 2005 (scale same as above)
    PAY_5: Repayment status in May, 2005 (scale same as above)
    PAY_6: Repayment status in April, 2005 (scale same as above)
    BILL_AMT1: Amount of bill statement in September, 2005 (NT dollar)
    BILL_AMT2: Amount of bill statement in August, 2005 (NT dollar)
    BILL_AMT3: Amount of bill statement in July, 2005 (NT dollar)
    BILL_AMT4: Amount of bill statement in June, 2005 (NT dollar)
    BILL_AMT5: Amount of bill statement in May, 2005 (NT dollar)
    BILL_AMT6: Amount of bill statement in April, 2005 (NT dollar)
    PAY_AMT1: Amount of previous payment in September, 2005 (NT dollar)
    PAY_AMT2: Amount of previous payment in August, 2005 (NT dollar)
    PAY_AMT3: Amount of previous payment in July, 2005 (NT dollar)
    PAY_AMT4: Amount of previous payment in June, 2005 (NT dollar)
    PAY_AMT5: Amount of previous payment in May, 2005 (NT dollar)
    PAY_AMT6: Amount of previous payment in April, 2005 (NT dollar)
    default.payment.next.month: Default payment (1=yes, 0=no) <p></p>



----------------------
# Evaluation

<p></p> Evaluasi menggunakan AUC <p></p>","# Dataset Description

<p> Data Train dan Data Test <p>",True,True
4686,nyu-computer-vision-csci-ga2271-2021,"# Description

<p>In this assignment, your goal is to achieve the highest&nbsp;test set accuracy on the&nbsp;<a href=""http://benchmark.ini.rub.de/?section=gtsrb&amp;subsection=news"" target=""_blank"">German Traffic Sign Recognition Benchmark</a>.&nbsp;</p>
<p>

You should follow the instructions for assignment in the Colab notebook on the course webpage <a> here </a>. This specifies a simple convolutional network architecture. 

You should modify this, implementing tricks covered in class, to produce models that yield improved performance. The template code will produce a CSV as output that contains predictions for the test set images. This should be uploaded to this website, which will then score the results.</p>
<p>Good luck training your models! &nbsp;</p>
<h2>Acknowledgements</h2>
<p>Many thanks to <strong>Anirudhan J. Rajagopalan</strong>, the class TA from 2016 and  <strong>Soumith Chintala </strong> (FB AI Research), for putting this assignment together.&nbsp;</p>
----------------------
# Evaluation

<p>The evaluation metric used will be classification accuracy, i.e. the fraction of test examples for which the predicted label agrees with the ground truth label.</p>
<p>You should use the submission format specified in the template code. The first column lists the image ID, the second is the predicted label.&nbsp;</p>",# Dataset Description,True,True
