4718,aipi350-optimization,"# Description

<p>This is an INDIVIDUAL competition. You can use any material, but not allowed to contact anyone but the professor </p>

<p>A Major electrical car manufacturer Tesma has requested NBZ media to build an advertisement plan for the following 2 weeks. Tesma wants to air 30 sec commercials, in such a way that they reach at least 50 million male users 30-50 years old and 60 million female users 20-50 years old. Tesma does not allow NBZ to schedule more than 10 spots in the same day and more than 2 spots in a particular show/day combination. </p>

<p> Tesma requires an even distribution of spots (accumulated across all days) across shows, requiring the number of spots not to vary more than 20% across shows. For example, if one show has 100 spots, other shows can only have 80 to 120 spots assigned. Similarly, Tesma needs an even distribution across days, allowing only a maximum of 30% variation across days.</p>

<p>
Tesma's budget is $10,000, which means the plan cannot exceed this amount, but it is in NBZ'a interest to get as close to the budget as possible.
</p>

<p>The available TV shows, their cost (dollars per one spot) and expected audience (millions per one spot) are provided in the data.
</p>

<p>
Formulate an optimization problem to decide how to schedule Tesma commercials.
</p>

<p>
Code tip to read data with two sets in SAS:</p>
`read data kaagle into SET1=[data_col_name_1];`
`read data kaagle into SET2=[data_col_name_2];`
`read data kaagle into`
    `   [data_col_name_1 data_col_name_2]`
    `   input_num1=data_col_name_3`
    `   input_num2=data_col_name_4;`


----------------------
# Evaluation

<p>Your solution will be compared against the optimum solution and an RMSE score calculated.</p>","# Dataset Description

The Kaagle_Competition_Data has the available Shows, Dates and their cost (dollars per one spot) and expected audience (millions per one spot).

The kaagle_mapping shows the mapping of the variable id to the Show/Date combination. 

The kaagle_sample_solution has the exact format that your solutions needs to have to be uploaded. Any other format or column names will be rejected.",True,True
