4762,miedu-duyduc-absa,"# Description

# Project Definition
## Background

Sentiment analysis is part of the Natural Language Processing (NLP) techniques that consists in extracting emotions related to some raw texts. This is usually used on social media posts and customer reviews in order to automatically understand if some users are positive or negative and why. 

This project will use TripAdvisor data for this project. Each observation consists in one customer review for one hotel. Each customer review is composed of a textual feedback of the customer's experience at the hotel and an overall rating. The data can be found here: https://www.kaggle.com/c/miedu-duyduc-absa 

##Objectives
Final check of overall knowledge that students have acquired during Full-Stack Data Science Bootcamp.

##Question Researches
For each textual review, we want to predict if it corresponds to a good review (the customer is happy) or to a bad one (the customer is not satisfied). The reviews overall ratings can range from 1 to 5 stars. There is a special class names `No Rating` meaning user hasn't left any rating to that aspect.

## Expected Outcomes
Build a model that is capable of predicting sentiment of a review on TripAdvisor
Applying Sentiment Analysis technique to resolve a real application problem


----------------------
# Evaluation

&gt; Submissions are evaluated using `F1` between the predicted and expected answers.","# Dataset Description

## Files

*   **train.tsv** - the training set
*   **test.tsv** - the test set

## Columns

1. Number of Airline
2. Name of Airline
3. Reviewer name
4. Review rating
5. Review Date
6. Review Title
7. Review Text
8. Some tags about this flight: each tag is seperated by `|`
9. Date of travel
11. Responser Name
12. Response Date
13. Response Text
14. Reviewer Profile Url
15. Nationality of Airline
16. Crawl Time
17. Legroom
18. Seat comfort
19. In-flight Entertainment
20. Customer services
21. Value for money
22. Cleanliness
23. Check-in and boarding
24. Food and Beverage

*Last 8 columns are 8 aspect rating that I splited for you. These are also your predictions in `test data`*

###  Meaning of aspect-rating values:
* `-1` means customer hasn't rated this aspect
* `1` to `5` equais to its rating star",True,True
4763,bkai-neopolyp,"# Description

This compet is test!!!
----------------------
# Evaluation

The evaluation is based on Dice coefficient.

---


## Submission Format

n order to reduce the submission file size, our metric uses run-length encoding on the pixel values. Instead of submitting an exhaustive list of indices for your segmentation, you will submit pairs of values that contain a start position and a run length. E.g. '1 3' implies starting at pixel 1 and running a total of 3 pixels (1,2,3).

The competition format requires a space delimited list of pairs. For example, '1 3 10 5' implies pixels 1,2,3,10,11,12,13,14 are to be included in the mask. The pixels are one-indexed
and numbered from top to bottom, then left to right: 1 is pixel (1,1), 2 is pixel (2,1), etc.

The metric checks that the pairs are sorted, positive, and the decoded pixel values are not duplicated. It also checks that no two predicted masks for the same image are overlapping.

The file should contain a header and have the following format. Each row in your submission represents a single predicted nucleus segmentation for the given id.
---
