4785,utkml-nba-prediction-competition,"# Description

##UtkML NBA Prediction Competition
Sports fans and announcers alike try to make predictions on the outcome of NBA games with many conflicting arguments and with little avail. In this competition you will use machine learning to make predictions on the outcome of NBA games with the datasets provided. Whoever makes the most accurate predictions wins.


## Provided Files
- **games_train.csv**

- **games_test.csv**

##Information about File Columns
- **GAME_ID**
   An ID provided to distinguish games from one another.

- **HOME\_TEAM\_ID**
   An ID provided to distinguish home teams from one another.

- **VISITOR\_TEAM\_ID**
   An ID provided to distinguish visitor teams from one another.

- **SEASON**
   The season each game took place in.

- **FG\_PCT\_home/away**
   Percentage of field goals made for home and away teams respectively.
   
- **FT_PCT\_home/away**
   Percentage of free throws made for home and away teams respectively.

- **FG3\_PCT\_home/away**
   Percentage of 3 point field goals made for home and away teams respectively.

- **AST\_home/away**
   Number of assists made by home and away teams respectively.

- **REB\_home/away**
   Number of rebounds made by home and away teams respectively.






----------------------
# Evaluation



## Evaluation Metric
The evaluation metric for this competition is Mean F-Score. For more information on [Mean F-Score](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/F-score) click the link. 

## Submission Format

Each file should be submitted as a .csv file. This file should contain two columns, `id` and `wins`. The data in the `wins` column should be treated as binary with a ""1"" denoting a win and a ""0"" denoting a loss.

The file should look like this:
```
id,wins
0,1
1,1
etc...
```","# Dataset Description

You are provided with two tabular datasets, both games_train.csv, and games_test.csv. You will train your model with the training data and evaluate it against the test data.


## Files

*   **games\_train.csv** - the training set
*   **games\_test.csv** - the test set


## Columns

- `GAME_ID` -
   An ID provided to distinguish games from one another.

- `HOME_TEAM_ID` -
   An ID provided to distinguish home teams from one another.

- `VISITOR_TEAM_ID` -
   An ID provided to distinguish visitor teams from one another.

- `SEASON` -
   The season each game took place in.

- `FG_PCT_home/away` -
   Percentage of field goals made for home and away teams respectively.
   
- `FT_PCT_home/away` -
   Percentage of free throws made for home and away teams respectively.

- `FG3_PCT_home/away` -
   Percentage of 3 point field goals made for home and away teams respectively.

- `AST_home/away` -
   Number of assists made by home and away teams respectively.

- `REB_home/away` -
   Number of rebounds made by home and away teams respectively.

## Evaluation
The score that we use to evaluate your performance is Mean F-score, also known as the [F1-score](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/F-score). This metric works similar to accuracy in that its values are 0-1, but it's more robust in that it is meant to work better on imbalanced datasets.",True,True
