4810,data-boot-camp-challenge,"# Description

Hello class! See [this page](https://www.kaggle.com/c/titanic) for a description of the project. 

I encourage all of you to try doing things on your own for a while before looking at the answers, but know that in the ""code"" and ""discussions"" section you can sort by ""most voted"" to see some phenomenal tutorials and tips for working with this data set. For a fantastic data analysis and machine learning guide in Jupyter Notebook form, see [this page](https://www.kaggle.com/startupsci/titanic-data-science-solutions) and/or [this page](https://www.kaggle.com/chapagain/titanic-solution-a-beginner-s-guide).
----------------------
# Evaluation

## Goal
It is your job to predict if a passenger survived the sinking of the Titanic or not.
For each passenger in the test set, you must predict a 0 or 1 value for the variable.

## Metric
Your score is the R2 score.

## Submission File Format
You should submit a csv file with exactly 179 entries plus a header row. Your submission will show an error if you have extra columns (beyond PassengerId and Survived) or rows.

The file should have exactly 2 columns:
* PassengerId (sorted in any order)
* Survived (contains your binary predictions: 1 for survived, 0 for deceased)
```
PassengerId,Survived
892,0
893,1
894,0
```
Etc.
You can download an example submission file (gender_submission.csv) on the Data page.","# Dataset Description

To get descriptions of the columns, see [this page](https://www.kaggle.com/c/titanic/data)",True,True
