4859,adml-final,"# Problem Statement

You work at a multinational bank that is aiming to increase it's market share. Recently, the bank have been promoting one of it¡¯s core products. A key issue is optimizing targeting for marketing is, under a growing pressure to increase profits and reduce costs.

As a data scientist, you are working on improving for the next marketing campaign with a greater effectiveness and ROI. In order to achieve this, we have to analyze the past consumer data, identify the patterns, and predict the consumer¡¯s propensity to buy the promoted product. The model result is a valuable tool to help the marketing team to use their budget wisely to target potential buyers. 
 
With the given training data, you need to train and fine-tune a series of models, and then apply the model to test data and predict the outcome. The ROC AUC will be used to evaluate the model performance

----------------------
# Questions


## Questions:

### 1.	(10 points) Import customer data. Do some basic exploratory data analysis to describe the data numerically or graphically. 
### 2.	(20 points) Based on training data, build and fine-tune a logistic regression model to predict if a customer will purchase or not. Please evaluate the model performance using cross-validation. 
### 3.	(20 points) Based on training data, build and fine-tune a catboost or xgboost model to predict if a customer will purchase or not. Please evaluate the model performance using cross-validation. Hint: Catboost has an internal encoding algorithm to handle categorical variables.  
### 4.	(10 points) Based on training data, build and fine-tune another non-tree based model, e.g., MLP, SVM etc. Please evaluate the model performance using cross-validation
### 5.	(20 points) Propose and build a stacking model based on previous models you have built. 
### 6.	(10 points) Based on previous models you have built, apply the model to test data and predict the outcome. 
### 7.	(10 points) If the marketing department want to use the prediction in question 6 directly to select the potential customers for the campaign, what potential problems do you see from this approach? What methods do you suggest to select the potential customers?  
----------------------
# Description

See data description under the ""Data"" Tag.
Please rename your submission file with:  netID + ""_final.csv""","# Dataset Description

Data is included in the file 

**Train.csv** - The training set

**Test.csv** - The test set

Each row represents a customer, each column contains following customer¡¯s attributes 

- 1 - `age`  

- 2 - `job`: type of job 

- 3 - `marital`: marital status 

- 4 - `education` 

- 5 - `default`: has credit in default? 

- 6 - `housing`: has housing loan? 

- 7 - `loan`: has personal loan? 

- 8 - `balance`: Balance of the individual.

- 9 - `contact`: contact communication type
 
- 10 - `month`: last contact month of year
 
- 11 - `day`: last contact day of the month
 
- 12 - `campaign`: number of contacts performed during this campaign and for this customer (numeric, includes last contact)

- 13 - `pdays`: number of days that passed by after the customer was last contacted from a previous campaign (numeric; -1 means customer was not previously contacted)

- 14 - `previous`: number of contacts performed before this campaign and for this customer (numeric)

- 15 - `poutcome`: outcome of the previous marketing campaign (categorical: `'failure'`, `'nonexistent'`,`'success'`)

Output variable (desired target):

- 16 - `y` - has the customer purchased the product? (binary: `'yes'`,`'no'`)",True,True
4860,ieeedatathon,"# Description

Welcome to the ""Mini-Datathon""! Gear yourselves up for an exciting real-world application challenge that we have in store for you. This is where you will have to give your brain a workout and use your skills, to make a Classification Model for the given situation!

## **About the data**
The apparel industry houses a huge amount and variety of data. At every step of the supply
chain, data is collected and stored by each supply chain actor. This data, when used intelligently,
can help with solving a good deal of problems for the industry.

Data mining and machine learning have been at the forefront of research, helping to solve
analytical problems and overcoming business problems. The power of data mining in analyzing big data has been proven in various studies.

This dataset includes various attributes of the apparel industry which may include the logistics of the department, incentives, amount of workers, time given for a target etc. The dataset comprises of over 1000 instances which need to be analyzed and used to **predict the productivity performance of the teams.**

## **Tasks**

**(a) Convert the target column i.e. `actual_productivity` column into three classes (0, 1, 2) using the given thresholds:**
- 0 (low productivity) for `actual_productivity` <= 0.5
- 1 (moderate productivity) for 0.5 < `actual_productivity` <= 0.8
- 2 (high productivity) for `actual_productivity` > 0.8

**(b) Create a classification model to classify productivity performance into defined classes (0, 1, 2).**

### Now that you have come this far, head to the data section and show us what you got!
![check](https://encrypted-tbn0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcSKRx5vM1A-WYg8cxu0FFYOU6HKOcHE7YRmww&usqp=CAU)
----------------------
# Evaluation

![check](https://media.makeameme.org/created/evaluate-form-an.jpg)","# Dataset Description

## Files

*   **train.csv** - the training set
*   **test.csv** - the test set
*   **sample_submission.csv** - a sample submission file in the correct format

## Columns

- date : Date in MM-DD-YYYY
- day : Day of the Week
- quarter : A portion of the month. A month was divided into four quarters
- department : Associated department with the instance
- team_no : Associated team number with the instance
- no_of_workers : Number of workers in each team
- no_of_style_change : Number of changes in the style of a particular product
- targeted_productivity : Targeted productivity set by the Authority for each team for each day.
- smv : Standard Minute Value, it is the allocated time for a task
- wip : Work in progress. Includes the number of unfinished items for products
- over_time : Represents the amount of overtime by each team in minutes
- incentive : Represents the amount of financial incentive (in BDT) that enables or motivates a particular course of action.
- idle_time : The amount of time when the production was interrupted due to several reasons
- idle_men : The number of workers who were idle due to production interruption
- **actual_productivity : The actual productivity that was delivered by the workers. It has to be categorized into three classes: 0 (low productivity), 1 (moderate productivity), 2 (high productivity).**

**All the best!**
### May the Accuracy be with You!
![check] (https://drivendata-public-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/go-forth-and-model.jpg)",True,True
4861,machine-learning-challenge-sistemas-embebidos,"# Description

**Descripci¨®n del reto**
En el siguiente enunciado se presenta el primer reto del curso de Sistemas embebidos de la universidad de los Andes, enfocado en Machine Learning. Este reto consiste en crear un modelo de ceros utilizando alg¨²n framework de inteligencia artificial (Tensorflow, PyTorch, SkLearn, etc) que sea capaz de clasificar de la mejor manera 4 tipos de se?ales de transito. 

Cada equipo debe subir las etiquetas de cierto conjunto de im¨¢genes de evaluaci¨®n que se encuentran adjuntos en el dataset. Al subir su archivo con etiquetas se asignar¨¢ de forma automatica el puntaje de precisi¨®n que tiene el modelo de cada uno de los equipos. La calificaci¨®n del modelo del challenge ser¨¢ proporcional al puntaje que cada equipo sea capaz de obtener. Es decir, las calificaciones del reto ser¨¢n distribuidas de la siguiente manera seg¨²n el puesto que obtengan al finalizar la competencia el d¨ªa **29 de octubre de 2021**: 

1. 5.0
2. 4.5
3. 4.0
4. 3.5

Una vez realicen y suban las etiquetas de las se?ales de transito del dataset de evaluaci¨®n, es necesario que realicen una presentaci¨®n en clase explicando la arquitectura que desarrollaron y los argumentos de la misma. Adem¨¢s deben subir el enlace de un v¨ªdeo demostrativo en donde pongan a prueba el modelo que desarrollaron utilizando una raspberry y una c¨¢mara web. 

**Calificaci¨®n**
La calificaci¨®n del challenge para cada uno de losequipos en total ser¨¢ distribuida de la siguiente manera: 

- Modelo del challenge (Nota de Kaggle): 70%
- V¨ªdeo demostrativos desde la raspberry: 20%
- Presentaci¨®n de clase: 10%


**Aclaraci¨®n**
- El grupo de profesores har¨¢ un modelo que tenga una presici¨®n de referencia. Esta precisi¨®n de referencia debe ser superada por los estudiantes para que su calificaci¨®n sea asignada de forma correcta. 

- Para la detecci¨®n de se?ales de transito es totalmente valido llegar a utilizar otro tipo de datsets que encuentren en l¨ªnea o que realicen ustedes. 

**Sobre el Dataset**
El dataset se encuentra disponible en la p¨¢gina de esta competencia. El dataset cuenta con 850 im¨¢genes con 4 clases diferentes de se?ales de transito. La informaci¨®n de las recuadros que encierran cada una de las se?ales de las im¨¢genes est¨¢ dadas un unos archivos de formato PASCAL VOC. Las clases con las que cuenta el dataset son: 

- S¨¦maforo (Trafic light) - 0;
- Se?al de alto (Stop) - 1;
- Limite de velocidad (Speedlimit) - 2;
- Cruce peatonal (Crosswalk) - 3;


@misc{make ml,
title={Road Signs Dataset},
url={https://makeml.app/datasets/road-signs},
journal={Make ML}}
----------------------
# Evaluation

La metrica de evaluaci¨®n para esta competencia es la Precisi¨®n por categoria. Esta estadistica comunmente usada en el ¨¢rea de Machine Learning nos determina que tan bueno o malo es nuestro modelo clasificando las diferentes etiquetas que se tienen. 

En general la precis¨®n es la raz¨®n entre los verdaderos positivos (Clasificados correctamente en una clase) y el n¨²mero de elementos totales que corresponden a dicha clase. 

## Formato de entrega
Para cada una de las im¨¢ganes de prueba en el dataset, las entregas deben tener dos columnas. 'Id' y 'category' refiriendose a la clase a la que permanece cada una de las im¨¢genes ('stop', 'speedlimit', 'traficlight', 'crosswalk'). La extensi¨®n del archivo debe ser un archivo .csv 

El archivo debe contener el siguiente formato de encabezado:
```
id,category
road87,1
```",# Dataset Description,True,True
4862,11785-fall2021-hw3p2,"# Description

The feature data of this homework are the same as homework 1 part 2. There are many variable length utterances comprised of 40 dimensional timesteps. You can use recurrent layers and their variants. You may also use convolutional layers if you so choose.

Your task will be to take the sequence of features and map them to a sequence of phonemes. Keep in mind the number of phonemes will not equal the number of timesteps. Refer to the write-up for more information.
----------------------
# Evaluation

The evaluation metric will be the Levenshtein distance (character level minimum edit distance) from the ground truth. The labels will have the sequence of phonemes, but not the alignment. To handle this CTC Loss will be used during training and a search should be used on the output distribution for prediction. More information is provided in the writeup.","# Dataset Description

File Descriptions
- phoneme_list.py: contains mapping of phonemes to indices
- train.npy: training features
- train_labels.npy: training labels which are phoneme sequences
- dev.npy: validation features
- dev_labels.npy: validation phoneme sequences
- test.npy: test data features
- sample_submission.csv: sample submission

Please refer to the write-up.",True,True
