4940,ml-2021-assignment-2,"# Description

---
In this competition you are asked to implement a text classification model. You will be working with the famous IMDB dataset that contains movie reviews labeled with positive/negative sentiments. You goal is to predict the sentiment given the review.
----------------------
# Evaluation

---

The evaluation metric for this competition is the accuracy score. That is:

$$
ACC = \frac{1}{n}\sum_{i = 1}^n[y^i = f(x^i)]
$$

where $$(y^i, x^i)_{i = 1}^n$$ is the dataset and $$f(x)$$ is the model.

## Submission Format

**For every review in the test set**, submission files should contain two columns: `id` and `sentiment`. `sentiment` should be a string, either `positive` or `negative`. The `id` column should have numbers from 0 to n, where n is the number of reviews in the test set. `id = 0` corresponds to the first review in the test set, `id = n` to the last one.


The file should contain a header and have the following format:
```
id,sentiment
0,positive
1,negative
...
```","# Dataset Description

Here you can find and download the data required for the competition.

`train_imdb_dataset.csv` contain the training set of reviews and their sentiments.

`test_reviews.csv` contains the test set of reviews you should predict the sentiments for.",True,True
