4945,esda-nilm-2021,"# Description

Welcome to the ESDA non-intrusive load monitoring (NILM) competition of 2021! You will compete individually or in teams to classify appliances based on voltage and current data, sampled at high resolution. We have processed the raw data into a number of features (see the Data tab above). 


----------------------
# Evaluation

You will be evaluated on classification accuracy: that is the proportion of correct class labels. Although each classification is effectively a multi-label classification (e.g. +fridge+washing_machine) there are no points for getting one of the labels correct. Each combination is treated as an individual class. 

The public leaderboard shows the classification accuracy of submissions on a subset of the data (30%). The actual results, evaluated on the remaining 70%, will be different and are only released at the end of the competition.","# Dataset Description

The submitted data is non-intrusive load monitoring (NILM) data. Your task is to predict **appliances**: the appliances in use when the measurement was taken. The appliances column is formatted as follows: +{appliance1}+{appliance2}...

## Files

- Training data **vw_train.csv**
- Testing data **vw_test.csv**
- Example submission **sample_submission.csv**",True,True
4946,creditriskinbankinglogreg2021,"# Description

Financial institutions usually use statistical models to estimate credibility of applicants for a loan. Applicant with the higest risk are declined, those who are appoved can be assigned different available product parameters based on their score.

Using provided data set, create a logistic regression model, that will serve for assessment of applicants creditbility. Quality of the model will be measured by its separation power - Gini coefficient.

To pass the competition sucessfully, competitiors should reach Gini higher than 49 Gini on the undisclosed sample.
----------------------
# Evaluation

Performance of the logistic regression model will be measure by its power to separate good and bad clients - Gini coefficient.

##Submission Format
For every out of sample application ID (SK\_ID\_CURR), submission files should contain two columns: SK\_ID\_CURR and estimated probability of default or its logit transformation (score).

The file should contain a header, be in cvs file with comma as a separator. First column is named SK\_ID\_CURR and the second one SCORE.

```
SK_ID_CURR,SCORE
1111111,0.1
```","# Dataset Description

