5051,plaksha22-cm005-project,"# Description

This is a classification problem to distinguish between a signal process which produces supersymmetric particles and a background process which does not.
<br>The data has been produced using Monte Carlo simulations. The first 8 features are kinematic properties measured by the particle detectors in the accelerator. The last ten features are functions of the first 8 features; these are high-level features derived by physicists to help discriminate between the two classes. 

----------------------
# Evaluation

The evaluation for this project will be based on accuracy. The accuracy will be based on right classification of an instance as either Class 0 or Class 1.","# Dataset Description

## Files

*   **train.csv** - the training set
*   **test.csv** - the test set
*   **sample_submission.csv** - a sample submission file in the correct format

## Columns

<br> Please refer all possible documentation to understand these column values and their relevance to the problem.

* `lepton_1_pT` - 
* `lepton_1_eta` - 
* `lepton_1_phi` - 
* `lepton_2_pT` - 
* `lepton_2_eta` - 
* `lepton_2_phi` - 
* `missing_energy_magnitude` -  
* `missing_energy_phi` - 
* `MET_rel` - 
* `axial_MET` - 
* `M_R` - 
* `M_TR_2` - 
* `R` - 
* `MT2` - 
* `S_R` - 
* `M_Delta_R` - 
* `dPhi_r_b` - 
* `cos(theta_r1)` - 
* `class` - Output class of either 0 or 1. 1 is for signal and 0 is for background.",True,True
5052,protein-compound-affinity,"# Description

# Background of the competition

AI for Drug Discovery Workshop and Data Challenge by Gulf Coast Consortia (GCC)

It is of critical importance to characterize compound¨Cprotein interaction for drug discovery and development, whether screening compound libraries for given protein targets to achieve desired effects or testing given compounds against possible off-target proteins to avoid undesired effects. However, experimental characterization of every possible compound¨Cprotein pair can be daunting, considering the enormous chemical and proteomic spaces. Computational prediction of compound¨Cprotein interaction (in term of quantitative levels: affinity) has therefore seen much progress recently, especially for repurposing and repositioning known drugs for new protein targets.

# Why computational protein-compound affinity prediction 
* The proteomic-chemical space faces combinatorial explosion
* Expensive docking and energy calculation in traditional methods
* Powerful deep learning for accurate prediction, courtesy of data and GPU resource

# Tasks in this competition
* Task 1:  IC50 prediction for seen proteins and compounds (unseen pairs)
* Task 2:  IC50 prediction for GPCRs (never seen in training data)
* Task 3:  Virtual screening of JAK2 compounds.  Ground truth measurements were actually in Kd

#  Evaluation metric/Submission portal/Leaderboard
* Task1: MSE/[Submission](https://www.kaggle.com/c/protein-compound-affinity/submit)/[Leaderboard](https://www.kaggle.com/c/protein-compound-affinity/leaderboard);  Spearman's rho/[Submission](https://www.kaggle.com/c/pro-lig-aff-task1-pearsonr/submit)/[Leaderboard](https://www.kaggle.com/c/pro-lig-aff-task1-pearsonr/leaderboard)
* Task2: MSE/[Submission](https://www.kaggle.com/c/pro-lig-aff-task2-mse/submit)/[Leaderboard](https://www.kaggle.com/c/pro-lig-aff-task2-mse/leaderboard);  Spearman's rho/[Submission](https://www.kaggle.com/c/pro-lig-aff-task2-pearsonr/submit)/[Leaderboard](https://www.kaggle.com/c/pro-lig-aff-task2-pearsonr/leaderboard)
* Task3: Spearman's rho/[Submission](https://www.kaggle.com/c/pro-lig-aff-task3-spearmanr/submit)/[Leaderboard](https://www.kaggle.com/c/pro-lig-aff-task3-spearmanr/leaderboard)

# Note
* The provided inputs are protein sequence and ligand SMILES, thus structure-free. So the simplest features are just the paired texts.  But you are welcome to use bioinformatics tools to predict structure features in addition to sequence features, such as secondary structure and solvent accessibility. You are also welcome to use tools such as RDkit for ligand features.
*  Once features are determined, please feel free to use advanced models from computer vision or natural language processing to encode the input features. 

# References
* Karimi, M., Wu, D., Wang, Z. and Shen, Y., 2019. DeepAffinity: interpretable deep learning of compound¨Cprotein affinity through unified recurrent and convolutional neural networks. Bioinformatics, 35(18), pp.3329-3338.
* Karimi, M., Wu, D., Wang, Z. and Shen, Y., 2020. Explainable Deep Relational Networks for Predicting Compound¨CProtein Affinities and Contacts. Journal of Chemical Information and Modeling, 61(1), pp.46-66.
* You, Y. and Shen, Y., 2020. Cross-modality protein embedding for compound-protein affinity and contact prediction. arXiv preprint arXiv:2012.00651.

----------------------
# Evaluation

Evaluation metrics are [MSE](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mean_squared_error) and [Pearson correlation coefficient](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pearson_correlation_coefficient).

## Submission Format
The file should contain a header and have the following format:
```
Id,Expected
1,6.7
2,5.3
3,4.5
```

* `Id`: The column number for the test sample in **test_taskn.csv**
* `Expected`: The predicted affinity value (between 2.0 to 11.0)","# Dataset Description

* Input: protein and compound SMILES sequences; output & label: experimentally measured affinity of ic50
* Evaluation metrics: MSE and Pearson correlation coefficient
* Training data what is provided
* Test data what is provided
  * Task1: test set
  * Task2: one transfer set of GPCR
  * Task3: one screening set of JAK2

## Files

*   **train.csv** - the training set
*   **test_taskn.csv** - the task n (1/2/3) test set data
*   **sampleSubmission_taskn.csv** - the sample submission file for task n (1/2/3) with `Id` and `Expected` columns, `Id` is the row number for the test sample in **test_taskn.csv**, and `Expected` is the predicted affinity value (between 2.0 to 11.0)

## Columns 

*   `protein_sequence` - definition of protein sequence
*   `compound_smiles` - definition of compound SMILES
*   `label` - ic50 values",True,True
