# Evaluation

The evaluation metric for this competition is [Mean Absolute Error](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mean_absolute_error). Mean absolute error (MAE) is a measure of errors between paired observations expressing the same phenomenon.","# Dataset Description

# Dataset

## Train/Valid/Test data: 2012-01-01 ~ 2014-12-31 (3 years) / 2015-01-01 ~ 2015-12-31 (1 year) / 2016-01-01 ~ 2016-12-31 (1 year) for 141 stocks with market index, respectively.

*   Input: 11 numeric features of 60 previous days for each stocks, the index 0 is for the market index. (shape of x_t: [142 (1 + 141), 60, 11], Reference: Enhancing Stock Movement Prediction with Adversarial Training (Feng et al., IJCAI-19))

*   Target: Closing price ratio over the previous day for a given date of each stocks (shape: [141])",True,True
5068,deeplearning2021competition,"# Description

Kyung Hee University Deep Learning Lecture Project Challenge
The goal of this challenge is to achieve high performance in a given dataset using techniques learned in the lecture.
You can use any neural networks and find your own model architecture to find out how to achieve optimal performance.
To prevent using a lot of GPU resources, you should use a network that can train by using the resources provided by Google Colab.
The baseline is the ResNet-34 result trained on Google Colab from TA and this code will be provided for all.
