# Evaluation

Evaluation","# Dataset Description

Data description",True,True
5078,idao-2022-bootcamp-insomnia,"# Description

In today's world of developing stress and anxiety more and more people suffer from sleep disorders. It's quite obvious that insomnia strongly affects people's lifestyles and along with that causes economical and even social safety problems. Moreover, it may lead to other (yet unexplored) long-term consequences. 
According to [authoritative researches] (https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC1978319/) about a fifth of adult population at any given point of time experience symptoms of sleep disorder. Individual employers and entire governments are incredibly interested in effective, blooming and full of energy workers and citizens. Thus, it is highly important to be able to predict sleep disorders as early as possible in order to prescribe appropriate in-time treatment.

In this mini ML contest you are offered to solve a task of predicting insomnia given person's physical, health and lifestyle parameters.

Good luck and have fun!
----------------------
# Evaluation

The evaluation metric for this competition is [logloss](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Loss_functions_for_classification#Logistic_loss). You may take a look how to calculate it using sklearn [here] (https://scikit-learn.org/stable/modules/generated/sklearn.metrics.log_loss.html) 

## Submission Format

**For every person in the test dataset**, submission files should contain two columns: `id` and `insomnia` - estimated probability of person with that id having sleep disorder. 

The file should contain a header and have the following format:
```
id,insomnia
5,0.5
6,0.5
7,0.5
10,0.5
11,0.5
```","# Dataset Description

## Files

*   **TRAIN.csv** - the training set
*   **TEST.csv** - the test set
*   **sample_submission.csv** - a sample submission file in the correct format

## Columns

* *id* - person's identificator
* *age* - person's age in years
* *weight*- person's weight in kilograms 
* *height*- person's height in centimeters
* *sex* - person's sex
* *stress* - level of stress during last month (1, 2, 3 - higher values correspond to larger stress)
* *doctor* - relative number of visits to doctor previously (1, 2, 3 - higher values correspond to greater number of visits)
* *sport* - is person physically active or not (binary)
* *pernicious*_1 - does person have some bad habit or not (binary)
* *pernicious*_2 - does person have some another bad habit or not (binary)
* *ubp/lbp* - upper/lower blood pressure in mmHg
* ***insomnia*** - target, does person have sleep disorder or not (binary)",True,True
5079,cusco-pucp-2021-02-heart-attack,"# Description

Este desaf¨ªo consiste en predecir que personas tienen riesgo de enfermedad coronaria en los pr¨®ximos 10 a?os. El *dataset* fue obtenido en un estudio que recolecta informaci¨®n de comportamiento, demograf¨ªa y m¨¦dica (hist¨®rica y actual) de una persona. Cada variable (columna) es un factor de riesgo potencial.

En el archivo *submission* deben estar las ""probabilidades"" de las predicciones realizadas por el modelo desarrollado.
----------------------
# Evaluation Metric

La evaluaci¨®n ser¨¢ el AUC (Area Under Curve)
----------------------
# Instructions

Bienvenido a la ""Competencia sobre predicci¨®n de Ataques al Coraz¨®n"" brindada en el ""Curso de Capacitaci¨®n en Machine Learning y Data Science con Python 2021-02"" para Cusco.

## Instrucciones

1. Leer las p¨¢ginas dentro de la secci¨®n ""Overview""
2. Leer la secci¨®n ""Data""
3. Leer la secci¨®n ""Rules""
4. Click en ""Join the Competition""
5. Ir a la secci¨®n ""Team"" y establecer el nombre de su equipo
6. Desarrollar un modelo y enviar sus predicciones siguiendo el formato del archivo ""sample_submission.csv""
7. Cumplir con todas las reglas de la competencia","# Dataset Description

