5101,text-representations,"# Description

This is a competition. You should make a classificator using data from train.csv file and predict labels for data from test.csv file. Then you should export your predictions as a .csv file and upload a submission.

The aim is to try and compare different text preprocessing pipelines and different text representations. So, classification algorithm is the same for everyone: [logistic regression](https://scikit-learn.org/stable/modules/generated/sklearn.linear_model.LogisticRegression.html) 
----------------------
# Evaluation

The evaluation metric for this competition is [accuracy](https://developers.google.com/machine-learning/crash-course/classification/accuracy#:~:text=Accuracy%20is%20one%20metric%20for,predictions%20Total%20number%20of%20predictions). Accuracy is the fraction of predictions our model got right.

## Submission Format

A submission file should contain two columns: `Id` and `Category`. 
The file should contain a header and have the following format:
```
Id,Category
0,good
...
```
File should be saved without an index:
`my_submission.to_csv('my_submission.csv', index=False)`","# Dataset Description

