5123,datathon-21,"# Description

Welcome to ""Datathon2021""! Gear yourselves up for an exciting real-world application challenge that we have in store for you. This is where you will have to give your brain a workout and use your skills, to make a Regression Model for the given situation!

*About the Data*
This dataset includes various attributes of the average deaths caused by cancer, mean number of reported cases of cancer diagnosed annually, etc in in various countries. The dataset comprises of over 3000 instances which need to be analyzed and used to predict the cancer mortality rates in the US countries. 

*Task*
Your task is to build a regression model to predict the target death rate.
Good Luck and Have Fun!
----------------------
# Evaluation

Coefficient of determination also called as R2 score is used to evaluate the performance of a linear regression model. It is the amount of the variation in the output dependent attribute which is predictable from the input independent variable(s). It is used to check how well-observed results are reproduced by the model, depending on the ratio of total deviation of results described by the model.","# Dataset Description

## Files

*   **train.csv** - the training set
*   **test.csv** - the test set
*   **sample_submission.csv** - a sample submission file in the correct format

## Columns

* Target_Death_Rate: Dependent variable. Mean per capita (100,000) cancer mortalities(a)

* RateOfIncidence: Mean per capita (100,000) cancer diagoses(a)

* medianIncome: Median income per county (b)

* Income: Percent of populace in poverty (b)

