5130,ntu-dsp2-2021-part2,"# Description

In this homework, you need to design a method to identify bearing health condition. The dataset contains 3 classes with 3600 training samples, and 600 testing samples recorded from bearing test rig.

In order to do health bearing condition classification, you should design an automatic pipeline to finish this work. For example, we first preprocess each sample to the spectrogram and then train a convolutional neural network with them.
----------------------
# Evaluation

##Evaluation
The evaluation metric for this homework is Classification Accuracy.

For example,

Prediction: 1, 2, 3, 0, 0 

Answer: 1, 2, 2, 2, 0

Your classification accuracy will be 0.6","# Dataset Description

# Data set: https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1ZN3yixI8rxzKN7ojMyWQo8_9T_DCt2C8",True,True
5131,pro-lig-aff-task2-mse,"# Description

# Background of competition

AI for Drug Discovery Workshop and Data Challenge by Gulf Coast Consortia (GCC)

It is of critical importance to characterize compound¨Cprotein interaction for drug discovery and development, whether screening compound libraries for given protein targets to achieve desired effects or testing given compounds against possible off-target proteins to avoid undesired effects. However, experimental characterization of every possible compound¨Cprotein pair can be daunting, considering the enormous chemical and proteomic spaces. Computational prediction of compound¨Cprotein interaction (in term of quantitative levels: affinity) has therefore made much progress recently, especially for repurposing and repositioning known drugs for previously unknown but desired new proteins.

# Why computational protein-compound affinity prediction 
* The proteomic-chemical space faces combinatorial explosion
* Expensive docking and energy calculation in traditional methods
* Powerful deep learning for accurate prediction, courtesy of data and GPU resource

# Tasks in this competition
* Task 1:  IC50 prediction for seen proteins and compounds (unseen pairs)
* Task 2:  IC50 prediction for GPCRs (never seen in training data)
* Task 3:  Virtual screening of JAK2 compounds.  Ground truth measurements were actually in Kd

#  Main portal of the competition
[Main page](https://www.kaggle.com/c/protein-compound-affinity/overview)

# Note
* The provided inputs are protein sequence and ligand SMILES, thus structure-free. So the simplest features are just the paired texts.  But you are welcome to use bioinformatics tools to predict structure features in addition to sequence features, such as secondary structure and solvent accessibility. You are also welcome to use tools such as RDkit for ligand features.
*  Once features are determined, please feel free to use advanced models from computer vision or natural language processing to encode the input features. 

# References
* Karimi, M., Wu, D., Wang, Z. and Shen, Y., 2019. DeepAffinity: interpretable deep learning of compound¨Cprotein affinity through unified recurrent and convolutional neural networks. Bioinformatics, 35(18), pp.3329-3338.
* Karimi, M., Wu, D., Wang, Z. and Shen, Y., 2020. Explainable Deep Relational Networks for Predicting Compound¨CProtein Affinities and Contacts. Journal of Chemical Information and Modeling, 61(1), pp.46-66.
* You, Y. and Shen, Y., 2020. Cross-modality protein embedding for compound-protein affinity and contact prediction. arXiv preprint arXiv:2012.00651.","# Dataset Description

* Input: protein and compound SMILES sequences; output & label: experimentally measured affinity of ic50
* Evaluation metrics: MSE and Pearson correlation coefficient
* Training data what is provided
* Test data what is provided
  * Task1: test set
  * Task2: one transfer set of GPCR
  * Task3: one screening set of JAK2

## Files

*   **train.csv** - the training set
*   **test_taskn.csv** - the task n (1/2/3) test set data
*   **sampleSubmission_taskn.csv** - the sample submission file for task n (1/2/3) with `Id` and `Expected` columns, `Id` is the row number for the test sample in **test_taskn.csv**, and `Expected` is the predicted affinity value (between 2.0 to 11.0)

## Columns 

*   `protein_sequence` - definition of protein sequence
*   `compound_smiles` - definition of compound SMILES
*   `label` - ic50 values",True,True
