5212,medallion-monthly-test,"# Description

Can you predict how popular a youtube video will be based solely on it's description, channel information and launch date? If you can you might win this month's competition!

In this competition we are testing out kaggle's competition platform. You are tasked with predicting a youtube video's view count. The scoring metric is root mean squared error (RMSE)

Rules:
- Don't use external data.
- Try to create your solution in a kaggle notebook so that after the competition is over you can share it.
----------------------
# Evaluation

## Evaluation Metric

The predictions will be scored using [RMSE](https://scikit-learn.org/stable/modules/generated/sklearn.metrics.mean_squared_error.html) between predicted view counts and true view counts.

## Submission Format

Submission files should contain two columns:
`id` - unique identifier for the video and trending date
`view_count` - Predicted number of views on that date.


The file should contain a header and have the following format:
```
id,view_count
_wNsZEqpKUA_2021-12-01,50000
2jfbXZiE6Lc_2021-12-01,50000
```","# Dataset Description

# Youtube Video View Count Prediction
Can you predict the number of views for a video?

# Training/Test Data (train.parquet/test.parquet)
- `id` - Unique Identifier for the row (combindation of video id and trending date)                      
- `video_id` - Unique Identifier for the video
- `title` - Title of the Video
- `publishedAt` - Datetime the video was published
- `channelId` - Id of the channel hosting the video
- `channelTitle` - Title of the channel hosting the video
- `categoryId` - Video category
- `trending_date ` - Date on which we are predicting the view count
- `tags` - Video Tags
- `view_count` - **Not provided in the test set** Number of views as of the trending date
- `likes` - Number of likes as of the trending date **Not provided in the test set**
- `dislikes` - Number of dislikes **Not provided in the test set**
- `comment_count` Comment Count **Not provided in the test set**
- `thumbnail_link` Link to the thumbnail of the video.
- `comments_disabled` True/False if comments are disabled.
- `ratings_disabled` True/False if ratings are disabled.
- `target` - The like to view count ratio of the video **TARGET COLUMN**
- `description` Video description

the `thumbnails` folder contains jpg images of the thumnails for the videos when available. They can be used for training your model.",True,True
