5220,tweet-mental-health-classification,"# Description

The task is to classify tweets into 4 different categories. The tweets were scraped using Tweety API. The data contains a `train.csv` which contains labelled data to train.

This is a straight forward classification task.

A [baseline](https://www.kaggle.com/kishalmandal/behavioural-tweets-eda-and-bertweet-baseline) notebook has been made public. It shows the use of CountVectorizer, TF-IDF vectorizer to build a Logistic Regression model and BerTweet transformer from Hugginface(built on PyTorch).
----------------------
# Evaluation


The evaluation metric for this competition is [Accuracy Score](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Accuracy_and_precision). It is basically the number of correct predicted labels divided by the total number of correct labels.

## Submission Format

**For every tweet in the dataset**, submission files should contain two columns: `id` and `labels`. 
The file should contain a header and have the following format:
```
id,labels
1,Normal
2,Normal
```","# Dataset Description

The dataset contains 3 files:

## Files

*   **train.csv** - the training set
*   **test.csv** - the test set
*   **sample_submission.csv** - a sample submission file in the correct format

## Columns

*   `id` - Id of the tweet
*   `tweets` - contains the tweet (text)
*   `label`?- label to which class the tweet belongs to",True,True
