<p>
We use Absolute Error (AE) as metric and set the target as 1. So if you get a score 0.312, you AE score will be 1 - 0.312 = 0.688. Lower AE means better model. The system will calculate the AE for you, so you should just update the averaged reward and don't reverse it.
</p>
