5257,rm-loan-data-competition,"# Description

This competition is to build a predictive model for loan acceptances using the data set in the file, ""cprm_onlineautoloan_datacail_trainingset_5foldsetup.xlsx"" which is also online here as the ""train.csv"" file.   The file includes information from 16,783 applications for auto loans, which is a sample of a large data set including only consumers in California and Illinois.  The Excel file is set up for 5-fold validation where you can enter a fold 1-5 as the validation test while the rest form the training set.    Descriptions of each of the fields and background on the data set are given on the concept check description. Please note that both ¡°Apply¡± and ¡°SAS_Fund_Date¡± contain information about the actual value of whether the loan offer was accepted. 

In addition to this training set for building your model, there is also an additional equal-size sample of California and Illinois applicants that forms the test set.  Your goal in constructing your model will be to predict the outcomes in the test set.  You should build a logistic model of the probability of acceptance (which is the ¡°apply¡± field in the dataset ¨C note that you cannot use this field in your prediction since it is unknown at the time of application).  You can then apply your model to the data in the test set (which excludes the actual loan acceptance columns) and enter your probability predictions as in the ""sample_submission.csv"" file. 


## Acknowledgements

We thank the Columbia University Center for Pricing and Revenue Management for the data for this competition. 
----------------------
# Evaluation

Your submission will be evaluated using the mean absolute error.  

---



## Submission Format

**For every ID in the test set**, submission files should contain two columns: `Id` and `apply`. 


The file should contain a header and have the following format:
```
Id, apply
1,0.25
2, 0.15 
...
```","# Dataset Description

The files for this competition are csv files that contain information as described in the data description section of the Concept Check #4 sheet.   The **cprm_train.csv** file contains the training set including key response under ""apply"" with ""1"" for a loan acceptance and ""0"" for not. The **cprm_test.csv** file contains the test set information excluding both the ""apply"" and ""fund_date"" information.  The **cprm_submission_sample.csv** file contains a sample submission file. 

## Files

*   **cprm_train.csv** - the training set
*   **cprm_test.csv** - the test set
*   **cprm_submission_sample.csv** - a sample submission file in the correct format


## Columns

* Tier *
* Primary_FICO *
* State * 
* Type *
* Apply Date * 
* Approve_date *
* Fund_Date *
* Term *
* New_Rate *
* Used_Rate *
