- Test Images - [Full Size](http://ptak.felk.cvut.cz/plants/DanishFungiDataset/DF21-images.tar.gz) [~50Gb]
- Test Images (max side size 300px) - Available bellow in folder [DF21-images-300]

**Metadata**

- Train metadata (Available bellow)
- Test metadata (Available bellow) [DF21-images-300]",True,True
5304,ml-olympiad-tensorflow-malaysia-user-group,"# Description

## What is ML Olympiad
An associated Kaggle Community Competitions hosted by ML GDEs or TFUGs, sponsored by Google Developers. (ML GDEs or TFUGs host ML community competitions on Kaggle and ML Ecosystem team sponsors swag prizes to winners of each competition.

## TensorFlow Malaysia User Group (TFMUG)
TensorFlow Malaysia User Group (TFMUG) was founded in 2017. The group's aim is to enable people to create and deploy their own Deep Learning models built using primarily TensorFlow. TFMUG aims to build the key skill sets for this group from the combination of both beginner and intermediate models as well as advancing to the next level with knowledge sharing and presentations about cutting edge papers and techniques.

## ML Olympiad's Objective
To train ML for developers leveraging Kaggle¡¯s community competition. This is an opportunity for the participants to practice ML. This is the first 2022 global campaign of the ML Ecosystem team and this helps build stronger communities.

## Datasets
Credit card fraud dataset from the region is used for this hackathon.

## Task
In this competition, you are given a Credit Card Fraud dataset with some missing values. You are required to build model to predict Credit Card fraud class.

## Evaluation
Evaluation is based on **mean F-score**. This leaderboard is calculated with approximately 40% of the test data. The final results will be based on the other 60%, so the final standings may be different. The final winners will be determined by **combining both public (40%) and private (60%) results**.

## Prizes
Swag prizes for top winners are sponsored by Google Developers. Top three winners will receive swags. 

![](https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/q4Yt-J4FAgVcIA_C-a8XSZ4t-IxDQKeK2A9X0eCBrL-_20UqrblaP8TpztWjCftmtOHysmHnQVmlgfV05SP7pzpduAwRUXc5LLyESvpvCUiOzMNy57M9KFoeEq2kxKhLRlBaHx0-fK8=w2400)

## Acknowledgements:
We thank Google Developers and ML Ecosystem for sponsoring this competition.

## Organizers:

- TensorFlow Malaysia User Group (TFMUG)
- Sunway University DataXSight Research Cluster
- Malaysia R User Group (MyRUG)

\#MLOlympiad \#TFMUG
----------------------
# Evaluation

## Evaluation
Submissions are evaluated on **mean F-score**. The F-score is a way of combining the precision and recall of the model, and it is defined as the harmonic mean of the model's precision and recall

## Submission File
Use the sample_submission.csv file as a guide for submission.

## Results
This leaderboard is calculated with approximately 40% of the test data. The final results will be based on the other 60%, so the final standings may be different. The final winners will be determined by *combining both public (40%) and private (60%) results*.","# Dataset Description

The dataset is a sample of credit card fraud dataset. Based on the dataset, build a prediction model to predict fraud.

*   **train.csv** - the training set
*   **test.csv** - the test set.  The task is to predict the correct label.
*   **sample_submission.csv** - a sample submission file in the correct format

## Columns

*   `col_0 to col_25` - variables related to credit card transactions
*   `class`?- 0 as non-fraud and 1 as fraud",True,True
