- Winners will be contacted by the meetup organizer. If you a member of the meetup, you will get a meetup message. If you are not a member of the meetup, you will be sent a message through the kaggle platform. So, if you are a winner, please check your email for a message.
- Awards will then be mailed by Google Developers through regular postal mail.
- The meetup organizer is not responsible for any lost swag deliveries, and is not in charge of delivery of swags.
----------------------
# Evaluation

The evaluation metric is: accuracy","# Dataset Description

This dataset is adapted from the Stellar Classification Dataset - SDSS17. 
Every observation is described by feature columns and 1 class column which identifies it to be either a star, galaxy or quasar.

# Citation
fedesoriano. (January 2022). Stellar Classification Dataset - SDSS17. Retrieved [Date Retrieved] from https://www.kaggle.com/fedesoriano/stellar-classification-dataset-sdss17.
 
## Files

*   **train.csv** - the training set
*   **test.csv** - the test set
*   **sample_submission.csv** - a sample submission file in the correct format


## Columns

* obj_ID = Object Identifier, the unique value that identifies the object in the image catalog used by the CAS
* alpha = Right Ascension angle (at J2000 epoch)
* delta = Declination angle (at J2000 epoch)
* u = Ultraviolet filter in the photometric system
* g = Green filter in the photometric system
* r = Red filter in the photometric system
* i = Near Infrared filter in the photometric system
* z = Infrared filter in the photometric system
* run_ID = Run Number used to identify the specific scan
* cam_col = Camera column to identify the scanline within the run
* field_ID = Field number to identify each field
* spec_obj_ID = Unique ID used for optical spectroscopic objects (this means that 2 different observations with the same spec_obj_ID must share the output class)
* redshift = redshift value based on the increase in wavelength
* plate = plate ID, identifies each plate in SDSS
* MJD = Modified Julian Date, used to indicate when a given piece of SDSS data was taken
* fiber_ID = fiber ID that identifies the fiber that pointed the light at the focal plane in each observation
* label = object class (galaxy, star or quasar object)

# Predictions
To help you, classes were changed to integers. You should predict the label. Galaxy = 0, Quasar = 1, Star = 2",True,True
