5323,autism-prediction,"# Description

Welcome to ML Olympiad hosted by TFUG Chennai and TFUG Mysuru .

### What is ML Olympiad?

An associated Kaggle Community Competitions hosted by ML GDEs or TFUGs, sponsored by Google Developers. 

[Source](https://www.kaggle.com/andrewmvd/autism-screening-on-adults)

### Abstract
Improve Autism Screening by creating predicting the likelihood of having this condition.

### About this dataset
What is Autism
Autism, or autism spectrum disorder (ASD), refers to a broad range of conditions characterized by challenges with social skills, repetitive behaviors, speech and nonverbal communication.

### Causes and Challenges
It is mostly influenced by a combination of genetic and environmental factors. Because autism is a spectrum disorder, each person with autism has a distinct set of strengths and challenges. The ways in which people with autism learn, think and problem-solve can range from highly skilled to severely challenged.
Research has made clear that high quality early intervention can improve learning, communication and social skills, as well as underlying brain development. Yet the diagnostic process can take several years.

### The Role of Machine Learning
This dataset is composed of survey results for more than 700 people who filled an app form. There are labels portraying whether the person received a diagnosis of autism, allowing machine learning models to predict the likelihood of having autism, therefore allowing healthcare professionals prioritize their resources.

## Acknowledgements

**Citations**

Tabtah, F. (2017). Autism Spectrum Disorder Screening: Machine Learning Adaptation and DSM-5 Fulfillment. Proceedings of the 1st International Conference on Medical and Health Informatics 2017, pp.1-6. Taichung City, Taiwan, ACM.
Thabtah, F. (2017). Machine Learning in Autistic Spectrum Disorder Behavioural Research: A Review. To Appear in Informatics for Health and Social Care Journal. December, 2017

[Image Source](https://www.verdict.co.uk/machine-learning-autism/)

**License**

Public Domain

**Data Source**

The data files for this competition was developed synthetically by using [CTGan](https://github.com/sdv-dev/CTGAN) on [Autism Screening on Adults Dataset](https://www.kaggle.com/andrewmvd/autism-screening-on-adults). 
The dataset creation, as well as the competition setup, was done by [Suryansu Dash](https://www.linkedin.com/in/suryansu-dash-a71b9712b/) and [Laxman Naik](https://www.linkedin.com/in/laxman-naik/) of [GDSC CET-Bhubaneswar](https://gdsc.community.dev/college-of-engineering-technology-bhubaneswar/)

#MLOlympiad
----------------------
# Evaluation

The evaluation metric for this competition is [AUC-ROC Score](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Receiver_operating_characteristic). The AUC-ROC Score is commonly used for classification tasks. It measures the degree or measure of separability between the classes. The ROC curve is plotted with TPR against the FPR where TPR is on the y-axis and FPR is on the x-axis.

TPR or True Positive Rate can be defined as (True Positives / (True Positives + False Negatives))
Similarly FPR, or False Positive Rate, can be defined as (False Positives / (False Positives + True Negatives))

AUC - ROC curve is a performance measurement for the classification problems at various threshold settings

## Submission Format

Every Submission file should have the the following format:
```
ID,Class/ASD
1,1
```
You can refer to the sample_submission.csv file to get an idea on how to frame the submission file.","# Dataset Description

The details of the files provided, as well as the column information for domain knowledge, is given below:
## Files

*   **train.csv** - the training set
*   **test.csv** - the test set
*   **sample_submission.csv** - a sample submission file in the correct format

## Columns

*   `ID` - ID of the patient
*   `A1_Score to A10_Score` - Score based on Autism Spectrum Quotient (AQ) 10 item screening tool
*  `age` - Age of the patient in years
*  `gender` - Gender of the patient
*  `ethnicity` - Ethnicity of the patient
*  `jaundice` - Whether the patient had jaundice at the time of birth
*  `autism` - Whether an immediate family member has been diagnosed with autism
*  `contry_of_res` - Country of residence of the patient
*  `used_app_before` - Whether the patient has undergone a screening test before
*  `result` - Score for AQ1-10 screening test
*  `age_desc` - Age of the patient
*  `relation` - Relation of patient who completed the test
*  `Class/ASD` - Classified result as 0 or 1. Here 0 represents No and 1 represents Yes. This is the target column, and during submission submit the values as 0 or 1 only.",True,True
5324,ds-programming-test,"# Description

En Los ¨¢ngeles existe un sistema compartido de bicicletas que brinda datos an¨®nimos acerca del uso del servicio que ofrecen. La tabla que se proporciona contiene el hist¨®rico de viajes que se han realizado durante cerca de 9 meses, y contiene una columna que es de particular inter¨¦s y que se buscar¨¢ analizar a m¨¢s profundidad: Passholder_type.  A continuaci¨®n se presentan las columnas que contiene la tabla:

- trip_id: identificador ¨²nico para el viaje
- duration: duraci¨®n del viaje en minutos
- start_time: dia/hora donde en viaje inicia en formato ISO 8601 tiempo local
- end_time:  dia/hora donde el viaje termina en formato ISO 8601 tiempo local
- start_station: la estaci¨®n donde el viaje inici¨®
- start_lat: la latitud de la estaci¨®n donde el viaje se origin¨®
- start_lon: la longitud de la estaci¨®n donde el viaje se origin¨®
- end_station: la estaci¨®n donde el viaje termin¨®
- end_lat: la latitud de la estaci¨®n donde termin¨® el viaje
- end_lon: la longitud de la estaci¨®n donde termin¨® el viaje
- bike_id: un entero ¨²nico que identifica la bicicleta
- plan_duration: n¨²mero de dias que el usuario tendr¨¢ el paso. 0 significa un viaje ¨²nico (Walk-up plan)
- trip_route_category: ¡°Round trip¡± son viajes que empiezan y terminan en la misma estaci¨®n
- passholder_type: El nombre del plan de passholder

Para el problema anal¨ªtico, se desea saber si es posible inferir si el tipo de pase es ¡°Monthly Pass¡± tomando en cuenta las dem¨¢s variables de viaje. 


----------------------
# Evaluation

Submissions are scored by categorization accuracy.","# Dataset Description

La evaluaci¨®n del modelo se realiza de manera autom¨¢tica a trav¨¦s de la plataforma. Se encuentran tres archivos:

- train_set.csv: datos que servir¨¢n para construir el modelo

- test_set.csv: datos que no tienen la variable dependiente y que se debe hacer predicci¨®n

- sample_submission.csv: formato en el cual se debe subir las predicciones

En el tab de Submit Predictions se hace upload de un archivo con el formato adecuado.Favor de registrarse con alg¨²n pseud¨®nimo que no est¨¦ relacionado con su nombre y comp¨¢rtenoslo. El objetivo principal no es llegar al mejor resultado en t¨¦rminos de la m¨¦trica de error, si no estar seguros de tomar en cuenta aspectos indispensables al crear este modelo anal¨ªtico. Por lo que sobrepasando el benchmark se considera una buena entrega.",True,True
5325,qualityeducation,"# Description

O Brasil ¨¦ considerado um pa¨ªs com dimens?es continentais, ¨¦ o quinto maior pa¨ªs do planeta. A grande extens?o territorial do Brasil proporciona ao pa¨ªs uma enorme diversidade de paisagens, climas, topografia, fauna e flora. 

Infelizmente hoje no Brasil se estima ter por volta de 11 milh?es de analfabetos e 5,9 milh?es de pessoas desempregadas. A educa??o permite a mobilidade socioecon?mica ascendente e ¨¦ a chave para escapar da pobreza. A educa??o ajuda a reduzir as desigualdades e alcan?ar a igualdade de g¨ºnero e ¨¦ crucial para promover a tolerancia e sociedades mais pac¨ªficas. Desigualdades na educa??o s?o exacerbadas pelo COVID-19.

