5335,tamkeen,"# Description

#Who is tamkeen?
Since our inception in 2006, we have always made it our mission to empower the private sector to drive economic growth in the Kingdom of Bahrain by providing programs and support for enterprises and individuals. In line with the Kingdom¡¯s collective efforts and comprehensive vision towards creating a thriving business-friendly ecosystem with a highly skilled Bahraini workforce, Tamkeen invested BHD 1 billion in direct support and contributed to facilitating approximately BHD 700 million in indirect support through partners in the banking sector to encourage and expand the funding opportunities available to the private sector and specifically small and medium enterprises (¡°SMEs¡±). These opportunities enable the private sector to strengthen and further develop Bahrain¡¯s national economy. 

#What is the competition about?
At Tamkeen, we provide funds for start-ups, SMEs, and seed-stage companies, To help speed up this process, we use data to predict a company¡¯s requirements and allocate funds based on those requirements and the offerings of the company. This data is then fed into a chatbot which calculates and predicts the funding needed by the company. 

It is expected from the Participant to build a predictive model to help companies estimate the funds needed.    

#Participant Confirmation: 

By participating in this competition, you agree to the following: 

1. The data provided by Tamkeen is to be used for the purposes of the competition only;  
2. Tamkeen shall retain ownership of any data submitted by the participant; 
3. Tamkeen has the right to cancel, terminate, modify or suspend this competition at any time in its sole discretion; Tamkeen reserves the right to disqualify any participant who tampers with the submission process or any other part of the competition; 
4. Tamkeen employees are not eligible to participate in the competition nor can participants approach Tamkeen staff to request more data beyond what is provided as part of the competition; 
5. Participants agree that the submission and any information gathered as a part of this competition may be used by Tamkeen. Tamkeen may use this information solely to improve their products or to provide customized services to the public; and 
6. Participants agree that Tamkeen, Kaggle and its affiliates may use the Participants name and likeness for advertising and promotional purposes without additional compensation. 
----------------------
# Evaluation

#Metric 
Submissions are evaluated on Root-Mean-Squared-Error (RMSE) between the logarithm of the predicted value and the logarithm of the observed sales price. (https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Root-mean-square_deviation) 

Submission File Format 
The file should contain a header and have the following format: 
ID,Total.fund","# Dataset Description

This data is for a fund dataset where we want to find a relationship between the funds and the other features to automate our fund process, 

## Files

*   **train.csv** - the training set
*   **test.csv** - the test set
*   **sample_submission.csv** - a sample submission file in the correct format

## Columns

*   `Company.Sector` - this column is for the company sector (For example, Education, Manufacturing, Sales and trading, Food and Beverage, etc.....) 
*   `ID`?-  This ID column just for reference 
*   `Company.Income`?-  This column is for the targeted company¡¯s annual income 
*   `Starting.Captial`?- This column is for the starting capital for the targeted company
*   `Company.Stage`?-  This column determines which stage is the targeted company in ?
*   `Target.localization`?- This column determines what the target localization rate the company is aiming for 
*   `Total.localization.rate`?-  This column determines the rate of local employees in the company  
*   `Total.other.rate`?-  This column determines the rate of non-local employees in the company 
*   `Number.of.local.employee`?-  This column determines the number of local employees in the company 
*   `Number.other.employee`?- This column determines the number of non-local employees in the company 
*   `Active.employee`?-   This column determines the number of active employees 
*   `Local.Shareholders`?-  This column determines the number of local shareholders in the company
*   `regional.Shareholders`?-  This column determines the number of regional shareholders in the company
*   `Other.Shareholders`?-  This column determines the number of non-local shareholders in the company 
*   `Male.Shareholders`?- This column determines the number of male shareholders in the company 
*   `Female.Shareholders`?- This column determines the number of female shareholders in the company 
*   `Number.of.Activities`?-This column is for the number of activities the target company is doing at a specific time   
*   `Total.fund`?- This column is for the funding that Tamkeen will offer the target company 


Disclaimer: This dataset is synthetic and does not represent Tamkeen data in any shape or form. The dataset is to be used for this competition exercise purposes only.",True,True
5336,mgta-415-challenge-ucsd-rady-school,"# Description

This challenge is designed for Master of Business Analytics students at the Rady School of Management, University of California, San Diego. This is part of the course requirements for MGTA 415 Analyzing Unstructured Data.

## Challenge Objective
The dataset contains details about restaurants and their reviews. You are asked to design data mining models to predict the restaurant type using the observed variables.
----------------------
# Evaluation

## Evaluation Metrics
Your predictions will be evaluated against the ground truth restaurant types. The F1 score is adopted as the evaluation metric.

## Submission Format
You are asked to run your models locally, on the Rady server, or by other means on your own, and upload your final prediction file. It is a csv file with headers of two columns: *Id* and *Predicted*. The first character **must** be capitalized. The first column corresponds to the *id* in the *test.csv* file and the second column contains the predicted restaurant type.

Once submitted, the system will evaluate on a fixed portion (40%, randomly chosen) of the test set and compute f1-score accordingly. Then your score will be displayed on the leaderboard.
**Please note that the leaderboard during the challenge is NOT final.** The final leaderboard will be refreshed once the challenge ends. A new f1-score will be calculated based on the other 60% portion which has not been tested yet.

Every day, you can make at most 20 submissions. So please start early and make sure you have enough time to tweak your models and hyper-parameters. You will be able to choose 2 submissions for the final evaluation and the system will pick the best score you have.","# Dataset Description

***train.csv*** It contains all the training data that you can use in this challenge. The first column *id* provides you with the unique key to identify the restaurants. 
Different columns show different features/attributes of a restaurant, including free texts, numerical features, and categorical features.
There are also many missing values. So please conduct some exploratory data analysis (EDAs) first before you work on feature engineering.

**test.csv**: It contains all the restaurants that you need to predict their types. The format is the same as the *train.csv*, except that the *label* column has been removed.

***baseline.ipynb***: It contains a logistic regression model trained on document vectors computed by averaging word vectors of its constituent words from reviews. By running this notebook, you will be able to get a *predicted.csv* as the output. This would give a score of 0.72390. The baseline gives an example of using restaurant reviews only, but you are free to utilize any attributes/features in your approach. You should aim for better preformance.",True,True
5337,jan-30-22stellar,"# Description

In this assignment students need to predict `y=Class` of a stellar entity based on its spectral features. 

See **Rules** tab for more details.

## Acknowledgements
1. We thank the [Sloan Digital Sky Survey (SDSS) authors](https://arxiv.org/abs/2112.02026) and [fedesoriano](https://www.kaggle.com/fedesoriano) for posting [Stellar Classification Dataset - SDSS17](https://www.kaggle.com/fedesoriano/stellar-classification-dataset-sdss17) dataset on Kaggle.com. The dataset has been augmented for this competition
1. The image is from NASA website, 2017, https://www.nasa.gov/feature/goddard/2017/hubble-captures-massive-dead-disk-galaxy
1. **Competition Authors**. [HSE](https://hse.ru/) [ML Teaching Team](https://www.hse.ru/edu/courses/?filial=22723&lecturer=409923484&year=2021): [Oleg Melnikov](https://www.linkedin.com/in/olegmelnikov/), [Alexey Boldyrev](https://www.hse.ru/org/persons/223985242), [Vladimir Kirillin](https://www.hse.ru/org/persons/499313273), [Sergey Chervontsev](https://www.hse.ru/org/persons/305134539), Margarita Lazareva, Tatyana Yazykova, Mike Ovyan, Lika Lomidze, Vladimir Novikov, Valeriya Rogovchenko
----------------------
# Evaluation

The evaluation metric is [**accuracy score**](https://scikit-learn.org/stable/modules/generated/sklearn.metrics.accuracy_score.html), which is the default classification accuracy in `sklearn` library.

The submission format is:

        id,Class
        1,G
        2,S
        3,Q","# Dataset Description

Source of data and description below: [fedesoriano](https://www.kaggle.com/fedesoriano). (January 2022).  [Stellar Classification Dataset - SDSS17](https://www.kaggle.com/fedesoriano/stellar-classification-dataset-sdss17). Note: this dataset has been augmented for this competition.

* More information about the license: https://classic.sdss.org/gallery
* SDSS Publications: Abdurro¡¯uf et al., The Seventeenth data release of the Sloan Digital Sky Surveys: Complete Release of MaNGA, MaStar and APOGEE-2 DATA (Abdurro¡¯uf et al. submitted to ApJS) [arXiv:2112.02026](https://arxiv.org/abs/2112.02026)
 
## Context
In astronomy, stellar classification is the classification of stars based on their spectral characteristics. The classification scheme of galaxies, quasars, and stars is one of the most fundamental in astronomy. The early cataloging of stars and their distribution in the sky has led to the understanding that they make up our own galaxy and, following the distinction that Andromeda was a separate galaxy to our own, numerous galaxies began to be surveyed as more powerful telescopes were built. This dataset aims to classify stars, galaxies, and quasars based on their spectral characteristics.
 
## Content
The dataset is oversampled to 200,000 observations with 14 features 
 
1. alpha = Right Ascension angle (at J2000 epoch)
1. delta = Declination angle (at J2000 epoch)
1. u = Ultraviolet filter in the photometric system
1. g = Green filter in the photometric system
1. r = Red filter in the photometric system
1. i = Near Infrared filter in the photometric system
1. z = Infrared filter in the photometric system
1. run_ID = Run Number used to identify the specific scan
1. cam_col = Camera column to identify the scanline within the run
1. field_ID = Field number to identify each field
1. redshift = redshift value based on the increase in wavelength
1. plate = plate ID, identifies each plate in SDSS
1. MJD = Modified Julian Date, used to indicate when a given piece of SDSS data was taken
1. fiber_ID = fiber ID that identifies the fiber that pointed the light at the focal plane in each observation
1. Class = object class (Galaxy, Star or Quasar object)",True,True
