5346,ml-olympiad-used-car-price,"# Description

**Goal of the Competition**
The goal of this competition is to accurately used car price by building a prediction model trained on Craigslist world's largest collection of used vehicles for s.

Your work will help developers to build a strong mobile app which can evaluate used car price for sales.

#MLOlympiad
----------------------
# Evaluation

Evaluation is purely based on RMSLE accuracy.","# Dataset Description

This dataset contains information about used cars.
This data can be used for a lot of purposes such as price prediction to exemplify the use of linear regression in Machine Learning.
The columns in the given dataset are as follows:

- name
- year
- selling_price
- km_driven
- fuel
- seller_type
- transmission
- Owner

For used motorcycle datasets please go to https://www.kaggle.com/nehalbirla/motorcycle-dataset",True,True
5347,ml-olympiad-gdscuiz-and-tfugagadir,"# Description

# ML Olympiad:  Genome Sequences Classification

## Goal of the Competition

The goal of this competition is to accurately classify genomes by building a machine learning model.

## Context 

Every living being has a set of chromosomes that depicts its characteristics and features. These chromosomes are composed of nucleotides: A, C, G, and T. Also known as DNA genomes. The complete list of these nucleotides is called a genome sequence. 

Since a genome sequence is different for every living being, the ability to determine the species of the organism from its genome could be very helpful for research and biology-related works. However, it is difficult to perform this task without comparing the DNA of this organism to the DNA of creatures of the same species.
From another standpoint, our current technology is not near enough for us to fully understand the genomes and the genetic codes, which are the basis of every organism.

Launching this competition might open further possibilities and doors on this topic. It will allow AI enthusiasts to hone their skills, and contribute to the field of biology. As well as utilize ML/DL-based technologies to classify genome sequences of different given species.

The participants will have to create models to classify the genome sequences of Human vs Gorilla based on their genome sequence. 

Individuals or groups of up to three people are allowed to participate in the competition. 

> This is a Code Competition. Refer to [Code Requirements](https://www.kaggle.com/c/ml-olympiad-gdscuiz-and-tfugagadir/overview/code-requirements) for details.



**Swag prizes for top winners are sponsored by Google Developers.**
----------------------
# Evaluation

# Evaluation

## Goal

The goal is to predict whether a genome is a 'Homo\_sapien' genome or is it 'Gorilla\_gorilla' genome

## Metric

The score will be the [categorization accuracy](https://developers.google.com/machine-learning/crash-course/classification/accuracy) of classified genomes.

## Submission Format

**For every genome in the dataset**, submission files should contain two columns: `id` and 'species'. 

The file should contain a header and have the following format:
```
id,species
1,'Homo_sapiens'
2,'Gorilla_gorilla'
```

## This is a Model Competition
The participants are required to submit 3 parts:

### 1. A Submission file
The submission file should contain a header with two columns:

id : a number that contains the id of the genome sequence.

species: a string is either 'Homo\_sapiens' or 'Gorilla\_gorilla'.

The submission file must be named submission.csv. 

This will allow you to see your ranking on the public leaderboard of the competition.

### 2. A Jupyter Notebook

A Jupyter notebook of the code you wrote to create this solution.

The file name should be 'team\_name\_genome\_classifier.ipynb'. Please include the team¡¯s name in the filename. 

**This part will be requested after the end of the competition.**

### 3. The model
The trained model 'team\_name\_genome_classifier.h5'. Please include the team¡¯s name in the filename. 

This part will be requested after the end of the competition to validate the results.
----------------------
# Timeline

# Timeline
February 07, 2022 - Start Date.
March 05, 2022 - Final Submission Deadline.

All deadlines are at 11:59 PM UTC. The competition organizers reserve the right to update the contest timeline.
----------------------
# Prizes

# Prizes
The top 3 teams will be rewarded with Swags sponsored by Google Developers.
----------------------
# Acknowledgement

# Acknowledgement
We would like to thank [Google Developers](https://developers.google.com/) for sponsoring this competition. As well as the [TensorFlow User Group Agadir](https://www.meetup.com/TFUGAgadir/) Team, and the [Google Developer Student Clubs - University of Ibn Zohr](https://gdsc.community.dev/university-of-ibn-zohr/) Team for helping in the organization of this competition.

----------------------
# Code Requirements

## This is a Code Competition
Submissions to this competition must be made through Notebooks. In order for the ""Submit"" button to be active after a commit, the following conditions must be met:

- CPU Notebook <= 9 hours run-time
- GPU Notebook <= 9 hours run-time
- Internet access disabled
- Freely & publicly available external data is allowed, including pre-trained models
- Submission file must be named submission.csv

Please see the Code Competition FAQ for more information on how to submit. And review the code debugging doc if you are encountering submission errors.
