5350,ml-olympiad-preserving-north-african-culture,"# Description

????Ahoy, welcome to our competition! You¡¯re in the right place.
Swag prizes for top winners are sponsored by Google Developers.
Hashtags: #MLOlympiad #Google #GDSC #IEEE #IEEE_ESSTHS_SB #IEEE_ENIT_SB #PyData_Tunisia
Thank you for participating in our competition, we wish you all good luck and let us preserve for the future!

**The Challenge**
Culture is an umbrella term that encompasses the social behavior and norms found in human societies, as well as the knowledge, beliefs, arts, laws, customs, capabilities, and habits of the individuals in these groups. Thus it is really important for us to preserve it for all future generations..

To survive the brink of time, and the ever-changing interests of people no matter where they live, your job in this challenge is to build a classification model that answers the question: ¡°what culture does this image represent? using our dataset, composed of raw images of architecture, food, clothing, tattoos, festivals, statues, monuments, and paintings from north-African countries ( Algeria, Egypt, Lybia, Morocco, Mauritania, Sudan, and Tunisia).

### Overview of How Kaggle¡¯s Competitions Work
1. Join the Competition
Read about the challenge description, accept the Competition Rules and gain access to the competition dataset.

2. Get to Work
Download the data, build models on it locally or on Kaggle Kernels (our no-setup, customizable Jupyter Notebooks environment with free GPUs) and generate a prediction file.

3. Make a Submission
Upload your prediction as a submission on Kaggle and receive an accuracy score.

4. Check the Leaderboard
See how your model ranks against other Kagglers on our leaderboard.

5. Improve Your Score
Check out the discussion forum to find lots of tutorials and insights from other competitors.


What Data Will I Use in This Competition?

Train.csv will contain the details of a subset of the pictures, and importantly, will reveal which culture they are a part of, also known as the ¡°ground truth¡±.

The `test.csv` dataset contains similar information but does not disclose the ¡°ground truth¡± for each picture. It¡¯s your job to classify these images

Using the patterns you find in the train.csv data, try to classify these images to their cultures as accuratly as possible.

Check out the ¡°Data¡± tab to explore the datasets even further. Once you feel you¡¯ve created a competitive model, submit it to Kaggle to see where your model stands on our leaderboard against other Kagglers.

How to Submit your Prediction to Kaggle
Once you¡¯re ready to make a submission and get on the leaderboard:
1. Click on the ¡°Submit Predictions¡± button
2. Upload a CSV file in the submission file format. You¡¯re able to submit 10 submissions a day.
Submission File Format:

You should submit a CSV file with exactly 978 entries plus a header row. Your submission will show an error if you have extra columns (beyond Id and country_label) or rows.
The file should have exactly 2 columns:
Id (sorted in any order)
country_label (contains the label of the county associated with your classified image)


Got it! I¡¯m ready to get started. Where do I get help if I need it?
For Competition Help: ML Olympiad Discussion Forum
Technical Help: Kaggle Contact Us Page

Good luck to you all !
----------------------
# Evaluation

***Goal***
It is your job to classify each image to it's appropriate country or culture
For each in the test set, you must predict the country as a string representing the country_label



***Metric***
Your score is the percentage of images you correctly classify. This is known as accuracy.



***Submission File Format***
You should submit a CSV file with exactly 978 entries plus a header row. Your submission will show an error if you have extra columns (beyond Id and country_label) or rows. The file should have exactly 2 columns: Id (sorted in any order) country_label (contains the label of the county associated with your classified image)



```
Id,country_label
0001,02
0002,55
0003,19
Etc.
```
You can download an example submission file (country_submission.csv) on the Data page.","# Dataset Description

The training and test sets contain images of architecture, food, clothing, tattoos, festivals, statues, monuments, and paintings from all north-African countries ( Algeria, Egypt, Lybia, Morocco, Mauritania, Sudan, and Tunisia). Each image contains one or multiple elements. 
The data has been approximately split 75%/25% for training/test. Each category has at least 1 instance in both the training and test datasets.",True,True
