5355,birdso-satellite-ml-2022,"# Description

## Welcome!
This is the page for the competition task of the BirdSO Machine Learning Event!

## Overview
There are many distinct features that can distinguish between bird calls, many of which are hard to track with the untrained ear. However, a neural network is very well capable of being able to conduct analysis on up to 61 ""genera of spectral features"" characteristic of 88 different bird species native to the United Kingdom. 


Your task is to develop a model using machine learning that can accurately associate a given bird call with a bird species, specified in the Data tab above.


## Acknowledgements

We thank xeno-canto: [www.xeno-canto.org](url) for providing the dataset, and Edoardo Ferrante for compiling the train and test datasets.
----------------------
# Evaluation

The metric used to calculate your score will be Categorization Accuracy.","# Dataset Description

## Files

*   **train.csv** - the training dataset consisting of 1,760 bird call recordings, each classified as belonging to a species of bird
*   **test.csv** - the test set consisting of 16,626 bird call recording, unclassified
*   **birdsong_metadata.csv** - supplemental information specifying classified species and other relevant classification data regarding each bird call recording


## Task
Develop and train a neural network on the given train dataset (train.csv) to classify bird calls as belonging to 1 of 88 distinct bird species listed in the metadata (birdsong_metadata.csv), and subsequently test its performance using the provided test dataset (test.csv). 

There are 61 genera of auditory spectral features that can be extracted from the recordings in the datasets, and each species of bird can count on 20 data points. For additional statistics regarding the datasets, please refer to [https://www.kaggle.com/fleanend/birds-songs-numeric-dataset](url) at which the datasets were compiled.

Your submission.csv file should be formatted as id,species for each test set case.

## Submissions
In the Code tab below the competition header above, select the ""New Notebook"" button. This should navigate you to a blank local API, called a Kaggle Kernel, in which you will be writing your code. After you have finished programming, select the ""Save Version"" button in the upper right corner. In the pop-up window, select the option ""Save & Run All (Commit)"" from the dropdown menu before confirming ""Save"". To submit your Kernel's generated .csv submission file, navigate back to Code tab on the competition platform, and select the ""Your Work"" tab. Select the first/most recent notebook, and select the ""Data"" tab at the top of the screen under the notebook name. On the right below ""Output"", select the ""submission.csv"" file and submit to the competition.

To submit your Kaggle Kernel/notebook to event supervisors at machine.learning@birdso.org, navigate to your notebook's editing page and select ""Download Notebook"" from the File dropdown at the top. Upload your notebook to an email addressed  to machine.learning@birdso.org with your team name and number for evaluation.",True,True
5356,galsenaixpaps-delivery-assignment,"# Description

> Welcome to ML Olympiad hosted by [GalsenAI](https://galsen.ai/) and [Paps](https://papslogistics.com/) ??

# What is ML Olympiad?

**ML Olympiads** are associated Kaggle Community Competitions hosted by ML GDEs (Here [Thierno](https://developers.google.com/community/experts/directory/profile/profile-thierno-ibrahima-diop)) or TFUGs, sponsored by Google Developers. 

# Goal of the Competition
The aim of this competition is to build a multi-class classification model capable of accurately predicting the most suitable driver for one or several given orders based on the destination of the order and the paths covered by the deliverers.

Your work will help Paps to optimize its deliveries by reducing the number of drivers needed during the deliveries.

## Context
PAPS is a Senegal-based logistics and delivery company that offers customers various logistics services. PAPS is one of the largest last-mile fleets in Senegal, making over 10 million deliveries across its two markets since its inception.

PAPS clients span a range of industries, such as Banking, Telecommunications, and Pharmaceuticals and each customer has specific delivery needs. Assigning the right type of delivery to the right driver quickly becomes a real challenge with such a high number of orders to process.

![Paps deliverers next to their van and making a delivery](https://papslogistics.com/wp-content/uploads/Paps-slider-12-1.jpg)

Until now, the assignment of orders to the appropriate deliverers was manual, which posed constraints in terms of processing time, scaling, and overall efficiency. Fortunately, the processing history has been maintained and continuously updated which allows the use of advanced analysis and prediction techniques to optimize the process.
#MLOlympiad
**Swag prizes for top winners are sponsored by Google Developers.**
----------------------
# Evaluation

Submissions for this competition are evaluated using [Mean F1-Score](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/F-score) between the predicted and expected answers.

F1 is calculated as follows: 
![F1 formula](https://inside-machinelearning.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/09/F1-Score.png)

Where:
![precision and recall formulas](https://miro.medium.com/max/888/1*7J08ekAwupLBegeUI8muHA.png)

The F1 metric weights recall and precision equally, and a good retrieval algorithm will maximize both precision and recall simultaneously. Thus, moderately good performance on both will be favored over extremely good performance on one and poor performance on the other.

**NOTE:**
&gt; - True Positive [TP]   = your prediction is 1, and the ground truth is also 1 - **you predicted a positive** and **that's true**!
- False Positive [FP]    = your prediction is 1, and the ground truth is 0 - **you predicted a positive**, and **that's false**.
- False Negative [FN] = your prediction is 0, and the ground truth is 1 - **you predicted a negative**, and **that's false**.

## Submission Format

**For every Order in the dataset**, submission files should contain two columns: `Order UID_` and `driver_id`. 
&gt; `driver_id` is between 0 and 79 and represents a mapping with the real id of the drivers.

The file should contain a header and have the following format:
```
Order UID_, driver_id
11326944f24cef4fcaaae0e7c391e21efe3d4d7c01af817917c08b842bbfc53a, 0
ea02e4c2c2d7c08037a7ad5c3a0d783a1e9edb162200f4dd5c5d6f7b4c0d070d, 0
169aa82c0225bf6f449b1b20e0090fa5a581e2f58cc2a17d85a20a58922b36f2, 0
ef73a6526107fd80fd7f87c453798e5a3f02edd7c0bf09e4ec178424f3d315cd, 0
4f9b60444a55153059a07baa92bf1b80d3638b6c9f2d4ea5bcb8242327690c86, 0
3545c1b564366d0aa09f678578ee00da3db38fda37fdf8abc5a99f94fec07226, 0
c9eae2911e82989777188303c543521d18a16cd0f4527253ca7d2a6be759a029, 0
3ab4e58e675eda0f76fb299fc78b0dd0b94af60b3252ddf0cad83ee072fa69a6, 0
473512d0b28cc619202cc04893559777a048bf9eaa5479520db129d799db8302, 0

```
----------------------
# Timeline

- **February 05, 2022** - Start Date.

- **March 05, 2022** - Final Submission Deadline.

All deadlines are at 11:59 PM UTC on the corresponding day unless otherwise noted. The competition organizers reserve the right to update the contest timeline if they deem it necessary.
----------------------
# Prizes

> **Swag prizes for the top 3 winners are sponsored by Google Developers.**
> **The cash prize of 150.000 FCFA is sponsored by PAPS.**
----------------------
# About Co-Sponsor PAPS

![Paps logo](https://play-lh.googleusercontent.com/ZK05n6eJ8SCAxaLbp2qHROPvmDkgTNUNW8bsTgGCLdKjhxijHxCF2ggc5e6Mxtjbhvon)
Founded in 2016, **Paps** is a Senegalese company that operates in end-to-end logistics. We offer innovative solutions to companies and merchants to ensure the distribution of documents and packages anywhere in Senegal, in the sub-region, and internationally.

## Services :
- Instant or scheduled pick-up of parcels and mail;
- Storage of goods in a secure warehouse that complies with standards;
- Delivery of insured parcels in a relay point or in last miles;
- Professional services: management and payment of cash on delivery, providing couriers, returns management, collection, and periodic reporting.

Our services are based on the use of information and communication technologies in order to respond to addressing problems in Africa.

Learn more [here](https://papslogistics.com/).","# Dataset Description

The dataset contains a history of thousands of deliveries made by Paps. It is anonymized real data from the Paps database and therefore may contain some noise and missing data.

## File descriptions
1. Training sets
*   **train_orders.csv** - order details
*   **train_parcels.csv** - parcel details related to orders
2. Test sets
*   **test_orders.csv** - order details
*   **test_parcels.csv** - parcel details related to orders
3. Other
*   **drivers_clean.csv** - information about the drivers

## Data Fields

*   `order_UID_`?- an anonymous id unique to a given delivery
*   `order_client_UID`?- an anonymous id unique to a given client
*   `driver UID_`?- an anonymous id unique to a given driver
*   `parcel UID_`?- an anonymous id unique to a given parcel
*   `size`?- size of a given parcel
*   `receiver_specification_address`?- delivery address
*   `Mission`?- Mission type
  -  `M_A_D`?- Provision of a driver to a customer for a given time
  -   `Messagerie`?- Regular delivery where the package is picked up from the customer, goes to the warehouse and is then delivered to the different recipients
  -   `Tourn¨¦e`?- Concerns clients who have several branches that are regularly visited to pick up or drop off packages",True,True
