5407,life-expectancy-multiclass-classification,"# Description

In this competition, you will build a multiclass classification model to predict the U.S. Region with a particular life expectancy value.

## Data sources
The used dataset has been generated from the following sources:
- [U.S. Life Expectancy at Birth by State and Census Tract - 2010-2015](https://catalog.data.gov/dataset/u-s-life-expectancy-at-birth-by-state-and-census-tract-2010-2015)
- [U.S. State Life Expectancy by Sex, 2018](https://catalog.data.gov/dataset/u-s-state-life-expectancy-by-sex-2018)

In addition to the previous datasets, the researchers found the following additional datasets:
- [U.S. Gross Domestic Product by County](https://www.bea.gov/data/gdp/gdp-county-metro-and-other-areas)
- [U.S. Census Bureau Regions and Divisions](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/cphalpert/census-regions/master/us%20census%20bureau%20regions%20and%20divisions.csv)

Thanks, to the [Versatile Data Kit](https://github.com/vmware/versatile-data-kit), deployed by VMware, we have built the final dataset, which is shown in the following figure:
![The Life Expectancy merged dataset](https://miro.medium.com/max/1400/1*gUrnawcL0_ZQYZc4YwascA.png)

You can read in more detail how we built the final dataset in [this article](https://towardsdatascience.com/from-raw-data-to-a-cleaned-database-a-deep-dive-into-versatile-data-kit-ab5fd992a02e), entitled From Raw Data to a Cleaned Database: A Deep Dive into Versatile Data Kit, as well as in the original [VDK Github repository](https://github.com/vmware/versatile-data-kit/tree/main/examples/life-expectancy).

## Objective
The objective of this competition is to build a multiclass classification system, that, given some input features related to life expectancy, predicts the U.S. region associated to that life expectancy.

Good Luck and have fun!






----------------------
# Evaluation

The evaluation metric for this competition is Categorization Accuracy

## Submission Format

**For every record in the test set, submission files should contain two columns: `Id` and `Category`. The `Id` corresponds to the Id of the row, `Category` corresponds to the predicted class.


The file should contain a header and have the following format:
```
Id,Category
1,West
```","# Dataset Description

Data include the following files

*   **train.csv** - the training set
*   **test.csv** - the test set
*   **sample_submission.csv** - a sample submission file in the correct format

In the training set, the column `region` is the class to predict.",True,True
