5448,classification-of-plants-of-southeast-asia,"# Description

We are pleased to cordially invite university students, who consider Data Science and related fields their careers, to attend the 3rd International Competition in Data Science & Artificial Intelligence, organized by The International Society of Data Scientists. Students graduated within 5 years are eligible to attend. Each team can optionally have an advisor, who may be a professor or a data science professional. The competition is to create a playground for young Data Scientists to grow skills, knowledge, experience, and collaboration for their career path. The competition committee includes professors and industry leaders around the world.

Professor Marc B?hlen has collected a machine-vision ready image collection of ethnobotanically significant flora of south-east Asia on the island of Bali in 2020 - 2021 together with Balinese residents with intimate local knowledge in coordination with expertise from the Indonesia National Research and Innovation Agency. He is willing to provide the data to the competition, and curious to see if you can take the challenge.

Will you be able to recognize these plants using machine learning and deep learning skills? Your team will submit the result for evaluation at the end of the competition.

The committee chairs of this competition track include:
Dr. Shaima Ali, Assistant Professor (Software Engineering), Electrical and Computer Engineering Department, Western University (Canada)
Marc B?hlen, Professor, Department of ART, Emerging Practices in Computational Media, University at Buffalo, New York, USA
Dr. Quang Hieu Vu, Head of Data Platform at ZaloPay
Dr. Christopher Do, ISODS President
Dr. Nam Nguyen, ISODS Vice President
Mr. Cory Wang, ISODS Vice President

## About - The International Society of Data Scientists

The International Society of Data Scientists (or The ISODS), at www.isods.org, registered as a Massachusetts non-profit, is a professional organization for Data Science and AI practitioners and researchers, which may include Data Scientists, Machine Learning Scientists, AI Scientists, Data Analysts, Data Engineers, Software Engineers, Risk Analysts, Actuaries, Business Analysts, and more, who apply Data Science and AI at work. ISODS promotes Data Science and AI domestically in the United States as well as internationally via professional exams, competitions, conferences, training, and publications.

## Acknowledgements

We thank Professor Marc B?hlen, Department of ART, Emerging Practices in Computational Media, University at Buffalo, New York, USA for providing this dataset.

We thank [Professors and Industry Leaders](https://www.isods.org/news-times/item/27-competition-committee-for-the-3rd-annual-international-data-science-ai-competition-for-the-year-2022) who volunteer to participate and contribute in the competition committee.

----------------------
# Evaluation

The evaluation metric for this competition is accuracy.

## Submission Format

Submission files  (*.csv) should contain two columns: `id` and `class`. `class` is the labels of the test dataset predicted by the model.

The file should contain a header and have the following format:
```
id, class
1.jpg,bamboo
2.jpg,mango
3.jpg,mango
```
----------------------
# What To Earn

The competition is to provide experience to young data scientists, who are students. We do not offer cash prizes according to Kaggle's rules. Instead, top performers will be selected to submit their reports as conference papers in the related conference by ISODS, and considered passing the ISODS Deep Learning 1 (DL1) exam if using the relevant approaches. Paper authors may choose to make the paper more interesting by considering this[ extra data](https://u.pcloud.link/publink/show?code=XZUqGVVZJ9lI5NUfTXSOQ8Qfoz5KVLJNT79y) in which there are more than one plant in each image.

`The ISODS provides professional exams toward several designations of the Society, including Associate Master (CM), Fellow Master (FM), and Grandmaster (GM). These titles are not related to similar titles by Kaggle.`
