----------------------
# Data Science At Fiverr

As you may have noticed, this competition is being run by **Fiverr**, an online platform that **connects freelance talent (including awesome data scientists like yourselves) to potential customers from around the world**.

**We're looking for people with great data science skills to join the platform and offer their services.** I encourage you all to take a minute and check out the [Data Science category](https://www.fiverr.com/categories/data/data-science/full-project?source=drop_down_filters&ref=project_type%3Acomputer_vision&utm_source=press&utm_medium=brand-partnerships&utm_campaign=bm_ge-ww_an-kaggle-seller-acq).

You'll see data scientists offering services in areas such as **computer vision, machine learning, natural language processing**, and more, and they are exposed to potential customers from around the world. 

They offer a wide range of services including providing **scripts for tagging & annotating data sets to building models to building fully functional apps**. 

![](https://www.googleapis.com/download/storage/v1/b/kaggle-forum-message-attachments/o/inbox%2F9686982%2F0efd007ddd03447762de37ec0b171ea8%2FScreen%20Shot%202022-08-08%20at%2010.30.07.png?generation=1659944790112628&alt=media)","# Dataset Description

Your goal is to predict the probability of whether a new user to the Fiverr platform will become a spammer based on actions taken before and after registering to the platform. 

- The training set contains anonymized data on ¡À456K unique users. The `label` column indicates whether or not the user became a spammer. 
- The test set contains anonymized data on ¡À24K unique users. 

## Files

*   **train.csv** - the training set
*   **test.csv** - the test set
*   **sample_submission.csv** - a sample submission file in the correct format

## Columns in the Training Set

*   `label` - indicates whether or not the user became a spammer. A ""1"" indicates the user became a spammer, a ""0"" indicates the user did not become a spammer. 
*   `user_id`?- the unique ID of the user
*   Columns X1 through X51 are different parameters that a user took before or after registering to the platform. This could be things like ""whether or not the username contains an underscore"" or ""the number of characters in the users email"" or ""whether a user came from a valid referrer (i.e. google, bing, or another site)."" Due to privacy issues, columns for all of these parameters have been named X with a following number.  

## Solution 

In your solution, you need to provide 2 columns for each of the ¡À24K users you're making predictions on:

*   `user_id`?- definition of feature_1
*   `prediction` - where you predict whether or not the user became a spammer, related to the `label` column in the training set.",True,True
