5486,kaggle-knight1,"# Description

## Note
Hackathon will end sharp at 27th February 2PM.

**1. Introduction**
Kaggle Knight is a 36 hour long thrilling hackathon, where you will be asked to solve tasks of varying complexities designed by
experts and the participants coming up with the most innovative and efficient
solutions will be rewarded.

**2. Problem Statement**
Companies these days have the opportunity to develop sophisticated predictive models to boost their sales and make better marketing plans. Thanks to the increasing amount of data being created by people online, companies have an almost bottom-less pool of critical information. But not all of it is relevant. It takes a lot of effort to sift through all that data, figure out what's relevant and what's not, and then put all the relevant data to work and create a marketing plan. But Machine Learning can make this process a lot easier.

Design a Machine Learning model to predict if a client will subscribe to a term deposit or not.

We will provide a marketing campaign data set to the participants: it will be in categorical and numerical formats. The participants will select various parameters from that data set based on the relevance and train their ML models to predict whether a certain customer will subscribe to a term deposit or not.

Remarks: Participants have the freedom to integrate their model into a mobile app or a web app. They can make this choice according to their requirements.

**3. Event Structure**
¡ñ Platform: Kaggle
¡ñ Notebooks as well as CSV files have to be submitted here.
¡ñ Team Size: 1-4 people.
¡ñ Duration: 36 hours (26th February 8 AM  - 27th February 2 PM.
¡ñ Judging criteria: According to the accuracy on the Kaggle leaderboard. More about that on the Evaluation page.
¡ñ Theme: India in 2030-40-50.
¡ñ We will have a single problem statement.
¡ñ Each team will be given Certificate of Participation.

**4. Judging Criteria**
¡ñ According to the categorization accuracy on the Kaggle leaderboard.
¡ñ Testing Time. Precision Score, Recall, F1 Score, and AUC will be used in case of ties.
¡ñ The top 3 teams will have to make a presentation in front of the panel and
based on their scores by the panel, ranks will be given.

**5. Submission Criteria**
¡ñ Actual testing data will be uploaded on Kaggle at 26th February 2 PM. Submissions after 26th February 2 PM will only be considered.
¡ñ 10 submissions can be made per day.
¡ñ Please Submit a Zip file containing the submission csv file and the .py file of the code.

**Note**
All decisions taken by the organizing team will be deemed as final, and no
more changes will be encouraged, thus holding the full authority to change
any of the above rules as per circumstances.

## Acknowledgements

We thank Matellio for sponsoring this event and providing this dataset.
----------------------
# Evaluation

## Evaluation

¡ñ The evaluation will be done using categorization accuracy on Kaggle leaderboard.
¡ñ Include metrics Submission time, Precision, Recall, F1 score, and AUC in notebook, as it will be used for in case of ties.
¡ñ Submit your submission csv file with columns 'Id' and 'Category'.","# Dataset Description

## Important Note

**For preserving confidentiality of the dataset, actual testing data will be uploaded at 26th February 2 PM. Submissions after 26th February 2 PM will be only valid. So do not waste your 10 submissions per day on submitting before that. No excuses will be entertained on this matter.**

## Dataset Provided

Data contains two files:

**1. xtrain_csv.csv**

It contains 16 features ('age', 'job', 'marital', 'education', 'default', 'balance', 'housing', 'loan', 'contact', 'day', 'month', 'duration', 'campaign', 'pdays', 'previous', 'poutcome').


**2. yrain_csv.csv**

It contains outcomes in 'yes' or 'no' labels. 

**3. xtest_csv.csv**

It contains 16 features ('age', 'job', 'marital', 'education', 'default', 'balance', 'housing', 'loan', 'contact', 'day', 'month', 'duration', 'campaign', 'pdays', 'previous', 'poutcome').

**4. sample_sub_csv.csv**

Contains the sample submission csv file.

## Acknowledgements

We thank Matellio for sponsoring this event and providing this dataset.",True,True
5487,funml-hw4-p6,"# Description

## **Problem 6: Implementing Image Segmentation via Unsupervised Clustering on Kaggle Competition (20pts)**

This is a Kaggle competition problem where you are asked to perform unsupervised clustering on an RGB image using the algorithms you studied in class in conjunction with the various feature combinations and color spaces. We provide you with two images: a simple image consisting of geometric shapes and another one containing more complicated objects, both in RGB. The images can be downloaded by running the following snippet of code:

```
!gdown --id 1ZAvUJktJ0aojeXWJnuxuYqHlLslCZ9T-
!gdown --id 1Qh2HppgVSAniVqWxRsbJ7cZFhUpRdUpI
```
You can then load the two images as shown below:

```
import imageio

im1 = imageio.imread('img1.png')
im2 = imageio.imread('img2.png')
```

Since this is an open-ended question, you should try to design your own features to achieve better classification results. By submitting your result to Kaggle, you will see your multi-class classification accuracy and ranking on the leaderborad. 10 pts will depend on your ranking (top 10% get 10pts, top 11%-20% get 9pts, etc.), and another 5 pts depend on your method explanation and clear, well-labeled plots and images.<br>

[Note:]
- After having your ideal result, please save your result in `result_img1` and `result_img2` in the cell below.

- We have defined the label for each class in each image. Make sure you use the same settings as us and feel free to use the provided swapping label code to swap labels if needed.

 - for `img1.png`, use k=3, background labels as 0, rectangle labels as 1 and triangle labels as 2
 - for `img2.png`, use k=2, background labels as 0, dog labels as 1 

- After your `result_img1` and `result_img2` are ready, run the cell below to create a `submission.csv`. Please download it from this notebook and submit it in our [Kaggle](https://www.kaggle.com/c/funml-hw4-p6) competition.

- Please remember to note your Kaggle competition nickname in this notebook. We will use your ranking to grade.

- You have 10 submission quota each day to submit your result and get your multi-class classification accuracy and ranking.

- We calculate the multi-class classification accuracy with ground-turth hand-crafted labels in both images by 

$$\text{Accuracy} = \frac{\text{# of correctly labeled pixels}}{\text{total # of pixels}}$$

### Reference

T.-Y. Lin, M. Maire, S. Belongie, J. Hays, P. Perona, D. Ramanan, P. Dollar, and C. L. Zitnick. Microsoft COCO: Com- ¡ä
mon objects in context. In ECCV, 2014.
----------------------
# Evaluation

Submit the submission.csv file generated from .ipynb file.","# Dataset Description

Data is in the .pynb file.",True,True
