5519,chemicalengineeringhackathonchemplus2022,"# Description

Are you a Chemical Engineer interested in the non traditional fields of Machine learning and Artificial Intelligence? Are you a Machine learning Enthusiast who is curious how chemical engineers make use of these techniques, we have you covered with the Chemical Engineering Hackathon.

Format:
Participants can participate either individually or in teams of 2 
This competition will be held in 2 rounds
Participants will be solving the first stage of the PS on kaggle from 5/03/22( change according to when we want to put this up)
Top 5 winners from the first round will be called upon to present their solution in front of an expert panel.
The final prizes will be distributed after considering the combined performance  in both the rounds.



----------------------
# Evaluation

Evaluation is based on categorical Accuracy. 
The evaluation obtained here is based on 30% of the test data uploaded.","# Dataset Description

In this competition you will be predicting the type of defects found in alloys. Images are named with a unique ID. You must classify the defects in the test set.

Each image may have no defects (not included in the train.csv), a defect of a single class, or defects of multiple classes. For each image you must segment defects of each class (Class = [0, 1, 2, 3, 4]).

The segment annotations are also provided for training purposes.

 the data set will be provided through a drive link 
The file uploaded here for publishing sake",True,True
