----------------------
# Evaluation

### Evaluation metric

The evaluation metric for this competition is [Area Under Receiver Operating Characteristic Curve (AUC-ROC)](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Receiver_operating_characteristic). 

### Submission Format

For each `row_id` in the test set, you must predict a value for the `anomaly` variable. The file should contain a header and have the following format:

```
row_id,anomaly
0,0
1,0
2,1
```
----------------------
# Timeline

## Competition Timeline

  - April 27, 2022: Competition start date.
  - July 24, 2022: Entry deadline. You must accept the competition rules before this date in order to compete.
  - July 24, 2022: Team merger deadline. This is the last day participants may join or merge teams.
  - July 31, 2022: Final submission deadline.

All deadlines are at 23:59 UTC on the corresponding day unless otherwise noted. We, as competition organizers, reserve the right to update the contest timeline if we deem it necessary.
----------------------
# Acknowledgements

##Acknowledgements

We thank the organizers of the [ASHRAE - Great Energy Predictor III]( https://www.kaggle.com/c/ashrae-energy-prediction/) competition and [winning teams](https://www.kaggle.com/competitions/ashrae-energy-prediction/leaderboard) for their datasets and solutions. We would also like to thank the [Large-scale Energy Anomaly Detection (LEAD) project](https://github.com/samy101/lead-dataset) team members to establish a taxonomy of generalizable anomalies prevalent in the building energy data and then putting in several man-hours to carefully annotate and validate this extended dataset. The training set used in this competition is a subset from the [LEAD project](https://github.com/samy101/lead-dataset). A final complete version with annotated meter readings from all buildings will be released later. A detailed description of the anomaly annotation process and initial benchmarks are presented in [this article](https://arxiv.org/abs/2203.17256). 
