5633,fashion-and-beauty-reviews,"# Description

We are pleased to cordially invite university students, who consider Data Science and related fields their careers, to attend the 3rd International Competition in Data Science & Artificial Intelligence, organized by The International Society of Data Scientists. Students graduated within 5 years are eligible to attend. Each team can optionally have an advisor, who may be a professor or a data science professional. The competition is to create a playground for young Data Scientists to grow skills, knowledge, experience, and collaboration for their career path. The competition committee includes professors and industry leaders around the world.

In this NLP track, you will predict how satisfied customers are based on their product reviews, to help with insight in fashion and beauty products. 

The committee chairs of this competition track include:
Dr. Renzhi Cao, Assistant Professor at the Department of Computer Science, Pacific Lutheran University (Washington, USA)
Dr. Phu Vu, Regional Research Director at WorldQuant
Dr. Mohammad Soltanieh-ha, Assistant Professor at Questrom School of Business, Boston University (Massachusetts, USA)
Dr. Jianmo Ni, Software Engineer, Google
Dr. Christopher Do, ISODS President
Dr. Nam Nguyen, ISODS Vice President
Mr. Cory Wang, ISODS Vice President

## About - The International Society of Data Scientists

The International Society of Data Scientists (or The ISODS), at www.isods.org, registered as a Massachusetts non-profit, is a professional organization for Data Science and AI practitioners and researchers, which may include Data Scientists, Machine Learning Scientists, AI Scientists, Data Analysts, Data Engineers, Software Engineers, Risk Analysts, Actuaries, Business Analysts, and more, who apply Data Science and AI at work. ISODS promotes Data Science and AI domestically in the United States as well as internationally via professional exams, competitions, conferences, training, and publications.

## Acknowledgements

We thank Dr. Jianmo Ni from Google for the help with this dataset.

We thank [Professors and Industry Leaders](https://www.isods.org/news-times/item/27-competition-committee-for-the-3rd-annual-international-data-science-ai-competition-for-the-year-2022) who volunteer to participate and contribute in the competition committee.

----------------------
# Evaluation

The evaluation metric for this competition is RMSE (Root Mean Square Error).

## Submission Format

For every row in the test dataset, submission files (*.csv) should contain two columns: id and rating. 

The file should contain a header and have the following format:
```
id, rating
1,5
2,4
3,4
```
Note that the id column in the solution submission is just the row number in the ```review_test_post.tsv``` file (the id of 1 is the first review, the id of 2 is the second review, etc.; the last id is 250997)
----------------------
# What To Earn

The competition is to provide experience to young data scientists, who are students. We do not offer cash prizes according to Kaggle's rules. Instead, top performers will be selected to submit their reports as conference papers in the related conference by ISODS, and considered passing the ISODS Deep Learning 2 (DL2) exam if using the relevant approaches.

`The ISODS provides professional exams toward several designations of the Society, including Associate Master (CM), Fellow Master (FM), and Grandmaster (GM). These titles are not related to similar titles by Kaggle.`
----------------------
# Timeline

Start Date - March 28, 2022

Entry Deadline - Same as the Final Submission Deadline.

Team Merger Deadline - Same as the Final Submission Deadline.

Final Submission Deadline - June 19, 2022

All deadlines are at 11:59 PM UTC on the corresponding day unless otherwise noted. The competition organizers reserve the right to update the contest timeline if they deem it necessary.
----------------------
# All The Tracks

All Kaggle-based Community Competition Tracks are:

1> Company Bankruptcy Prediction
https://www.kaggle.com/c/company-bankruptcy-prediction

2> Classification of plants of Southeast Asia
https://www.kaggle.com/c/classification-of-plants-of-southeast-asia

3> Fashion and Beauty Review Classification
https://www.kaggle.com/competitions/fashion-and-beauty-review-classification/

There is no limitation in term of the number of tracks a team or individual can participate.

Top performers will be selected to submit their reports as conference papers in the related conference by ISODS. 

Top performers in track 1 are considered passing the ISODS Machine Learning exam; in track 2 as passing the Deep Learning 1 (DL1) exam; in track 3 as passing the Deep Learning 2 (DL2) exam. See more about ISODS Professional Exams organized by the International Institute of Data Science and Artificial Intelligence at ISODS website (https://www.isods.org).
----------------------
# Committee

The [competition committee composition](https://www.isods.org/item/27-competition-committee-for-the-3rd-annual-international-data-science-ai-competition-for-the-year-2022) is as follows:

