1. NASA/JPL-Caltech, Venus image, 1974, https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Venus_from_Mariner_10.jpg
1. ESA & MPS for OSIRIS Team, Mars image, 2007, https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:OSIRIS_Mars_true_color.jpg
1. pschemp, Gender Symbol image, 2006, https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Combotrans.svg
In this competition, students need to predict the gender (male or female) associated with an image of a celebrity face.
----------------------
# Evaluation

The evaluation metric is [**accuracy score**](https://scikit-learn.org/stable/modules/generated/sklearn.metrics.accuracy_score.html), which is the default classification accuracy in `sklearn` library.

Use `*sampleSubmission.csv` file template to populate your submission labels or you can generate your submission file from Pandas in the following format:

        id,y
        x10a06,0
        x10a2d,1
        x10a60,0","# Dataset Description

