5669,ih-hotel-booking,"# Description

Booking cancellations often directly impact a hotel's bottom line: many times the room(s) reserved are not booked again, resulting in lower occupation and, subsequently, revenue. To hedge this risk, hotels often demand a booking deposit, often calculated as a percentage of the reservations full price. However, this practice can directly impact demand as some customers might look for different hotels with no deposit (or a smaller one). Our goal is to build a model that, by predicting whether a booking will be cancelled or not, can be used by the hotel to implement different risk-aware strategies for calculating the deposit size. 

Let's use our recently acquired ML skillset to build a classifier! In this case we've been asked to create a model predicting booking cancellations in 2 different hotels. The data utilized here is real world anonymized data.

Data source:  https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S2352340918315191
----------------------
# Evaluation

The evaluation metric for this competition is [Mean F1-Score](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/F-score). The F1 score, commonly used in information retrieval, measures accuracy using the statistics precision \( \text{p} \) and recall \( \text{r} \).

Precision is the ratio of true positives \(\text{tp}\) to all predicted positives \(\text{tp} + \text{fp}\). Recall is the ratio of true positives \(\text{tp}\) to all actual positives \(\text{tp} + \text{fn}\). The F1 score is given by:

\[ \text{F1} = 2\frac{\text{p} \cdot \text{r}}{\text{p}+\text{r}}\ \ \mathrm{where}\ \ \text{p} = \frac{\text{tp}}{\text{tp}+\text{fp}},\ \ \text{r} = \frac{\text{tp}}{\text{tp}+\text{fn}} \]

The F1 metric weights recall and precision equally, and a good retrieval algorithm will maximize both precision and recall simultaneously. Thus, moderately good performance on both will be favored over extremely good performance on one and poor performance on the other.

## Submission Format

**For every id_booking in the validation dataset** provide a binary prediction of the cancellation status (`is_cancelled` in the training dataset). The file provided must have two columns:

- **id_booking** from the validation set
- **is_cancelled** from your predictions.","# Dataset Description

The files provided are:

- Training set (`tb_hotel_traintest.csv`) with all features and the response variable (`is_cancelled`)
- Validation set (`tb_hotel_feat_valid.csv`) with all features for making predictions
- Sample submission (`tb_hotel_sample_valid.csv`), which is an example of the file you must submit with predictions made from the validation set.

The PDF file contains more extensive description of each variable in the dataset.

## Files

*   **tb_hotel_traintest.csv** - the training set
*   **tb_hotel_feat_valid.csv** - the validation set
*   **tb_hotel_sample_valid.csv** - a sample submission file in the correct format

## Columns

* **hotel** - (str) Tipo de hotel.
* **is_cancelled** - (binary) Vari¨¢vel bin¨¢ria indicando cancelamento da reserva (0 = n?o cancelada, 1 = cancelada) - vari¨¢vel resposta do case.
* **lead_time** - (int) N¨²mero de dias entre data da reserva e data de entrada no hotel (quando a reserva foi feita).
* **arrival_date** - (date) Data de entrada no hotel (para quando a reserva ¨¦).
* **stays_in_weekend_nights** - (int) N¨²mero de dias em finais de semana na reserva.
* **stays_in_week_nights** - (int) N¨²mero de dias de semana na reserva.
* **adults** - (int) N¨²mero de adultos.
* **children** - (int) N¨²mero de crian?as.
* **babies** - (int) N¨²mero de bebes.
* **meal** - (str) Tipo de refei??o inclusa na reserva.
* **country** - (str) Pa¨ªs do cliente.
* **market_segment** - (str) Segmenta??o de marketing do cliente.
* **distribution_channel** - (str) Canal de vendas pelo qual a reserva foi feita.
* **is_repeated_guest** - (binary) O cliente j¨¢ ficou hospedado no hotel? (0 = n?o, 1 = sim).
* **previous_cancellations** - (int) Quantas reservas o cliente j¨¢ cancelou no passado.
* **previous_bookings_not_canceled** - (int) Quantas reservas o cliente j¨¢ fez e n?o cancelou no passado.
* **reserved_room_type** - (str) Tipo de quarto desejado.
* **assigned_room_type** - (str) Tipo de quarto reservado.
* **booking_changes** -  (str) N¨²mero de mudan?as na reserva entre data de reserva e entrada/cancelamento.
* **deposit_type** - (str) Tipo de adiantamento feito no momento da reserva.
* **agent** - (str) ID do Agente que fez a reserva (NA caso a reserva n?o tenha sido feita por um agente).
* **company**  - (str) ID da empresa que fez a reserva (NA caso a reserva n?o seja corporativa)
* **days_in_waiting_list** - (int) Quantos dias demorou a confirma??o da reserva.
* **customer_type** - (str) Tipo de reserva.
* **adr** - (float) Average Daily Rate, pre?o m¨¦dio de cada di¨¢ria na reserva.
* **required_car_parking_spaces** - (int) N¨²mero de vagas em estacionamento requisitadas na reserva.
* **total_of_special_requests** - (int) N¨²mero de requisi??es especiais na reserva (cama dupla, andar, quarto com vista...)
* **reservation_status_date** - (date) Data da ¨²ltima atualiza??o feita na reserva.",True,True
5670,sce-dl-course-spring-2022-part-2,"# Description

Your goal is to predict the label for test data values, based on the text (do not use the ID column! If you do, your score will be 0, and you will be at the bottom of the kaggle table).
Represent the text using a word embedding model with pre-trained word vectors. 
The choice of word vectors is up to you, and so is the choice of a package that retrieves them.
Then build a neural net using Keras and Dense layers; Drop layers can be used if your net overfits.
Train the net on the training data and evaluate it on the validation data. Your job is to get accuracy as high as possible for the validation set.
Then run your trained classifier on the test set and save the label you produce for every item in .csv file, as described below.
Note: you can use any of the normalization and data analysis methods in sklearn to improve your scores. You can filter the data any way you wish, as long as the code is written by you.
----------------------
# Evaluation

The evaluation metric for this competition is categorization accuracy (avg per all classes). Note that you have 7 classes! I.e. the problem is harder than the 1st competition.","# Dataset Description

Training set (text & labels)
