In this competition we use [Pearson correlation coefficient](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pearson_correlation_coefficient). Thus, the magnitude of your forecasts is not as important as their direction. If the direction of your forecasts is aligned with the direction of the observed closing prices (held out in Kaggle), then your correlation coefficient will be higher on the leaderboard. Read more in the Evaluation section of [Crypto Forecasting](https://www.kaggle.com/c/g-research-crypto-forecasting/overview/evaluation) competition from G-Research and their [tutorial](https://www.kaggle.com/cstein06/tutorial-to-the-g-research-crypto-competition).

