5691,deeplearning-hw2-transformer,"# Description

## Introduce
This is the Kaggle competition for  HW2 in NYCU Deep Learning Course.

Given the title and the content of the news, you need to train a model to correctly classify the news into 4 different category:

1.  World
2. Sports
3. Business
4. Sci/Tech

## Upload
You need to upload the result file for the submission
Details of the format, please check the Evaluation and Data
You need to upload related file to NewE3 (Check the announcement on NewE3 for details)

## Rules
Only one person as a team
The team name should name as your student ID, i.e. 08XXXXX, AXXXXXX, BXXXXXX
You can submit the answer 20 times every 24 hours
Do not share your result with your classmate

## Score Rules
Pass Transformer-Baseline, 15%
----------------------
# Evaluation

## Evaluation Metric
[Accuracy](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Accuracy_and_precision)

## Submission Format
Submission files should contain only one columns: Category (World, Sports, Business, Sci/Tech)

The file should contain a header and have the same format as [sample_submission.csv](https://www.kaggle.com/competitions/deeplearning-hw2-transformer/data?select=sample_submission.csv)","# Dataset Description

## File Description
train.csv - training set

test.csv - testing set for the leaderboard ranking and final scoring

sample_submission.csv - the sample submission file in the correct format

## Data Fields
Id - an anonymous id unique to a given news title

Category - the label category of the news title

Title - the title of the news

Description - news content",True,True
5692,project-2022-mpc-m1,"# Description

This dataset contains 13397 house prices composed of 20 different features:

*    id - unique identified for a house
*   pricePrice - is prediction target
*  bedroomsNumber - of Bedrooms/House
*  bathroomsNumber - of bathrooms/bedrooms
* sqft_livingsquare - footage of the home
* sqft_lotsquare - footage of the lot
*  floorsTotal - floors (levels) in house
*    waterfront - House which has a view to a waterfront
*   view - An index from 0 to 4 of how good the view of the property was
*  condition - How good the condition is ( Overall )
*    grade - overall grade given to the housing unit, based on King County grading system
*    sqft_above - square footage of house apart from basement
*    sqft_basement - square footage of the basement
*    yr_built - Built Year
*    yr_renovated - Year when house was renovated
*    zipcode - zip
*    lat - Latitude coordinate
*    long - Longitude coordinate
*    sqft_living15 - The square footage of interior housing living space for the nearest 15 neighbors
*    sqft_lot15 - The square footage of the land lots of the nearest 15 neighbors

The purpose of this project is to predict the price of unknown houses.
----------------------
# Evaluation

The evaluation metric for this competition is [Mean Squarred Error](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mean_squared_error). 
 $$MSE = \frac{1}{n} \sum_{i=1}^n (Yi-\hat{Y}i)^2$$

## Submission Format
For every house in the dataset</strong>, submission files should contain two columns: ID and Price.","# Dataset Description

The file 'houses.csv' contains 15762 houses represented by multiple information as explained in the section 'Overview'. The file 'house_competition.csv' contains 2365 new houses for which we do not have the price. The purpose is to predict the price of each new house using regression algorithms that we have seen in this course.",True,True
