description:
Here's the deal amigos!
You guys are given a dataset which will help farmers to get the cost of best quality crops.

The Challenge:

Raju really likes to compete on Kaggle, and he is in parallel universe on earth 8 where he already know the exact ratio of nutrients and minerals in
different crops and he also loves to play with data and extract useful patterns from data.

Features of parallel universe(some strange rules of earth 8):
there exist negative currency.
different states and crops doesn't make any difference in crop's cost, every crop have its own unique content of minerals and nutrients
based on its minerals and nutrients ratio.

He found a dataset on kaggle "" "" where he needs to find the cost of the crops with given parameters.

Data fields
Here's a brief version of what you'll find in the data description file.
k_ratio : potassium ratio in crop.
p_ratio : phosphorous ratio.
n_ratio : nitrogen ratio.
temp: temperature in which crops are going to be yield.
ph: ph of the crop(after using pesticides and all).
humidity: humidity in environment.
rainfall: level of rainfall in mm.
states: states in which crop is being grown.
crop: name of crops
Cost: target variable(cost of crop).
----------------------
