5726,ds36-whiskey-review-classification,"# Description

## Objective
Your objective is to train a text classification model to analyze textual reviews of certain whiskeys in order to predict the type of whiskey being reviewed.

## Background
The training dataset contains textual reviews of different kinds of whiskeys, and the category of whiskey being reviewed (1: Scotch, 2: Bourbon/Tennessee, 3: Craft, 4: Canadian).

However the training dataset contains textual reviews, but no categories. So your job is to produce a solutions file that contains your model's predicted category for each of the reviews in the training set.

## Data Dictionary
The competition data has been obtained from the Whiskey Advocate.

## Files
- train.csv - the training set
- test.csv - the test set
- sample_submission.csv - a sample submission file in the correct format

## Columns
- id: the review's unique identifier
- description: the review text itself
- category: the type of whiskey being reviewed (1: Scotch, 2: Bourbon/Tennessee, 3: Craft, 4: Canadian)","# Dataset Description

## Files

*   **train.csv** - the training set
*   **test.csv** - the test set
*   **sample_submission.csv** - a sample submission file in the correct format
*   **WhiskyFlavorDescriptors.csv** - supplemental information about the data

## Data Dictionary
- id - the review's unique identifier
- description the review text itself
- category the type of whiskey being reviewed",False,True
5727,idc-challenge-2022,"# Description

The goal of the IDC22 challenge in data science applied to bank marketing data is to score the best AUC for the given data.
----------------------
# Evaluation

The evaluation metric for this competition is **AUC** (Area Under ROC Curve).
<h2>Submission Format</h2>

Submission files should contain two columns: Id and Predicted
Id goes from 1 to 8238
Predicted values between 0 and 1, are the probability that customer Id belong to class label 'yes'

The file should contain a header and have the following format:

<pre>Id,Predicted<br>1,1<br>2,0.9<br>...<br></pre>

An example of submission file (sample_submission.csv) is available in the Data Section","# Dataset Description


<h2>File descriptions</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>data_desc.txt</strong> - description of the data</li>
<li><strong>training_data.csv</strong> - the training set</li>
<li><strong>training_classes.csv</strong> - the classes of the training data</li>
<li><strong>test_data.csv</strong> - the test set</li>
<li><strong>sample_submission.csv</strong> - a sample submission file in the correct format</li>
</ul>",False,True
