5814,bas-479-spring-22-option-1-will-they-donate,"# Description

See Canvas.

You are going to develop a model to predict if an alumnus will donate to UT in 2021 using information known about them through 2020.  The hope is that the patterns the model discovers will generalize into the future.  In other words, we can input what we know about the alumnus up through 2021 to come up with a good guess as to their probability of donating in 2022.
----------------------
# Evaluation

Your evaluation will be based on the AUC (area under the ROC curve). This allows the model to be tuned toward identifying the set of most likely individuals to donate (even if those probabilities aren't that high).","# Dataset Description

See Canvas for the .RData file you'll need to use to make predictions. The data attached here is simply a set of reviews for Ben & Jerry's ice cream and has nothing to do with this case.  But...ice cream!",False,True
5815,bas-479-spring-22-option-2-donation-amounts,"# Description

See Canvas.

You are going to develop a model to predict how much an alumnus has donated to UT as of 2021. The hope is that the patterns the model discovers will generalize into the future. In other words, we can input what we know about the alumnus up through 2021 to come up with a good guess as to what they have donated to UT so far.  This could help gauge and predict the lifetime value of graduates.
----------------------
# Evaluation

Entries will be gauged based on the RMSE.  Since predictions are for the log10 of the total amount of cash given, the RMSE (at least 10^RMSE) tells us the factor by which the predicted values are off from the true values.","# Dataset Description

See Canvas for the RData file used to build models and make predictions.  This is just an unrelated dataset I found on my computer.",False,True
