5817,sales-forecasting-in-covid-period,"# Description


This competition intends to predict the monthly sales/revenue of a business during the covid times. The objective is to include various public datasets and use the relevant data points that would help in correctly predicting the sales behavior.  


Example of some of the additional data points:    

- Stimulus given by US govt. during this period to everyone
- Crude prices
- vehicles sales
- GDP growth
- Unemployment Rate
- ...and so on
  


The intent here is to pick not all, but few of the variables that provide the most accurate prediction of sales. This will help in understanding which are the key data points that affect the sales, apart from the usual features","# Dataset Description

*Dependent Variable* : TOTAL_RETAIL

**Data is provided at weekly Level**

The data provided is from 1st week of 2018 to last week of 2020. There are a total of 156 weeks of sales data.

**Observation / Training Window**  

The first 144 weeks should be taken up as the observation or training window (Week 1 - 2018 to Week 40 - 2020)

**Prediction window**   

The last 12 weeks should be taken up as the prediction window (Week 41-2020 to Week 52-2020)",False,True
5818,sarahgetsadiamond-insead-dsb-22d,"# Description

Case: ¡°Sarah Gets a Diamond¡±, UVA-QA-0702 + data

The file ¡°Sarah Gets a Diamond data.xls¡± contains data about various attributes for over 9000 diamonds. For the first 6000 you also have the price.

The goal of this competition is to use the tools you've learned in previous courses to predict the prices of the remaining diamonds (i.e., those with IDs 6001 and above).

When done, create a spreadsheet containing two columns: ID and Price. For IDs, put 6001, 6002, etc., and for the prices, put the numerical values of your predictions (without dollar signs, or any other strings), e.g., 12345.6, 23456.7, etc.

Save the resultant file in the CSV format and submit it. Make sure the column names follow the uppercase and lowercase format and are exactly ID and Price. Example:
![Example of submission format ](https://i.imgur.com/kHxYOPk.jpg)


Your submission will be immediately scored on a fraction of the diamonds according to the Mean Absolute Percentage Error (MAPE) metric that we will discuss in class. The lower, the better.

## Acknowledgements

[http://store.darden.virginia.edu/sarah-gets-a-diamond ](http://store.darden.virginia.edu/sarah-gets-a-diamond)
