5820,breathe-pollen-classification,"# Description

BREATHE 

<h2>Pollen Classification competition</h2>
<p>Real-Time Airborne Particle Identifier Rapid-E from Plair SA is designed for real-time sampling and analysis of airborne particles. Compared to its predecessor PA-300   it delivers full time-resolved 24-angle scattering of near-UV laser beam, deep-UV laser-induced fluorescence in 32 measuring channels within a spectral range of 350¨C800 nm, eight sequential acquisitions with 500 ns retention and lifetime fluorescence at four spectral bands: 350-400, 420-460, 511-572, 672-800 and 2 ns temporal resolution. Recent studies indicate the use of flow cytometry has the potential for identification of bioaerosols , but dealing with a huge amount of diverse data makes AI method of choice for analysis.</p>

<h2>Data</h2>
<p>Three data modalities:</p>
- lifetime
- spectrum
- scattering
- size feature from scattering
- lifetime features

<h2>Acknowledgements</h2>
<p>We thank BREATHE project for providing this dataset.</p>

----------------------
# Evaluation

The evaluation metric for this competition is **Macro F1-Score**

Submission Format
Use empty solution file from Data page and enter predicted labels. Choose file name that will help you to follow progress and related to model/experiment you used to generate solution.","# Dataset Description

</p> Data are packed into csv files containing scattered light, fluorescence spectrum and lifetime of fluorescence signals for every sampled particle, additional features from scattering and lifetime data are also available </p>

<h2>File descriptions</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Training data</strong> - contains data files named according to data source type along with labels file, corresponding to pollen types</li>
<li><strong>Test data</strong> - in same format as training data, but without labels file</li>
<li><strong>sample.csv</strong> - a sample submission file in the correct format</li>
<li><strong>submission.csv</strong> - the submission file that should be filled in with the results of the classifications</li>
</ul>",False,True
