5846,hmsbigdata7,"# Description

In this competition you will have to predict finish times for participants last year's Challenge Roth Triathlon. The Challenge Roth is very popular with thousands of participants every year, and multiple world records have been broken here in the past

The Challenge Roth is a triathlon over Iron Man distance. Meaning participants will have to swim 3.86K, Bike 180.2K and run a marathon at the end. Your task is to predict finish times based on split times. However, you will only get the transfer times, first 2 bike splits and first 3 running splits!

The challenge is to predict finish times as accurate as possible. Like any data science challenges there will be simple and complex solutions. You are free to use any model you want, and you will still get your grade points if you finish last. But like in the triathlon, you will only get your medal if you actually finish, so make sure to upload your solution before the deadline
----------------------
# Evaluation

The evaluation metric for this competition is RMSE . The Root Mean Squared Error (RMSE) tells you something about the accuracy of your predictions. The higher the RMSE, the further your prediction differs from the truth

For every athlete in the dataset, submission files should contain two columns: id and predicted. id should be set as the index column of your submission file. and predicted contains the predicted finish times for all athletes in the test set. Make sure your submission has this format, otherwise you will not be able to upload your submission to Kaggle.","# Dataset Description

<p>Here you can find all the data that you need. You will find a .csv file with training data (features and actual finish times), a test-set with just the features (you will need to predict finish times on this dataset and upload your solutions), and a sample that shows you what you solutionfile should look like.</p>

<h2>File descriptions</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>challenge_train.csv</strong> - the training set</li>
<li><strong>challenge_predict_set.csv</strong> - the test set</li>
<li><strong>ExampleSolution.csv</strong> - a sample submission file in the correct format</li>

<h2>Data fields</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>id</strong> - participant id</li>
<li><strong>Category</strong> - participant category (age group & pro/am)</li>
<li><strong>Finish_Time</strong> - actual finish times in seconds</li>
<li><strong>Swim_To_Bike_Transfer</strong> - time to transfer from swimming to the bike in seconds</li>
<li><strong>BIKE_5km_split</strong> - 5K Bike Split time in seconds</li>
<li><strong>BIKE_37_5km_split</strong> - 37.5K Bike Split time in seconds</li>
<li><strong>Bike_To_Run_Transfer</strong> - time to transfer from bike to running in seconds</li>
<li><strong>RUN_3_5km_split</strong> - 3.5K Run Split time in seconds</li>
<li><strong>RUN_4_5km_split</strong> - 4.5K Run Split time in seconds</li>
<li><strong>RUN_8_0km_split</strong> - 8.0K Run Split time in seconds</li>
</ul",False,True
