5901,sentiment-analysis-with-logistic-regression,"# Description

Welcome to your first assignment. You have to implement logistic regression for sentiment analysis on tweets. You will train the logistic model on twitter_sample dataset. Having the model trained, you will be able to decide for any new unseen tweet if it has a positive sentiment or a negative one. To test your model, you will run the inference on GOP debate twitter dataset.

In your notebook, you will develop the following steps:

1. Extract features for logistic regression given some text
2. Implement logistic regression from scratch
3. Apply logistic regression on a natural language processing task
4. Test performance of your logistic regression
5. Perform error analysis

To train the model use the NLTK's Twitter corpus, named [twitter_samples](https://www.nltk.org/howto/twitter.html) which contains 30k of negative and positive tweets.

For testing purposes, use GOP debate twitter dataset which can be found in `Data` section of this competition.
----------------------
# Evaluation

The evaluation metric for this competition is accuracy. 

## Submission Format

**For every tweet in the `test.csv` dataset**, submission file should contain two columns: `id` and `Category`. `Category` should be a predicted sentiment, either 'Positive' or 'Negative' . The`id` should match the 'id' in the `test.csv` file.


The file should contain a header and have the following format:
```
id,Category
0,Negative
1,Positive
...
```","# Dataset Description

**About the Dataset**

This data originally came from Crowdflower's Data for Everyone library.

As the original source says,

> We looked through tens of thousands of tweets about the early August GOP debate in Ohio and asked contributors to do both sentiment analysis and data categorization. Contributors were asked if the tweet was relevant, which candidate was mentioned, what subject was mentioned, and then what the sentiment was for a given tweet. We've removed the non-relevant messages from the uploaded dataset.

The data contains **test.csv** and **sample_submission.csv** files.

## Files

*   **test.csv** - the test set
*   **sample_submission.csv** - a sample submission file in the correct format

## Columns

*   `id` -  id of the tweet
*   `text`?- text of the tweet
*    `Category` - true sentiment label for each tweet

You should predict the sentiment of each tweet in the test.csv file and upload the result in the csv format with just 2 columns: 'id' of the tweet and the predicted 'Category'.",False,True
5902,mlwithpython,"# Description

**Prezentare general?**
Datele au fost ?mp?r?ite ?n dou? grupuri:

setul de antrenament (train.csv)
setul de testare (test.csv)

Setul de antrenament ar trebui s? fie utilizat pentru a construi modelele de ?nv??are automat?. Modelul tau se va baza pe ""caracteristici"" precum sexul ?i clasa pasagerilor, etc. De asemenea, pute?i transforma caracteristicile (features) cu tehnicile invatate in lectiile anterioare pentru a crea noi caracteristici.

Setul de testare ar trebui s? fie utilizat pentru a vedea cat de bine se comport? modelul dvs. pe date nev?zute. Pentru setul de testare, **nu** este inclusa coloana target ('Survived'). Este sarcina ta s? prezici aceste rezultate. Pentru fiecare pasager din setul de testare, utilizeaza modelul pe care l-ai antrenat pentru a prezice dac? acesta a supravie?uit sau nu scufund?rii Titanicului (coloana 'Survived').

De asemenea, am inclus solution_example.csv, ca un exemplu de cum ar trebui s? arate un fi?ier cu solutia.

Dic?ionar de date
| Caracteristica | Definire | Comentarii |
| --- | --- | --- |
| survival | A supravetuit? | 0 = No, 1 = Yes |
| pclass | Clasa Biletului | 1 = 1st, 2 = 2nd, 3 = 3rd |
| sex | Sex |  |
| Age | Vista in ani |  |
| sibsp | # de fra?i/surori/so?i/so?ii la bordul Titanicului|  |
| parch | # de p?rin?i / copii la bordul Titanicului | |
| ticket | Numarul biletului |  |
| fare | Tariful pentru pasageri |  |
| cabin | Numarul Cabinei|  |
| embarked | Portul de ?mbarcare | C = Cherbourg, Q = Queenstown, S = Southampton |

**Detalii despre caracteristici**
pclass: O aproximare a statutului socio-economic (SES)
1st = superior
2nd = mediu
3rd = inferior

varsta: Varsta este frac?ionar? dac? este mai mic? decat 1. Dac? varsta este estimat?, este sub forma xx,5

sibsp: Setul de date define?te rela?iile de familie ?n acest mod:
Sibling = frate, sor?, frate vitreg, sor? vitreg?
Spouse = so?, so?ie (amantele ?i logodnicii au fost ignora?i)

parch: Setul de date define?te rela?iile de familie ?n felul urm?tor...
Parent = mam?, tat?
Child = fiic?, fiu, fiic? vitreg?, fiu vitreg
Unii copii au c?l?torit doar cu o bon?, prin urmare parch=0 pentru ace?tia.

Setul de date si competitia originala sunt indicate aici: https://www.kaggle.com/competitions/titanic/data?select=gender_submission.csv 
----------------------
# Evaluation

**Scop**
Este sarcina ta s? prezici dac? un pasager a supravie?uit sau nu scufund?rii Titanicului.
Pentru fiecare pasagnr din setul de test, trebuie s? prezici o valoare 0 sau 1 pentru 'Survived'.

**Metric?**
Metrica este procentul de pasageri pe care l-a?i prezis corect. Acest lucru este cunoscut sub numele de **acurate?e (accuracy)**.

Formatul fi?ierului de solutie
Trebuie s? incarci un fi?ier csv cu exact 269 randari plus un rand de antet (header row). Dac? ai coloane (?n afar? de PassengerId ?i Survived) sau randuri suplimentare, se va afi?a o eroare.

Fisierul trebuie sa aiba exact doua coloane:
-  PassengerId (ordinea nu conteaza)
-  Survived (contine prezicerile tale: 1 a supravetuit, 0 a decedat)

```
PassengerId,Survived
892,0
893,1
894,0
Etc.
```

Un exemplu poate fi gasit in tab-ul de ""Data"".","# Dataset Description

## Prezentare general?
Datele au fost ?mp?r?ite ?n dou? grupuri:

setul de antrenament (train.csv)
setul de testare (test.csv)

Setul de antrenament ar trebui s? fie utilizat pentru a construi modelele de ?nv??are automat?. Modelul tau se va baza pe ""caracteristici"" precum sexul ?i clasa pasagerilor, etc. De asemenea, pute?i transforma caracteristicile (features) cu tehnicile invatate in lectiile anterioare pentru a crea noi caracteristici.

Setul de testare ar trebui s? fie utilizat pentru a vedea cat de bine se comport? modelul dvs. pe date nev?zute. Pentru setul de testare, **nu** este inclusa coloana target ('Survived'). Este sarcina ta s? prezici aceste rezultate. Pentru fiecare pasager din setul de testare, utilizeaza modelul pe care l-ai antrenat pentru a prezice dac? acesta a supravie?uit sau nu scufund?rii Titanicului (coloana 'Survived').

De asemenea, am inclus solution_example.csv, ca un exemplu de cum ar trebui s? arate un fi?ier cu solutia.",False,True
5903,kcsai2022,"# Description

## The Rule of this competition

This is a beginner's image recognition competition using images of playing cards as the dataset. In this competition, **a pseudo ""poker"" game** is played according to the following evaluation formula, and the team with the largest S is the winner.


$$ S = M\_{acc} \sum\_k N\_k \log(N\_k k)$$

Here, **k** is a number of a card (from 1 to 13), and **M_acc** is a accuracy of model.

Although pseudo, this evaluation formula uses some of the rules of poker, where **N_k** represents the number of cards indexed by k. As in real poker, where ""pairs"" and ""three of a kind"" are used, in the above evaluation formula, the more cards with the same number on them, the higher the score.


As an example, suppose you have six cards in your hand, and the numbers of those cards are 2,2,2,2,3,3, then S / M_acc is 

$$4\times \log(2\times4) + 2\times \log(3\times 2) = 11.901$$

In a real poker game, a player has 5 cards in his or her hand. In this competition, however, 100 cards are classified using machine learning to calculate this evaluation function. (The numbers on the 100 playing cards are randomly sampled from a particular probability distribution.)

On the day of the competition, 100 playing card images will be distributed to each team. Please use the machine learning model you have created in advance to recognize those cards in the images and calculate the value of S

As in the original poker game, the teams are allowed to exchange cards within the time limit, so please work to make the value of S as large as possible.

## Sample of dataset

On the day of the competition, we will distribute 100 images showing the playing cards as follows 
