5914,sasviyaforlearners2022,"# Description

## Introduction

The SAS Viya for Learners Challenge hosted online through Kaggle InClass is geared towards students who are looking to get into and engage with machine learning problems. Students will walk through the data science process and learn how to build machine learning models on a simulated business problem, with a chance to prove their skills on the live leader board.

SAS Viya for Learners is a full suite of cloud-based software that supports the entire analytics life cycle ¨C from data, to discovery, to deployment ¨C and it also lets you code in SAS, Python or R. Machine learning is about using a combination of programming for model building, as well as visual, interactive interfaces to be able to explore data and test assumptions quickly.

### To Enter The Challenge:

* In order to to participate in the challenge, you need to register for access to the SAS Viya for Learners environment
* Please click on the Rules tab and accept the competition rules in order to participate.

## Table of Contents
1. The Challenge Problem
2. Challenge Structure & Getting Started
3. SAS Viya Resources
4. Contact & Acknowledgements

## The Challenge Problem

The World Health Organization(WHO) estimates approximately 17 million deaths occur every year due to cardiovascular diseases, particularly heart attacks and strokes. The heart dataset is a sample from an ongoing cardiovascular study based on residents from the town of Framingham, Massachusetts. The research recorded patients¡¯ information including lifestyle choices, medical heart conditions and other demographic traits. The purpose of this project is to train a model which can be used to predict individuals who are at risk of mortality.

## Challenge Structure
### Getting Started and Entering
To start developing the ML models for this challenge on SAS Viya for Learners, all participants need access to the environment. If you came here from the landing page, you should have an email with a provided credentials for you to access the environment. If you are signing up through Kaggle, please refer to the __SAS Viya For Learners Registration section__ on the left for more details.

Once you have access to the environment, please refer to the [Data](https://www.kaggle.com/c/sasviyaforlearners2021/data) section to understand and walk-through the data that will be used for the challenge.

### Rules

Please refer to the Evaluation and the Submission Requirements sections for more details.

## SAS Viya Resources 

To get you started, please refer to the Notebooks section of the Kaggle Competition page. In this Notebook section, are two programming templates in Python and R that walk-through a machine learning pipeline and build a simple model to get you started with the challenge.

For resources on how to use the SAS Viya graphical user interfaces, please refer to the __SAS Viya for Learners Resources Portal__.

## Contact &amp; Acknowledgements
- Please use the Discussion and Notebooks section for discussion on the challenge 
- Feel free to reach out to the SAS Academic team for any further questions (Academic@oz.sas.com)

Thanks for playing!
----------------------
# Evaluation And Submission Requirements

# Submission to Kaggle

## Submission Requirements

All submissions require the following components to be eligible:

- A CSV containing your model predictions on the test set labelled as submission.csv. This submission.csv is entered through the Kaggle competition page.

- Model code of your SAS model (built using SAS code, or the Python/R APIs). This is your model score code (.sas or .sas + ASTORE) and must be emailed to Academic@oz.sas.com

- Please also link your training notebook as part of your submission!

## Submission CSV Evaluation
All entries are evaluated on a final submission CSV file that contains two columns, ID and Predicted. 'ID' represents the unique Patient ID of the testing set and 'Predicted' is the prediction whether they are 0 (Alive) or 1 (Dead).

```
ID, Predicted
P_033, 1
P_034, 0

```

The scoring metric for the Submission CSV is the Categorization Accuracy.

## SAS Model Code
Along with your submission CSV, you must submit and provide accompanying model files so your submission can be replicated and you demonstrated that you used the SAS Viya procedures to build your model.

The model score code, which is either a .sas file or a combination of .sas &amp; ASTORE. These are scored representations of the model used to score new data.

These files can be emailed to Academic@oz.sas.com with an email titled ""SAS Viya for Learners Submission ###"" where ### is your Kaggle user or your team-name. 
----------------------
# Timeline

## Competition Timeline & Dates

- 8AM 20th June, 2022 - Competition page launches and participants are able to view the data and familiarise themselves with the problem.

- 8AM 18th July, 2022 - Challenge begins. The test dataset will be revealed on the Kaggle page and activated on the environment. Participants can then submit to the Leaderboard. Notebook and modelling templates will also be shared to help get participants started.

- 6PM 22nd July, 2022 - Competition ends and submission deadline.

All deadlines will be AEST (UTC+10) based unless otherwise noted.
----------------------
# Prizes

##Prizes 

Participants get a chance to hone their skills and receive: 

#### 1) SAS Badge for their resume that can also be displayed on LinkedIn. These are digital badges through Acclaim and are a way to display your skills with your LinkedIn network and prospective employers looking for SAS skills. 

There will be two badges offered: 

* A Participants for entering the challenge and making a submission. 
 ![Participants Badge](https://www.googleapis.com/download/storage/v1/b/kaggle-user-content/o/inbox%2F1570418%2F2e74bf1c45d23b8ede6da5f9c5998d28%2FParticipantBadge.png?generation=1593741499565967&alt=media)

* A Winner's Badge for the final Top 3 participants or team on the Leaderboard at the end of the challenge. 
![Winner's Badge](https://www.googleapis.com/download/storage/v1/b/kaggle-user-content/o/inbox%2F1570418%2Fc14af378f7d501afe09cf97fda8550e6%2FWinnerBadge.png?generation=1593741514430259&alt=media)
An email will be sent to the Top 3 Winners on the Leaderboard from the SAS Academic Team (Academic@oz.sas.com) on Monday 25th July 2022.  


#### 2) 4-week Virtual voluntary Internship for only the Top 3 individual entries on the Leaderboard with SAS Institute Australia. SAS Institute is a global leader in analytics, with an award-winning culture, which during this time you will: 

* Work alongside Senior engineers to assess and troubleshoot issues currently being reported by customers 

* Recreate customer issues in test environments using our SAS software, hands on use of SAS environments.  

* Understand process of raising issues internally through to achieving fixes and achieving acceptable outcomes for customers 

* Internship period is for 4 weeks in total and must be taken in January 2023 (from Monday 9 January to Friday 10th February ¨C Full time from 9.00am to 4.30pm Monday to Friday full time) 

* The recipient must also take the following 2 certifications before the commencement: 

 * https://www.sas.com/en_au/certification/credentials/foundation-tools/viya-programming-associate.html 

 * https://www.sas.com/en_au/certification/credentials/foundation-tools/programming-fundamentals.html 

* Upskill by learning base SAS which will set you up to gain your SAS Base Programming certification https://www.sas.com/en_au/certification/credentials/foundation-tools/base-programming-specialist.html which is to be completed at the completion of the internship 

* The internship is a voluntary 4-week program with the primary focus of providing firsthand knowledge and exposure into the real working environment to help you develop your career in analytics.  

 

## Prize Eligibility 

As stated in the Prizes section, you will be awarded: 

#### 1) A Digital SAS Badge - the Top 3 individual entries on the Leaderboard will receive a Winners Badge for submitting an eligible entry (in accordance with the Timeline and Rules stated on the Kaggle competition page) and a Participants badge for all others. 

 * To be eligible to receive the Winner's badge,?your Kaggle account must be registered with an Australian university student email. 

#### 2)  4-week Virtual voluntary Internship for only the Top 3 individual entries on the Leaderboard with SAS Institute Australia 

* To ensure the SAS experience, the internship will be conducted in a hybrid format where applicable. If any of the Top 3 individual entries are located Sydney, they are welcome into the SAS Lane Cove office and allowing you to gain both onsite and virtual exposure. This will be conducted in accordance with the government's COVID-19 guidelines and participants must abide by the SAS' entry requirements upon entry, else the internship will be conducted remotely from the convenience of your own home for those outside the Sydney State. 
* The internship is a voluntary 4-week program with the primary focus of providing firsthand knowledge and exposure into the real working environment to help you develop your career in analytics.  



