# SAS Viya For Learners Resources Portal

## Resources

For the SAS Viya for Learners Challenge, we have created a customised learning portal containing resources to learn how to use the SAS Viya platform. 

To access the portal:
1.	Go to [support.sas.com/myelearn](https://support.sas.com/edu/viewmyelearn.html) and log in to your profile. If you do not currently have a profile, please create one using a link provided on support.sas.com/myelearn.
2.	Once you've logged in to your My Training page, locate the ""To Activate a New Product"" box on the right side of the screen.
3.	Enter the activation code, __*FS00188916252*__ and click Submit.
4.	Review and accept the license agreement.
5.	You should now see the training in your list of active courses
6.	Click on the portal link to access the SAS Viya for Learners resources.

Once you have performed this initial activation, visit [support.sas.com/myelearn](https://support.sas.com/edu/viewmyelearn.html) or select My Training from any page on the SAS training web site and log in to your profile to access the portal.

## Kaggle Introduction

Follow the ""Step-by-Step Guide to Using Viya for Learners for 2022 Kaggle Challenge"" to familiarise yourself with using the Viya platform.","# Dataset Description

## Introduction 
The World Health Organization(WHO) estimates approximately 17 million deaths occur every year due to cardiovascular diseases, particularly heart attacks and strokes. 
The heart dataset is a sample from an ongoing cardiovascular study based on residents from the town of Framingham, Massachusetts. The research recorded patients¡¯ information including lifestyle choices, medical heart conditions and other demographic traits. 
The purpose of this project is to train a model which can be used to predict individuals who are at risk of mortality.
## Data Overview 
The data contains the following fields:
>*  ID - Patient ID
 >*  AgeAtStart - Age at start
 >*  AgeCHDdiag - Age cardiovascular disease (CVD) was diagnosed
  >*  BP_Status - Blood pressure status
  >*  Chol_Status - Cholesterol status
  >*  Cholesterol - Patient's Cholesterol reading
  >*  Diastolic - Patient's Diastolic Blood Pressure
 >*  Height - Patient's Height (Inches)
  >*  MRW - Metropolitan Relative Weight
  >*  Sex- Patient's Sex (Male/Female)
  >*  Smoking - Number of cigarettes per day
  >*  Smoking_Status - Smoking Status
  >*  Status - Patient's Status (1 = Dead/ 0 = Alive)
  >*  Systolic - Patient's Systolic Blood Pressure
  >*  Weight - Patient's Weight (Pounds)
  >*  Weight_Status - Weight status

## Instructions for the Challenge

Instructions for submission and the data will be revealed on the competition start date!

## File Descriptions

