5937,cv-lecture-22-final-project,"# Description

## Semi-Supervised Image Classification Competition

Image classification is a classic task in the Computer Vision domain. In this classification competition, you need to train your model based on 1) a total of 20 classes of labeled images; 2) auxiliary unlabeled images, and predict the type of images in the test set to get as much accuracy as possible.

NOTE: You are NOT allowed to use ImageNet pretrained weights.



----------------------
# Evaluation

We adopt the Categorization Accuracy metric for evaluation.","# Dataset Description

## File descriptions

(Labeled) Training set: `train/`, where images in the same sub-folder are in the same category.
(Unlabeled) Training set: 'unsup/'
Test set: `test/`

File that you need to upload: sample_submission.csv
Note: There is no .txt file, you need to write your own data_loader to process the data.",False,True
