# Evaluation

<h2>Goal</h2>
It is your job to predict the `label`, or species, of each image in the test dataset.
For each image in the test set, you must predict a 0 to 269 value for the label, where 270 is the number of bird species. The bird species can be seen in the `metadata.csv` file on the data tab.<p></p>
<p>The evaluation metric will be multi class accuracy, where discrete class labels must be predicted.</p>


<h2>Submission Format</h2>
<p><strong>For every image in the test dataset</strong>, submission files should contain two columns: `filename` and `label`. Filename should be a string and label should be an integer between 0 and 269.</p>
<p>The file should contain a header and have the following format:</p>
<pre>filename,label<br>test/6fbed82c07cd.jpg,0<br>test/d8399f767c45.jpg,0<br>...<br></pre>","# Dataset Description

