##References

1. Herweg, J.A., Kerekes, J.P., Oliver Weatherbee, David Messinger, Jan van Aardt, Emmett Ientilucci, Zoran Ninkov, Jason Faulring, Nina Raqueno, and Joseph Meola. ""[SpecTIR hyperspectral airborne Rochester experiment data collection campaign.](https://www.spiedigitallibrary.org/conference-proceedings-of-spie/8390/839028/SpecTIR-hyperspectral-airborne-Rochester-experiment-data-collection-campaign/10.1117/12.919268.short)"" (2012). Free Data Available [HERE](http://dirsapps.cis.rit.edu/share-2010/cgi-bin/share-2010.pl).
2. Ientilucci, Emmett J. ""[Target detection assessment of the SHARE 2010/2012 hyperspectral data collection campaign.](https://www.spiedigitallibrary.org/conference-proceedings-of-spie/9472/94720H/Target-detection-assessment-of-the-SHARE-2010-2012-hyperspectral-data/10.1117/12.2177201.short?SSO=1)"" In Algorithms and Technologies for Multispectral, Hyperspectral, and Ultraspectral Imagery XXI, vol. 9472, p. 94720H. International Society for Optics and Photonics, 2015.
----------------------
# Evaluation

The evaluation metric for this competition is [AUC](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Receiver_operating_characteristic). This score is calculated by finding area under the [ROC curve](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Receiver_operating_characteristic).

## Submission Format

Submission files should contain two columns: `pixel_id` and `target`. `pixel_id` represents the numerical ID denoted for each record in the `test.csv`. `target` is a number represents a class label. It should be one of five possible classes `0, 1, 2, 3, 4`.


The file should contain a header and have the following format:
```
pixel_id,target
1,1
```","# Dataset Description

This dataset comes from [SpecTIR Hyperspectral Airborne Rochester Experiment (SHARE)](http://dirsapps.cis.rit.edu/share-2010/cgi-bin/share-2010.pl).

In July 2010, the Digital Imaging and Remote Sensing (DIRS) Laboratory conducted a data colleciton campaign to collect coincident multi-modal imagery data. With the help of SpecTIR, LLC, Kucera International, and a host of people, the SpecTIR Hyperspectral Airborne Rochester Experiment (SHARE) was conducted. This campaign collected imagery using an airborne hyperspectral imager, a laser detection and ranging (LiDAR), and a high resolution multi-spectral imaging system over the Rochester, New York, area July 26 - 29, 2010. The data collected supported of nine simultaneous unique experiments, several of which leveraged data from multi-modalities. In addition to supporting the nine detailed experiments conducted, the impetus for the data collection campaign was to provide a multi-modal data package which would be a resource for additional uni- and multi-modal phenomenology studies. The sites for data collection included the Genesee River, a portion of the city of Rochester which is included as part of the Digital Imaging and Remote Sensing Image Generation (DIRSIG) Mega Scene 1, and the RIT campus itself. As such, open water, wetlands, and urban environments are included in the data set. More detailed information about the data collected, and the experiments previously conducted can be found in [this site](http://dirsapps.cis.rit.edu/share-2010/cgi-bin/share-2010.pl).

##Important!

Please keep in mind that currently that we are in **Phase 2**, so the ground truth is based on the `train_without_leak.csv` and `test_without_leak.csv` with **three possible classes** ((1) Red object, (2) Blue object, (3) Background) for the output.

## Files

*   **train_without_leak.csv** - the training set without a data leaked and reduced the classes to 2
*   **test_without_leak.csv** - the test set without a data leaked and reduced the classes to 2
*   **sample_submission_without_leak.csv** 

## Columns

*   `pixel_id` - ID of each pixel
*   `band_N`?- band value measured from a certain wavelength for a particular pixel. `N` denoted different wavelength used to measure that a band value.
*   `target` - only existed in `train.csv` represents the class assigned to a particular pixel

##References

1. Herweg, J.A., Kerekes, J.P., Oliver Weatherbee, David Messinger, Jan van Aardt, Emmett Ientilucci, Zoran Ninkov, Jason Faulring, Nina Raqueno, and Joseph Meola. ""[SpecTIR hyperspectral airborne Rochester experiment data collection campaign.](https://www.spiedigitallibrary.org/conference-proceedings-of-spie/8390/839028/SpecTIR-hyperspectral-airborne-Rochester-experiment-data-collection-campaign/10.1117/12.919268.short)"" (2012). Free Data Available [HERE](http://dirsapps.cis.rit.edu/share-2010/cgi-bin/share-2010.pl).
2. Ientilucci, Emmett J. ""[Target detection assessment of the SHARE 2010/2012 hyperspectral data collection campaign.](https://www.spiedigitallibrary.org/conference-proceedings-of-spie/9472/94720H/Target-detection-assessment-of-the-SHARE-2010-2012-hyperspectral-data/10.1117/12.2177201.short?SSO=1)"" In Algorithms and Technologies for Multispectral, Hyperspectral, and Ultraspectral Imagery XXI, vol. 9472, p. 94720H. International Society for Optics and Photonics, 2015.",False,True
5975,tss-2022-evaluation-1,"# Description

#  **Evaluation-1: Thapar Summer Scool on ML & DL 2022**

### **Rules:**
