[29] M. Beit-Ari¨¦, ¡°Hebrew codicology,¡± Tentative Typology of Technical Practices Employed in Hebrew Dated
Medieval Manuscripts. Jerusalem, 1981.
[30] M. Beit-Ari¨¦ and E. Engel, Specimens of medieval Hebrew scripts, in 3 vol. Israel Academy of Sciences
and Humanities, 1987, 2002, 2017.
[31] C. Sirat, Hebrew manuscripts of the Middle Ages. Cambridge University Press, 2002.
[32] A. Yardeni et al., The book of Hebrew script: history, palaeography, script styles, calligraphy & design.
Carta Jerusalem, 1997.
[33] B. Richler and M. Beit-Ari¨¦, ¡°Hebrew manuscripts in the Biblioteca palatina in parma: catalogue; palaeo-
graphical and codicological descriptions,¡± 2011.
[34] B. Richler, ¡°Hebrew manuscripts in the vatican library: catalogue,¡± Hebrew manuscripts in the Vatican
Library, pp. 1¨C790, 2008.


