6028,text-or-no-text,"# Description

## Competition Background
Content-based image retrieval (CBIR) has been a hot topic in computer vision for many years. It aims to retrieve images from a database based on the contents of the image. Content-based image retrieval systems are used in a variety of applications, such as search engines, photo sharing websites, stock photo websites, and even in mobile phone galleries. 

## Description
In this competition, we are tasked with simply predicting whether an image contains text or not. It all boils down to a simple binary classification problem. This is useful for searching for images in databases that contain useful information in the form of text, which can be applied in the applications above.
----------------------
# Dataset Info

The data for this competition consists of over 10,000 images, each of which is labeled as ¡°1¡± for images containing text, and ""0"" for images not containing text. The images are of various sizes, and range from various domains, such as outdoor scenes, screenshots, food and food products, artworks, landscapes, architecture, stock photos, diagrams, book pages, memes, and more.

Note that ""text"" can take many forms, such as different languages, printed or handwritten text, etc.

## Dataset Sources
Images from this dataset were scraped from Google Images. If you want to use the competition data for other uses, please keep in mind that the licenses for the images vary, such as Creative Commons, commercial licenses, and others.
----------------------
# Evaluation

This task in this competition is essentially a binary classification task. The **AUC metric** will be used to evaluate your predictions.

## Evaluation
For each image in the test set, predict a probability of it containing text or not. The submission file should have the following columns:
- ""id"": The filename of the test set image
- ""label"": The probability of it containing text or not","# Dataset Description

The data for this competition consists of over 10,000 images, each of which is labeled as ¡°1¡± for images containing text, and ""0"" for images not containing text. The images are of various sizes, and range from various domains, such as outdoor scenes, screenshots, food and food products, artworks, stock photos, diagrams, book pages, memes, and more.

Note that ""text"" can take many forms, such as different languages, printed or handwritten text, etc.

## Dataset Sources
Images from this dataset were scraped from Google Images. If you want to use the competition data for other uses, please keep in mind that the licenses for the images vary, such as Creative Commons, commercial licenses, and others.",False,True
