6076,fcg-2022-netherlands-accommodation-prices,"# Description

## Competition Description
Welcome to the Machine Learning Month 2022. In this competition, you are tasked to use machine learning to determine the rent of properties in the Netherlands. 

## Challenge
The Dutch housing crisis is one of the biggest problems that residents face.

Due to multiple factors, such as population growth and a shortage of construction workers, the availability of housing has decreased significantly. This decline has pushed rent to sky-high prices, which leaves many wondering whether they are being taken advantage of.

In order to answer this question, you are tasked to predict the rent of a house given its data (i.e. location, size, facilities etc.).

## Acknowledgments
The [Netherlands Rent Properties dataset](https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/juangesino/netherlands-rent-properties) that is used in the competition was compiled by Juan Gesino.

---

**Attention:** Winners will be determined not only by leaderboard, but also by their solution. Teams included in the top will have to provide a complete reproducible code with a solution in google colab or jupyter notebook. In the absence of a code (or if the code is not reproducible), the team is not considered for a winning place.

You can use any machine learning model, in particular, you can use any pre-trained models in the process of building a solution. If you are using a pre-trained model, be sure to include its source. Additional datasets not provided in the task cannot be used.
----------------------
# Evaluation

## Goal
It is your job to predict the sales rent price for each accommodation. For each `id` in the test set, you must predict the value of the `rent` variable. 

## Metric
Submissions are evaluated on the [Mean Absolute Error (MAE)](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mean_absolute_error) metric between predicted value and the observed price. 

![formula](https://latex.codecogs.com/svg.latex?%5Ctext%7BMAE%7D%20%3D%20%5Cfrac%7B%5Csum_%7Bi%3D1%7D%5E%7Bn%7D%7B%7Cy_i%20-%20%5Chat%7By_i%7D%7C%7D%7D%7Bn%7D)

## Submission File Format

The file should contain a header and have the following format:

```
id, rent
1, 550
2, 550
4, 550
5, 550
ect.
```

You can download an example submission file (sample_submission.csv) on the [data page](https://www.kaggle.com/competitions/fcg-2022-netherlands-accommodation-prices/data).
----------------------
# New To Kaggle?

## Overview of Kaggle Competitions

1. **Register for the competition**
Read the description, accept the rules, and join the competition.

2. **Build a machine learning model**
Download the [dataset][data] and develop the model locally or using an online hosting service such as [Google Colab][colab]. You can start with our [baseline solution][base] or open it straight in [Google Colab][base_colab].

3. **Make a submission**
Upload your predictions to Kaggle via _Submit Predictions_ button.

4. **Inspect leaderboard standing**
Observe how your model fares against other competitors.

5. **Refine your model**
The competition does not end upon the first submission. Change your code and research other methods. Come to the [lectures](https://www.kaggle.com/competitions/fcg-2022-netherlands-accommodation-prices/overview/timeline) and gain insight to further optimize your model.

