6088,kaggle-workshop,"# Description

Kaggle Workshop Challenge
---
This challenge is a Beginner level competition being organized as a part of the **Kaggle Workshop by Coding Club, IIT Guwahati.**

**The aim of this competition** is to help everyone get familiar with Competitions on Kaggle and so we have tried to keep the dataset relatable and clean.

The problem at hand is a **Multi-Class Classification problem** and the data is regarding the various features of a mobile phone. On the basis of these features one has to predict the price range of a mobile phone.

Here is a handy link to Kaggle's [competition documentation](https://www.kaggle.com/docs/competitions), which includes, among other things, instructions on [submitting predictions](https://www.kaggle.com/docs/competitions#making-a-submission)
----------------------
# Evaluation

Evaluation Metric
---
The evaluation metric for this competition is [Categorization Accuracy](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Accuracy_and_precision#In_multiclass_classification). For example, if a classifier makes ten predictions and nine of them are correct, the accuracy is 0.9 or 90%.

## Submission Format

**For every mobile in the dataset**, submission files should contain two columns: `id` and `price_range`.

The file should contain a header and have the following format:
```
id,price_range
1861,0
```","# Dataset Description



