6106,clu,"# Description

Material backorder is a common supply chain problem, impacting an inventory system service level and effectiveness. Identifying parts with the highest chances of shortage prior its occurrence can present a high opportunity to improve an overall company¡¯s performance. In this competition, you will train classifiers to predict future backordered products and generate predictions for a test set. 
----------------------
# Evaluation

The evaluation metric for this competition is AUC (area under the curve). The AUC (Area Under Curve) is the area enclosed by the ROC curve. A perfect classifier has AUC = 1 and a completely random classifier has AUC = 0.5. Usually, your model will score somewhere in between.
Submission Format

For every sku in the dataset, submission files should contain two columns: sku and went_on_backorder.

The file should contain a header and have the following format:

```
sku, went_on_backorder
1112168, 1
```","# Dataset Description

<h2>File descriptions</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>train.csv</strong> - the training set</li>
<li><strong>test.csv</strong> - the test set</li>
<li><strong>sampleSubmission.csv</strong> - a sample submission file in the correct format</li>
</ul>
<h2>Data fields</h2>
<ul>
<li>sku -sku code
<li>national_inv- Current inventory level of component
<li>lead_time -Transit time
<li>in_transit_qtry - Quantity in transit
<li>forecast_x_month - Forecast sales for the net 3, 6, 9 months
<li>sales_x_month - Sales quantity for the prior 1, 3, 6, 9 months
<li>min_bank - Minimum recommended amount in stock
<li>potential_issue - Indictor variable noting potential issue with item
<li>pieces_past_due - Parts overdue from source
<li>perf_x_months_avg - Source performance in the last 6 and 12 months
<li>local_bo_qty - Amount of stock orders overdue
<li>X17-X22 - General Risk Flags
<li>went_on_back_order - Product went on backorder
<li>Validation - indicator variable for training (0), validation (1), and test set (2)
</ul>",False,True
