6144,kaggle-pog-series-s01e03,"# Description

# It's CORN
Corn image classification competition!
![corn](https://naagar.github.io/cornseedsdataset/img/interpZ0.jpg)

Can you create an algorithm capable of classifying images of corn into one of four categories?
- pure
- broken
- discolored
- silkcut

# Welcome
Welcome to the third competition in the PogChamp series. This series is designed to help new data scientists grow in their knowledge and understanding of machine learning concepts. All are welcome, but viewers of the data science twitch community are especially encouraged to participate. We encourage you to watch Rob's live streams on his twitch channel many Tuesday, Thursday and Sundays 8:30PM-11:30 EST. This competition and much more will be discussed!

New to working with image data? Check out this youtube tutorial: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kSqxn6zGE0c

Winner have the chance to be eligible for some awesome prizes! You must sign up and attend a GTC session in order to be eligible. Sign up using this link: https://nvda.ws/3Qb0b9x


----------------------
# Evaluation

# Evaluation
In this competition you must classify images into one of four categories. You will be scored using [classification accuracy](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Accuracy_and_precision#In_multiclass_classification).

The classification labels are:
- pure
- broken
- discolored
- silkcut

# Submission
Your submission csv should contain two columns. The unique `seed_id` and the `label`.

```
seed_id,label
2,broken
11,silkcut
13,discolored
19,pure
```
----------------------
# Prizes

The top placing teams will be eligible to win prizes, provided that they meet the submission requirements.

<img title=""a title"" alt=""Alt text"" src=""https://bestgamingpro.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/Nvidia-GeForce-RTX-3080-Ti-review-Basically-a-3090-but-1024x683.jpg""  width=""500"">

- **First Place**: NVIDIA RTX 3080 Ti GPU
- **Second and Third Place**: Voucher for NVIDIA's Deep Learning Institute. 
- **Best Notebook**: Top notebooks will be voted on in a Twitch poll. The winner will win a voucher for NVIDIA's DLI.
- **Random Twitch Viewer**: Voucher to NVIDIA's Deep Learning Institute.

Learn more about the [NVIDIA DLI here.](https://www.nvidia.com/dli)

## Qualifications
In order to qualify for the prizes you must:
1. Register for NVIDIA's GTC Conference (it's FREE) using **this link**: https://nvda.ws/3Qb0b9x
2. Take a screenshot or picture of you attending one of the sessions.
3. Follow Rob's [twitch](https://bit.ly/3KBdf52) and [youtube](https://bit.ly/3HVeFpe) channels
4. Be a totally awesome person (oh wait you've already got that covered)

The host maintains the right to disqualify any participants for not following the [rules](https://www.kaggle.com/c/kaggle-pog-series-s01e03/rules) or other valid reasons. Don't worry about this unless you cheat.

I will pay shipping costs under $100 USD. Winners must pay any local customs tax. If the 1st place team consists of more than 1 participant, the prize will be sent to only one teammate.

<img title=""gtc"" src=""https://external-content.duckduckgo.com/iu/?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.thefpsreview.com%2Fwp-content%2Fuploads%2F2020%2F02%2FNVIDIA-GTC-2020-1024x576.png""  width=""500"">","# Dataset Description

The data for this competition contains images of corn. The corn image can be classified in one of four categories. Your model must classify for the test set:
- pure
- broken
- silkcut
- discolored

## Files

*   **train.csv** - the training set
*   **test.csv** - the test set
*   **sample_submission.csv** - a sample submission file in the correct format

* **train/** : Folder containing the png images for the training set
* **test/** : Folder containing the png images for the test set

## Columns

*   `seed_id` - unique id for each image/seed
*   `view`?- either `top` or `bottom`, the angle of the image.
*   `image` the filename of the associated image.",False,True
