1. http://neuralnetworksanddeeplearning.com
2. https://www.deeplearningbook.org","# Dataset Description

The data files contain data of molecular dynamic simulation of FCC metal compression. From the data presented it is possible to derive a constitutive equation, that is, the dependence of the stress state of the material (material response to deformation) on its internal characteristics (e.g., density or temperature)

## Files

*   **train.csv** - the training set (this data contain the temperatures of the deformed system 100 and 500K)
*   **test.csv** - the test set (the data contain the temperatures of the deformed system 300 K)

## Columns

*   `Step` - step of deformation 
*   `Temp`?- current temperature of the system 
*   `Density`?- current density of the system 
*   `Press`?- current pressure of the system 
*   `TotEng`?- total energy of the system 

## Files
*   **shok_wave_measurements.csv** - §Õ§Ñ§ß§ß§í§Ö §Õ§Ý§ñ §á§â§Ö§à§Ò§â§Ñ§Ù§à§Ó§Ñ§ß§Ú§ñ §Þ§Ö§ä§à§Õ§à§Þ PCA

## Columns

*   `H1[m]` - `tw[mks]` - §á§Ñ§â§Ñ§Þ§Ö§ä§â§í §å§Õ§Ñ§â§ß§à§Û §Ó§à§Ý§ß§í
*   `v1[m/s]`?-  `v20[m/s]` - §ä§à§é§Ü§Ú §á§â§à§æ§Ú§Ý§ñ §å§Õ§Ñ§â§ß§à§Û §Ó§à§Ý§ß§í",False,True
6175,2022-neural-network,"# Description

Analysis the data, and predict the quality of the wine.

Input variables (based on physicochemical tests):
1 - fixed acidity
2 - volatile acidity
3 - citric acid
4 - residual sugar
5 - chlorides
6 - free sulfur dioxide
7 - total sulfur dioxide
8 - density
9 - pH
10 - sulphates
11 - alcohol
Output variable (based on sensory data):
12 - quality (score between 0 and 10)

To simply the problem, we transfer quality to two class: bad and good.
If quality <= 5: bad (0)
If quality > 5: good (1)

Acknowledgements: [https://archive.ics.uci.edu/ml/datasets/wine+quality](https://archive.ics.uci.edu/ml/datasets/wine+quality)
