6208,enigma-tech-tatva-2022,"# Description

# Enigma | Tech Tatva 2022

## Fill the form below. It is necessary to determine winners and valid entries.
https://forms.gle/nh45o9Z84sG5Do7M7

# Background
You are hired by a company called AstroGem. This company deals with the buying and selling of precious gems. They receive thousands of requests on their platform from people who want to buy or sell their gems. Your responsibility is to predict the market price of the gem, so that the company can focus on the transactions which generate the most revenue for them, maximizing profit.

# Timings
From: 14th Oct, 2022 : 10 AM
To: 15th Oct, 2022 : 11 PM

# Support
In case of any queries, contact:

Yaswanth B: +91 9177756161


----------------------
# Evaluation

You need to submit your predicted data in the exact format of the given sample submission file

---
You will be evaluated based on your RMSE(Root Mean Square Error) score.

---

In case of a tie in scores, the participant who has submitted earlier shall be considered the victor.

---

## Leaderboard
The final standings will be based on both public and private leaderboards. The data for the public and private leaderboards are split in the ratio: 60%:40%

The final leaderboard will be released on 16th Oct, 2022 : 12PM

--- 

## Submission Format
The file should contain a header and have the following format:
```
id,price
``` 

## NOTE: To fix ""unexpected column"" error:
``
df_for_submission.to_csv('submission.csv', index=False)
``","# Dataset Description

# Files

*   **train.csv** - the training set
*   **test.csv** - the test set
*   **sample_submission.csv** - a sample submission file in the correct format


## Metadata - Column Desciption

*   `Carat` - ?Carat weight of the gem.
*   `Cut`?-  Cut quality of the gem. Quality is increasing order Fair, Good, Very Good, Premium, Ideal.
*   `Color` - ??Colour of the gem : with D being the best and J the worst.
*   `Clarity`?- ??Absence of Blemishes. (In order from Best to Worst, FL = flawless, I3= level 3 inclusions) FL, IF, VVS1, VVS2, VS1, VS2, SI1, SI2, I1, I2, I3
*   `Depth` - ??The Height of the gem, measured from the Culet to the table, divided by its average Girdle Diameter.
*   `Table`?- ??The Width of the gem's Table value expressed as a Percentage of its Average Diameter.
*   `X` - ??Length of the gem in mm.
*   `Y`?- ??Width of the gem in mm.
*   `Z` - ??Height of the gem in mm.",False,True
