6213,heart-disease-prediction-tfug-chd-oct-2022,"# Description

**What is  TFUG X Kaggle Campaign?**
An associated Kaggle Community Competitions hosted by ML GDEs or TFUGs, sponsored by Google Developers.

**Source**
This dataset has been synthetically cured from the original data source using CTGAN, as acknowledged in brief.

**Abstract**
To look into the dataset and classify whether a person is likely or unlikely to have a heart attack.

**About this dataset**
Though no official data is available, according to an estimate, around 1.5-1.7 million people die annually due to heart attack or cardiovascular ailments. Among the casualties, the ratio of young men is comparatively higher than women of their age group.

**Causes and Challenges**
The causes of cardiovascular disease can vary depending on the specific type. For example, atherosclerosis (plaque buildup in your arteries) causes coronary and peripheral artery disease. Coronary artery disease, scarring of your heart muscle, genetic problems, or medications can cause arrhythmias. Aging, infections, and rheumatic disease can cause valve diseases.


**The Role of Machine Learning**
The role of ML here is to use the above parameters to classify whether a person is likely to have a heart attack/disease or not.

**Acknowledgement**
Citations

fedesoriano. (September 2021). Heart Failure Prediction Dataset. Retrieved [Date Retrieved] 
Every dataset used can be found under the Index of heart disease datasets from UCI Machine Learning Repository on the following link: https://archive.ics.uci.edu/ml/machine-learning-databases/heart-disease/

**License**
Public Domain



----------------------
# Evaluation

The evaluation metric for this competition is [Logloss](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cross_entropy).

![](https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/1f3f3acfb5549feb520216532a40082193c05ccc)

![Logloss](https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/80f87a71d3a616a0939f5360cec24d702d2593a2)

## Submission Format

**For every submission**, submission files should contain two columns: `index` and `target`. `index` should be as per the submission.csv file. `target` should have values between 0 and 1.

The file should contain a header and have the following format:
```
index,target
0,1.0
```
