6223,icc-ml-2022a,"# Description

## Welcome To This Competition£¡
Machines have outperformed humans in many tasks. But this is all based on the fact that the data set we provide to the machine is clean and error-free. However, in some application scenarios, the data will be maliciously destroyed by humans, resulting in serious security problems and unsatisfactory performance of the machine. In this mission, a real-world attack and defense scenario is simulated. We are malicious hackers who have damaged and poisoned a batch of data. **Your mission is to find the damaged data samples and clean them as much as possible. On this basis, training a safe machine model and gives correct prediction results.**

## Task Setting:
We set up two tasks, each of which is a 5-class image classification task, and it is worth noting that we damage the datasets in different ways in each of the two tasks.
The score will be calculated on the predicted labels of the test set of the two task datasets.

## Acknowledgements

We thank Zhiyu Lin, Shangxi Wu, Xian Zhao, Ph.D. for organizing this competition.
----------------------
# Evaluation

