6238,electricistan-national-energy-grid,"# Description

## ? Welcome to the Mighty Kingdom of Electricistan!

Electricistan is a kingdom where houses are powered through a network of electrical cables and its energy is produced at different types of power plants ?? ?? ?? . This complex network is also called 'The Grid'. 

The supply voltage in The Grid is 230V and the frequency is 50 Hertz. These values have to be maintained at a consistent level, with a tolerance threshold of +/- 0.050 Hz. Accuracy is important: an increase or drop in frequency can damage equipment or cause a chain reaction and lead to a blackout! ? 

The power output of the system changes every second as electric equipments are turned on and off. To achieve the consistency in voltage and frequency, production has to match the demand. As power plants take time to adjust to changes in consumption, it is crucial to have a precise forecast. ?? 

?? Engineers of Electricistan are calling for your aid! Help them forecast electricity consumption in Megawatts every 15 minutes for the next two weeks as accurately as possible so that security of supply can be guaranteed! To help with the forecasting, they provide you consumption data from previous years. ?? 

 
----------------------
# Evaluation

## Goal
It is your job to predict the necessary power production in Electricistan. 
Submissions are evaluated by [root mean squared error(RMSE)](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Root-mean-square_deviation) between the predicted value and the observed power consumption. 

## Submission File

Submission files should contain two columns: `datetime` and `power`.

The file should contain a header and have the following format:
```
datetime,power
2022.09.15 00:15:00,500
2022.09.15 00:30:00,500
2022.09.15 00:45:00,500
2022.09.15 01:00:00,500
etc.
```
You can download an example submission file (sample_submission_csv.csv) on the Data page.","# Dataset Description

Dates and power consumptions are provided in the training set. 
The test set contains 1729 instances in 15 minutes distances between each other between the 15th of September and the 3rd of October of 2022 (roughly 2 weeks). Power consumption at these instances must be predicted and submitted. 

## Files

*   **train.csv** - the training set
*   **test.csv** - the test set
*   **sample_submission_csv.csv** - a sample submission file in the correct format


## Columns

*   `datetime` - the current date and time
*   `power`?- Power consumption in Megawatts (float)",False,True
