6257,wec-intel-rectask,"# Description

Hi! Let us lay out the task quite plainly - you have to make accurate classifications. There are 7 classes and around 6,000 training samples with 1000 features.  

Build a classfication(any) model with the necessary preprocessing that can accurately classify the test data. 
You can use Google Colab or Kaggle's own environment(in the code section) to build and train your models. A sample notebook has already been provided, along with the datasets for easy access to import into your notebooks.

Drive Folder: https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1t68W1CIumxz9r80ShmOuVTIe63iET6Tx?usp=sharing.



----------------------
# Evaluation

The evaluation metric for this competition is [Accuracy](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Accuracy_and_precision#In_binary_classification). You will be judged not only on your position in the leaderboard, but also the implementation (we will be taking a look at your notebooks). For example, using some form of feature selection would fetch you brownie points.



## Submission Format

**For every test sample in the dataset**, submission csv file should contain two columns: `ID` and `Labels`. As is obvious, every id must have a corresponding label.

If you get a failed submission, even though it looks like the csv file has the right format(when you display it with pandas), you might want to try setting `ID` as index and submitting. 

The file should contain a header and have the following format:
```
ID,Labels
1,1
2,6
3,2
4,2
```","# Dataset Description

The x_train.csv contains the training data without the labels and y_train.csv contains only the train labels. They have already been separated for you. 
## Files

*   **x_train.csv** - the training set without labels
*   **y_train.csv** - the labels for training set
*   **x_test.csv** - the test set
*   **sample_submission.csv** - a sample submission file in the correct format

## Columns

*   `ID` - definition of example_id
*   `Feature 1`?- definition of feature_1
*   etc.",False,True
6258,light-pollution-image-recognition,"# Description

Per la traduzione in italiano, si veda in basso.

This is a community competition on light pollution in the town of Varese, Italy. Varese is a city of about 80,000 inhabitants in northern Italy, 55 km northwest of Milan.

From the hills near Varese, one can have a perfect view over the Po Valley well-known for being worldwide one of the most light-polluted polluted areas.

On 18th October 2022, following ever-increasing energy bills, the city of Varese announced a major cost-saving initiative to reduce light pollution and save a part of the 2 million kilowatt hours in energy bills. Three major monuments will not be lit anymore at night. In addition, the 11000 street lamps will be dimmed overnight, saving 50%.

The dataset contains 32 pictures taken on 28 October 2022 with a Nikon D5000 camera every five minutes from h 19.43 to h 22.18 from the Sacro Monte di Varese, which has an altitude of 807 metres, overlooking Varese located at 382 metres above sea level.

The author wishes to establish a method to understand at what time the lights were either switched off or dimmed and to objectively identify major light-polluting locations. You are free to investigate anything else you might deem interesting.

The dataset was kindly provided by Hendrik Feddersen, Schiaparelli Observatory.

--------------------

Italian translation:

Si tratta di un concorso comunitario sull'inquinamento luminoso della citt¨¤ di Varese, Italia. Varese ¨¨ una citt¨¤ di circa 80.000 abitanti nel nord Italia, 55 km a nord ovest di Milano.

Dalle colline vicino Varese si ha una vista perfetta sulla Pianura Padana, nota per essere una delle zone pi¨´ inquinate da luce artificiale al mondo.

Il 18 ottobre 2022, a seguito di bollette energetiche sempre pi¨´ crescenti, la citt¨¤ di Varese ha annunciato un'importante iniziativa di contenimento dei costi per ridurre l'inquinamento luminoso e risparmiare una parte dei 2 milioni di kilowattora in bolletta energetica. Tre grandi monumenti non saranno pi¨´ illuminati di notte. Inoltre, verr¨¤ ridottto il flusso luminoso nei 11000 lampioni stradali durante la notte, risparmiando il 50%.

Il dataset contiene 32 immagini scattate il giorno 28 ottobre 2022 con una fotocamera Nikon D5000 ogni cinque minuti dalle 19.43 alle 22.18 dal Sacro Monte di Varese, che ha un'altitudine di 807 metri, e domina Varese situata a 382 metri sul livello del mare.

L'autore desidera che venga stabilito un metodo per capire a che ora le luci sono state spente o attenuate e per identificare oggettivamente i principali luoghi di inquinamento luminoso. Chiunque ¨¨ libero di indagare su qualsiasi altra cosa si possa ritenere interessante.

Il dataset ¨¨ stato gentilmente fornito da Hendrik Feddersen, Osservatorio Schiaparelli.022
----------------------
# Evaluation

Per la traduzione in italiano, si veda in basso.

I support the statement that Kaggle is a hub for inspiring content. In this sense, I provided the data set and the challenge. I think it is optimal for gaining experience in a modern image recognition task.

However, I am not in a position to state in advance how submissions will be scored and how students should format their submissions, as I do not know how to solve the challenge. 

I am available to answer any queries and to interact in any discussion.

Italian translation:

Sostengo l'affermazione secondo cui Kaggle ¨¨ un hub per contenuti stimolanti. In questo senso, ho fornito il data se e formulata la sfida. Penso che il data set sia ottimale per acquisire esperienza in una attivit¨¤ moderna di riconoscimento delle immagini.

Tuttavia, non sono in grado di stabilire in anticipo come verranno valutati le submissions e come gli studenti li dovrebbero formattare, poich¨¦ non so come risolvere la sfida.

Sono disponibile a rispondere a qualsiasi domanda e ad interagire in qualsiasi discussione.","# Dataset Description

Per la traduzione in italiano, si veda in basso.

This page contains 32 picture files in NEF format taken from the ""Moses terrace"" at 807 metres over sea level on the Sacromonte near Varese. The google maps location is 45.86018255194705, 8.793759785594766. The camera was fixed always pointing in the same direction.

Here is a nice picture of the statue of Moses overlooking Varese. The pictures were taken from the balcony above the Moses statue on the Sacromonte: http://www.varesefunicolari.org/smonte/gall12.jpg

Nikon Electronic Format (NEF) is a RAW file format for containing digital photos taken by Nikon cameras. NEF format contains every detail of the image captured by the camera sensors.

Each shoot was of 1 second, at ISO 1600 and at an aperture of the objective at 60 mm and F4.5. The camera was a Nikon D5000. The lens was a AF-S Nikkor 18-70 mm f-3.5 to 4.5.

Please note the picture below as it contains a couple of landmarks.
![](https://www.googleapis.com/download/storage/v1/b/kaggle-forum-message-attachments/o/inbox%2F471144%2Fc9ed7d702236e1e2dd22de18597b2959%2FDSC_3674_with%20descriptions.jpg?generation=1667208772747017&alt=media)
--------------------------------------------

Italian translation: 

Questa pagina contiene 32 file immagine in formato NEF tratti dalla ""terrazza del Mos¨¨"" a 807 metri sul livello del mare sul Sacromonte vicino a Varese. La posizione precisa di Google Maps ¨¨ 45.86018255194705, 8.793759785594766. La macchina fotografica era fissa puntando sempre nella sessa direzione.

Ecco una bella foto della statua di Mos¨¨ che domina Varese. Le foto sono state scattate dal balcone in alto: http://www.varesefunicolari.org/smonte/gall12.jpg

Nikon Electronic Format (NEF) ¨¨ un formato di file RAW per contenere le foto digitali scattate dalle fotocamere Nikon. Il formato NEF contiene ogni dettaglio dell'immagine catturata dai sensori della fotocamera.

Ogni scatto era di 1 secondo, ISO 1600 e un'apertura dell'obiettivo a 60 mm e F4.5. La fotocamera era una Nikon D5000. L'obiettivo era un AF-S Nikkor 18-70 mm da f-3.5 a 4.5.

Si prega di notare l'immagine qui sopra in quanto contiene un paio di punti di riferimento.",False,True
