6337,overnight-hackathon,"# Description

## Introduction 
While scrolling Instagram, have you ever encountered filters where you can detect your age or gender while filming yourself for a few seconds? Or various smart ad boards outside various stores? Have you ever wondered how it works? 

**The one-word answer is ¡®AI¡¯.**

**Facial Feature Analysis** has always been a topic of interest in the field of computer vision mainly due to its applicability. 
Especially **Automatic Age estimation** is a challenging problem attracting the attention of the computer vision and pattern recognition communities due to its many practical applications like authentication, human-computer interaction, behavior analysis, product recommendation based on user preferences, and many other areas. Many companies needed age and gender data capture, but few solutions were available.  Artificial neural networks, such as CNN's are a popular tool for tackling this problem, and several datasets which can be used for training models are available but these are few in number.

## Problem Statement
**In this problem you have to predict the age of a person with the help of their image**
----------------------
# Evaluation

####The submissions for this task will be evaluated on [RMSE](https://scikit-learn.org/stable/modules/generated/sklearn.metrics.mean_squared_error.html) between the predicted and actual age.

### Submission File

The CSV Submission file should have the following format.
`img_file , age`
`IMG_1000_HI_F.jpg,      29`
`IMG_10010_FI_M.jpg,       30`
`IMG_10011_HI_F,       31`","# Dataset Description

**Welcome to the first Overnight Hackathon by IITG.ai**

The data used in this competition consist of images of a person and you have to predict the **age** of a person using these images. All the training images have a naming format as given below:

![](https://www.googleapis.com/download/storage/v1/b/kaggle-forum-message-attachments/o/inbox%2F7780743%2Faecfcc4bf621276e9a9c0b956ac9a6d1%2Fform.PNG?generation=1668171657810737&alt=media)
**cnt** - number or id of that image
**gen** - gender of a person in that image
**age** - age of a person in that image



## Files

*   **Train_Images.zip** - the training images
*   **Test_Image.zip** - the testing images
*   **Test_Data.csv** - CSV file to submit your prediction",False,True
