6339,patentapplicationspl,"# Description

You landed your dream job as Junior Data Scientist. You first task is to design and implement a system which will read the contents of each application from Polish patent office and retrieve 3 most important information.  

Your task is to prepare a deep learning model (do NOT use regex) which receives text (and possibly regions) as input and produces 3 predictions: 

- (21) Numer zg?oszenia:  
- (22) Data zg?oszenia: 
- (72) Tw¨®rca(y) wynalazku: 

Unfortunately you received only 90 sample applications but they all have the same structure on the 1st page where all necesseary information is located. 

![](https://www.googleapis.com/download/storage/v1/b/kaggle-user-content/o/inbox%2F12317092%2F334336a2d13cfdea5b4924205e917634%2FMicrosoftTeams-image%20(2).png?generation=1668779399998277&alt=media)

----------------------
# Evaluation

The most important part is your code quality and readability. This is a playground dataset therefore we expect many solutions to have 100% score. The winner will be chosen by the quality and advancement of the model and data processing. 

Even if you didn't get a good test score we encourage you to upload your solution as we are looking for creative minds. 

The Evaluation committee:
1. Mateusz Konopelski
2. Mariusz Dzieci?tko
3. Adrian Kapczy¨½ski","# Dataset Description

Data is available in two destinations: **train** and **test**. 
Each file in **train** has a corresponding key in **train_labels.json**


## Files

*   **train** - the training set
*   **test** - the test set
*   **sample_submission.csv** - a sample submission file in the correct format

## Columns in sample_submission

* `id` -  name of the file [main identifier]
* `category` - joined together 3 information with "";"" separator

Example `category`:
```python
application_no = '111111'  # - application number extracted from PDF
application_date = '14.11.2022' # - application date extracted from PDF
invention_authors = 'Jan Nowak, Arkadiusz Nowak' # - invention authors in the same order as on application 
category = '111111;14.11.2022;JanNowak_ArkadiuszNowak'

```",False,True
6340,nwvs-predict-super-store-profit-s00,"# Description

Predict profit from stores in the Super Store dataset

https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/itssuru/super-store

EVAL METRIC: RMSE
----------------------
# Evaluation

EVAL METRIC: RMSE 

NO CHEATING OR ELSE GULAG","# Dataset Description

<p>The data is about Super Store sales. Contestants will use metadata about Super Store sales to predict profit. Each row is a product and volume of sales for a single product in a given store.</p>

<h2>File descriptions</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>train.csv</strong> - the training set</li>
<li><strong>test.csv</strong> - the test set</li>
<li><strong>sample_submission.csv</strong> - a sample submission file in the correct format</li>
</ul>

<p>The test set (test.csv) is a holdout of several states' orders.</p>

<h3>Data Dictionary</h3>

<ul>
<li><strong>id</strong> unique id per row</li>
<li><strong>ship_mode</strong> what mode was used to ship the item: 'First Class', 'Same Day', 'Second Class', 'Standard Class'</li>
<li><strong>segment</strong> whether the recipient is corporate or consumer</li>
<li><strong>country</strong> always United States</li>
<li><strong>city</strong> where the item was shipped (a city in the United States)</li>
<li><strong>state</strong> where the item was shipped (a state in the United States)</li>
<li><strong>postal_code</strong> ZIP Code in the United States</li>
<li><strong>region</strong> region in the United States: 'Central', 'East', 'South', 'West'</strong></li>
<li><strong>category</strong> type of item: 'Furniture', 'Office Supplies', 'Technology'</li>
<li><strong>sub_category</strong> sub-type of item: 'Accessories', 'Appliances', 'Art', 'Binders', 'Bookcases', 'Chairs', 'Copiers', 'Envelopes', 'Fasteners', 'Furnishings', 'Labels', 'Machines', 'Paper', 'Phones', 'Storage', 'Supplies', 'Tables'</li>
<li><strong>sales</strong> sales made for the order (USD)</li>
<li><strong>quantity</strong> quantity sold of the item</li>
<li><strong>discount</strong> discount applied to the order(from 0 to 1)</li>
<li><strong>profit</strong> profit made on the order (USD)</li>
</ul>",False,True
6341,5-flowers-image-classification,"# Description

For UOS AI class (and for anyone who is interested)

Image classification: 5 kinds of flowers

There are pictures with 5 kinds of flowers.

labels: daisy/dandelion/rose/sunflower/tulip -> 0/1/2/3/4

The labels in submission file should be integer (0/1/2/3/4).

*This data is from https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/alxmamaev/flowers-recognition
----------------------
# Evaluation

The evaluation metric for this competition is Categorization Accuracy.

Labels in your submission file should be integer (or string) type, i.e., 0/1/2/3/4.","# Dataset Description

Image classification: 5 kinds of flowers

