6364,kitchenware-classification,"# Description

![](https://www.googleapis.com/download/storage/v1/b/kaggle-user-content/o/inbox%2F107207%2Fd0bb11646735484d0955492c27d08dd1%2Finbox_107207_f6c4a743fc0aca0bd70d25a92298648d_logo_main3x.png?generation=1669038155750886&alt=media)

In [DataTalks.Club](https://datatalks.club/) we organize an image classification competition. 

In this competition you need to classify images of different kitchenware items into 6 classes:

- cups
- glasses
- plates
- spoons
- forks 
- knives

## Discussion 

The best platform to talk about the competition is the [#competition-kitchenware](https://app.slack.com/client/T01ATQK62F8/C04C7BY3WRF) channel in the DataTalks.Club slack (get the invite [here](https://datatalks.club/slack.html)).

## Who is it for

This competition is open for everyone.

But if you're a student of [Machine Learning Zoomcamp](http://mlzoomcamp.com), you can get extra course points if you participate in the competition. 

## Getting started

<p align=""center"">
    <a href=""https://github.com/DataTalksClub/kitchenware-competition-starter"" target=""_blank"" rel=""noopener"">
        <img src=""https://saturncloud.io/images/embed/run-in-saturn-cloud.svg"" alt=""Run in Saturn Cloud""/>
    </a>
</p>

We have prepared a starter notebook with Keras and SaturnCloud. Check the instructions on how to run it [here](https://github.com/DataTalksClub/kitchenware-competition-starter). You can also see it as a [video](https://www.loom.com/share/c41e5691bd36414fa4df8de9c905cc58). 


## Prizes 

* [RTX 3080 Ti](https://www.nvidia.com/en-us/geforce/graphics-cards/30-series/rtx-3060-3060ti/)
* $3000 in AWS credits
* Up to 40 points for ML Zoomcamp students
* And more!

We encourage active participation, not just the final score that you have. Some prizes will be distributed to encourage participation and learning actively. Don't get discouraged if you see somebody with a 100% score. Focus on learning, and you will get rewarded too.

The next milestone: 15 December. We will distribute $1600 in AWS credits (in $50 vouchers) to the competition participants who scored 25% or more.

For prizes, we will only take into account submissions made after December 5

## Preparing the dataset

We used Toloka for collecting the images for this competition. If you want to know how 
to collect a similar dataset, check this workshop:

https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=POGiLFWxQWQ

If you worked through the workshop and want to contribute extra kitchenware images, share your CSV file in Slack (in the `#competition-kitchenware` channel). We will put these images in this dataset:

https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/agrigorev/kitchenware-extra-images

You can use this data in addition to the main competition dataset and train a better model with it.

## Sponsors

Thanks to the course sponsors for supporting us and making the competition more interesting! 

<a href=""https://toloka.ai/"">
<img src=""https://www.googleapis.com/download/storage/v1/b/kaggle-user-content/o/inbox%2F107207%2Fd4bcf2f3da367a00087b2c2f89afbcda%2Ftoloka.png?generation=1670051275276452&alt=media"" />
</a>



<a href=""https://saturncloud.io/"">
<img src=""https://www.googleapis.com/download/storage/v1/b/kaggle-user-content/o/inbox%2F107207%2F6d08cfbf19792192ba1105a88bbb66e6%2Fsaturncloud%20logo.png?generation=1670496389320868&alt=media"" />
</a>


We also would like to thank 

* [Rustem Feyzkhanov](https://www.linkedin.com/in/ryfeus/) for donating $2000 in AWS Credits
* NVidia for contributing a GPU card to the prize pool
----------------------
# Evaluation

The evaluation metric for this competition is classification accuracy. 


## Submission Format

For each image, the submission should contain the image ID and the prediction for that image

```
Id,label
6534,knife
3504,cup
1649,plate
```

See the sample submissions file in the ""Data"" tab for more details 
----------------------
# Make It Production Ready

Training the most accurate model is great. But that's not the whole story. How difficult would it be to put your model into production?


To participate, you will need to 

- provide a brief description of your solution in your GitHub repo
- (optionally) a blog post

within 2 weeks after the competition ends§ð

To take part, write a message in the competition channel on slack with: 

- a link to your GitHub repository 
- a link to the blog post

## Prizes

We will select winners in the following categories:

- The most production-ready ML solution (the overall winner of the contest)
- The best GitHub repo with a solution
- The smallest model size (measured by the size of the models used in the final solution)
- The best article/blog post about the competition and your solution 
- The most popular article/blog post about the competition and your solution 

The winners in each category will get a certificate.

We will award LinkedIn premium memberships for 6 months (maximum 2 per team) to the team, which produces the best GitHub repo with the closest to the production-ready solution, while still being at the top of the leaderboard score.


## Judging panel

To evaluate the solutions, we will have a judging panel


* Tatiana Habruseva, PhD. Tatiana holds PhD in physics and has a strong background in physics, AI for medicine and machine learning. She led multiple R&D projects both in academia and industry and published 30+ research papers in different domains, including computer vision, medical signals, medical imaging, machine translation, astronomy and laser physics. Tatiana currently works as an AI Tech Lead at LinkedIn, developing recommender systems, knowledge graphs, and taxonomies. Tatiana delivered multiple presentations at PyCon, CVPR, and other events, and has a track record in competitive machine learning, being a competitions Kaggle Master. 
* Arseny Kravchenko. Arseny is a seasoned ML engineer who built and improved multiple highly reliable ML systems for various domains, including real-time video processing, manufacturing optimization and financial transactions analysis. Currently Arseny is co-writing a book named [""Principles of ML system design""](https://arseny.info/ml_design_book). Besides his engineering experience, Arseny has a track record of public speaking on ML-related topics, open source contributions, and competitive machine learning (competitions Kaggle Master","# Dataset Description

This dataset contains images of different kitchenware

## Files

*   **train.csv** - the training set (Image IDs and classes)
*   **test.csv** - the test set (Just image IDs)
*   **sample_submission.csv** - a sample submission file in the correct format
*   **images/** - the images in the JPEG format 

The dataset is released under the CC0 license: you can use it for any purposes, including commercial

## External dataset

You can use external data for this competition, but you must disclose all the datasets you use one week before the competition ends.",False,True
