6369,immobilienrechner-2022,"# Description

Willkommen bei der Kaggle Challenge

Bei diesem Teil der Aufgabe m¨¹sst ihr mit beliebigen Algorithmen das bestm?gliche Modell im Sinne des MAPE entwickeln. Dabei m¨¹sst ihr mindestens drei algorithmische Ans?tze ausprobieren und vergleichen, wobei mindestens ein multiples lineares Modell dabei sein muss. Die verschiedenen Algorithmen m¨¹ssen in eurem Code ersichtlich sein und in eurem Bericht erl?utert sein. Weist dabei auch auf die Vor- und Nachteile der verwendeten Algorithmen hin und wie ihr entschieden habt, welches Modell ihr verwendet.

F¨¹r die Submission hier Predicted den 'price_cleaned' auf dem bereitgestellten Testfile. Die Voraussagen m¨¹ssen zusammen mit der ID hochgeladen werden (Maximal 5 pro Tag). Eine Beispiel Submission ist im Datenteil hier auf Kaggle verf¨¹gbar. Zur Evaluation wird MAPE verwendet, jedoch nur auf einem Subset des kompletten Testsets. Am Ende der Challenge k?nnt ihr 5 Submission ausw?hlen, welche auch auf dem gesamten Testset evaluiert, stellt also sicher, dass ihr nicht overfitted.
----------------------
# Evaluation

The evaluation metric for this competition is the MAPE.

Submission Format
For every real-estate object in the test dataset, submission files should contain two columns: Id and Expecte.

The file should contain a header and have the following format:

```
Id,Expected
1,1
```","# Dataset Description

Dataset
Please use the training and test set provided in class. For your submission, only the ID and Prediction columns are needed. No other columns should be submitted.

Evaluation
We use the MAPE metric to evaluate your solutions. Please note, there is a limit of five submissions to the public leaderboard per day.",False,True
6370,dl-analise-sentimento,"# Description

Essa competi??o acad¨ºmica faz parte da disciplina <b>COC891 - Deep Learning</b> do PEC - Programa de Engenharia Civil - da UFRJ. 

Nessa competi??o voc¨º utilizar¨¢ os conceitos aprendidos em sala de aula para criar um modelo capaz de classificar o sentimento de um coment¨¢rio sobre um filme entre Positivo (1) ou Negativo (0). Os coment¨¢rios est?o em Ingl¨ºs. 

Voc¨º poder¨¢ utilizar quaisquer m¨¦todos aprendidos em sala como Redes Neurais Recorrentes, Redes Neurais Convolucionais ou mesmos realizar uma boa engenharia de atributos com modelos tradicionais de aprendizado de m¨¢quina supervisionado. 
----------------------
# Evaluation

A m¨¦trica de avalia??o da competi??o ¨¦ a ¨¢rea sob a curva ROC, conhecida como: AUC-ROC. (veja uma explica??o em https://developers.google.com/machine-learning/crash-course/classification/roc-and-auc). 

Essa m¨¦trica avalia simultaneamente os indicadores precis?o e revoca??o, al¨¦m de avaliar a qualidade das predi??es (a probabilidade inferida para a classe positiva). Para que se alcance valores pr¨®ximos de 1 no indicador (valor te¨®rico ideal), o seu modelo deve prever probabilidades pr¨®ximas de 1 (ex: 0.99) para sentimentos positivos e pr¨®ximas de 0 (0.01) para sentimentos negativos. 

## Formato de submiss?o

O seu arquivo de submiss?o deve estar em formato csv e possuir as colunas id (mesmo identificador do arquivo test.csv) e sentiment (as probabilidades do seu modelo), como ilustrado abaixo:

```
id, sentiment
0, 0.7
1, 0.02
2, 0.05
```
O arquivo deve possuir 10mil registros, o mesmo n¨²mero do arquivo test.csv disponibilizado.","# Dataset Description

Aqui est?o os dados para treinar e submeter as predi??es dos seus modelos.

## Arquivos

*   **train.csv** - conjunto de treino (voc¨º deve criar sua estrat¨¦gia de valida??o com esses dados)
*   **test.csv** - conjunto de testes (n?o cont¨¦m a coluna com o sentimento)
*   **sample_submission.csv** - exemplo de submiss?o com probabilidades geradas aleatoriamente (distribui??o uniforme)

## Atributos

*   `id` - identificador da avalia??o
*   `review`?- texto da avalia??o, em ingl¨ºs
*   `sentiment`?- 0 para sentimento negativo e 1 para sentimento positivo",False,True
6371,epfl-bio322-2022,"# Description

In an experiment on epigenetics and memory, Giulia Santoni (from the lab of Johannes Gr?ff at EPFL) measured the gene expression levels in multiple cells of a mouse brain under three different conditions that we call KAT5, CBP and eGFP. In this challenge, the goal is to predict - as accurately as possible - for each cell the experimental condition (KAT5, CBP or eGFP) under which it was measured, given only the gene expression levels.

The training data contains the normalized counts for 32285 genes in 5000 different cells together with the experimental condition under which each cell was measured. The test data contains only the normalized counts and your task is to predict the experimental condition.

Please have a look at the [Evaluation](https://www.kaggle.com/competitions/epfl-bio322-2022/overview/evaluation) section for the submission format and the evaluation criterion.
----------------------
# Evaluation

## Evaluation Metric

Your submissions are measured with the classification accuracy metric, i.e. the number of correct predictions divided by the total number of predictions.

## Submission Format

For every cell of the test set you should predict the experimental condition KAT5, CBP or eGFP.

The file you submit should contain a header and have the following format:
```
id,prediction
1,KAT5
2,CBP
3,KAT5
4,eGFP
5,CBP
...
```",# Dataset Description,False,True
