6423,motorcyclehabitprediction,"# Description

## Motivation
This is a playground competition based around binary classification of motorcyclist's behaviour, living in [Moscow, Russia](https://goo.gl/maps/u13fzy5BnhPLtgtB9).

Sometimes it is too cold to ride a motorcycle, sometimes - it's nice weather outside, but sometimes it's cold but there's no rain.
Is it possible to make a prediction based on the date and weather if he will ride a motorcycle? Quite likely.

## Data
There's 2 years worth of data split into 70%/30% by date. Both training and testing data contain weather information from a nearby airport weather station. Data points are irregular, but are at least weekly and at most daily.
Each day is labeled 1 if a motorcyclist chose to ride a motorcycle or considered weather outside suitable for riding and 0 if they didn't ride based of weather. 

## Acknowledgements

Dataset is provided by Kirill Setdekov ([ksetdekov@gmail.com](mailto:ksetdekov@gmail.com))
Weather data included in the dataset is aggregated from [https://rp5.ru/§¡§â§ç§Ú§Ó_§á§à§Ô§à§Õ§í_§Ó_§º§Ö§â§Ö§Þ§Ö§ä§î§Ö§Ó§à,_§Ú§Þ._§¡._§³._§±§å§ê§Ü§Ú§ß§Ñ_(§Ñ§ï§â§à§á§à§â§ä)](https://rp5.ru/§¡§â§ç§Ú§Ó_§á§à§Ô§à§Õ§í_§Ó_§º§Ö§â§Ö§Þ§Ö§ä§î§Ö§Ó§à,_§Ú§Þ._§¡._§³._§±§å§ê§Ü§Ú§ß§Ñ_(§Ñ§ï§â§à§á§à§â§ä))
----------------------
# Evaluation

The evaluation metric for this competition is  [AUC](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Receiver_operating_characteristic#Area_under_the_curve)
 50% of the test data will be used for public leaderboard, and 50% of the data will be used for the final ranking of thee results


## Submission Format

**For every author in the dataset test.csv**, submission files should contain two columns: `Id` and `y`. 
* `Id` matches the `Id` in sample submission file and test.csv
* `y` contains predicted probability of class 1 (rider chose to ride their motorcycle)


The file should contain a header and have the following format:
```
Id,y
256,1
257,0
...
```","# Dataset Description

## FAQ
| Question | Answer |
| --- | --- |
| What files do I need?  | All training info is in **train.csv**, data for evaluation is in **test.csv** and a submission example is in **sample_submission.csv**. |
| Data format: | Tabular data, where each row corresponds to a single day with a date and time stamp in the `time` column.|
| What am I predicting? | Probability of a rider choosing to drive a motorcycle that day. |
| What do column names mean? | Column descriptions are listed below ing the **columns section**  below.|

## Files

*   **train.csv** - the training set
*   **test.csv** - the test set
*   **sample_submission.csv** - a sample submission file in the correct format

## Columns

*   `y` - 1 or 0 if a person chose to use a motorcycle or not this day
*   `Id` - row number 
*    `time` - datetime, rounded to the previous midnight (using .dt.floor('d') method)
*    `T_min`, `T_mean`, `T_max` - minimum, mean and maximum air termperature for the day
*    `P_min`, `P_mean`, `P_max` - minimum, mean and max air pressure in mmHg, converted to sea level pressure
*    `U_min`, `U_mean`, `U_max` - minimum, mean and max relative humidity in % for the day (from 0 to 100)
*    `Ff_min`, `Ff_mean`, `Ff_max1` - minimum, mean and max windspeed in m/s during the day
*    `N_min`, `N_mean`, `N_max` - cloud cover ration from 0 (no clouds) to 1 (full cloud cover)
*    `VV_min`, `VV_mean`, `VV_max` - minimum, mean and max visibility in km (0 - no visibility, 10 - maximum)
*    `RRR_min`, `RRR_mean`, `RRR_max` -  minimum, mean and max precipitation/12 hours in mm (0 - no rain, higher - more rain)?",False,True
