6454,tams-ais-winter-2022-competition,"# Description

# Competition Description
The Texas Asian Mathematics School (TAMS) is an early college program located at the Northern University of Technology (NUT). NUT isn't some second-rate university - it is recognized by the Carnegie Classification as a Tier 3 research institution and is known for its outstanding college food and world-class faculty. Each year, millions of students from across the state of Texas apply for admission to TAMS, with only about two hundred students being selected to enroll at this prestigious school. They are among the best and brightest minds in the world, and at NUT, they will go on to change the world! Students that are accepted rarely even apply to other institutions after their two years at the school because of the exciting TAMS-to-Hawks scholarship, which provides a staggering $20,000 scholarship to TAMS students that decide to continue at NUT, along with automatic admission to the Honors College. 

Your job in this Kaggle competition is to help Dr. Hoover, the Associate Dean of Admissions for TAMS, calculate the admit chance for the applications he's received so far. Not only will it help him provide better admissions decisions, but it will also free up more time for him to help the TAMS population through his awe-inspiring seminars!

Sincerely,
the TAMS Artificial Intelligence Society

*This description is purely fictional. Any resemblance to the real world, whether past, present, or future is purely coincidental.*
----------------------
# Evaluation And Prizes

## Evaluation
Dr. Hoover has decided to use [RMSE](https://www.statisticshowto.com/probability-and-statistics/regression-analysis/rmse-root-mean-square-error/) as the evaluation format for this competition. Apparently, a TAMS student named Vickers Lind impressed the Dean of Research with his very advanced linear regression model, and thus the RMSE was suggested to Dr. Hoover.

## Submission Format

Submission files should contain two columns: `Serial No.` and `Chance of Admit`.

The file should contain a header and have the following format:
```
Serial No.,Chance of Admit
1,1
```

## Prizes
In order to incentivize TAMS students (who are very busy with their ground-breaking research), Dr. Hoover has provided prizes for this competition! The prizes are:

1st Place - CItadel Securities T-shirt
2nd Place - Citadel Securities Water Bottle

(not sponsored)","# Dataset Description

Dr. Hoover has graciously provided us with data about TAMS applicants. The test set comprises 20% of the total data for a total of 80 samples; the data in total has 400 samples. Various predictors are given within the training and test data to help us better predict admissions for Dr. Hoover!

## Files

*   **train_data.csv** - the training set
*   **test_data.csv** - the test set
*   **sample.csv** - a sample submission file in the correct format",False,True
