# Evaluation

# Evaluation

## Goal

The goal is to predict whether a pixel is an 'Argania' tree or # Evaluation

## Metric

The score will be the [F1 Score](https://developers.google.com/machine-learning/crash-course/classification) of classified genomes.

## Submission Format

**For every genome in the dataset**, submission files should contain two columns: `id` and 'cover'. 

The file should contain a header and have the following format:
```
id,species
1,'Argania'
2,'Not_Argania'
```

## This is a Model Competition
The participants are required to submit 3 parts:

### 1. A Submission file
The submission file should contain a header with two columns:

id: a number that contains the id of the tree.

cover: a string is either 'Argania' or 'Not_Argania'.

The submission file must be named submission.csv. 

This will allow you to see your ranking on the public leaderboard of the competition.

### 2. A Jupyter Notebook

A Jupyter notebook of the code you wrote to create this solution.

The file name should be 'team\_name\_genome\_classifier.ipynb'. Please include the team¡¯s name in the filename. 

**This part will be requested after the end of the competition.**

### 3. The model
The trained model 'team\_name\_genome_classifier.*'. Please include the team¡¯s name in the filename. 

This part will be requested after the end of the competition to validate the results.

### 4. External Data
If the team used any external data, we will request them to share the dataset they used to collaborate on creating a solid Dataset for future work on this problem.
