6572,ml-olympiad-book-recommendations-tfug-hajipur,"# Description

ML Olympiad - TFUG Hajipur hosts Book Recommendations challenge

# Welcome to the 2023 edition of the ML Olympiad!??

[**Download assets for participants**](https://drive.google.com/file/d/1pBzQdy49LSxaQ6HuBWn_k2ZjVGBb4ayf/view?usp=sharing)

# About
The main goal of evaluating the Goodreads dataset is to gain a solid understanding of the connections between the various characteristics that books may have, including their overall ratings, author variations over time, and language diversity.

# Role of Applied ML
Structured use of applied machine learning is important in a book recommendation system. It uses algorithms to assess a lot of information about users' reading inclinations, preferences for books and reading histories to suggest books they would enjoy. Based on each user's unique preferences, this data is then used to create customized recommendations for them. Collaborative filtering, content-based filtering, and matrix factorization are a few methods frequently employed in book recommendation systems. These methods are made to offer users precise and relevant recommendations, assisting them in finding new publications they would like.


# **Dataset**
The original dataset is from [bahramjannesarr](https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/bahramjannesarr/goodreads-book-datasets-10m). That was entirely scrapped from the [Goodreads API](https://www.goodreads.com/api). We have modified the original dataset such that the users will not be able to use the IDs from the existing dataset.

# What's the Challenge?
In this competition, your aim is to train a machine learning model based on the Goodreads dataset provided to you in the training file and further recommend best books.

### Show some excitement on socials 
* Share your progress using this hashtag on Twitter: #MLOlympiad #TFUGHajipur

### Book Sample
```json
 {
    ""Id"": ""101"",
    ""Name"": ""The Catcher in the Rye"",
    ""pagesNumber"": 277,
    ""RatingDistTotal"": ""total:2610840"",
    ""PublishMonth"": 30,
    ""PublishDay"": 1,
    ""Publisher"": ""Back Bay Books"",
    ""CountsOfReview"": 44046,
    ""PublishYear"": 2001,
    ""Language"": ""eng"",
    ""Authors"": ""J.D. Salinger"",
    ""ISBN"": ""0316769177"",
    ""Rating"": 3.8,
    ""RatingDist1"": ""1:133165"",
    ""RatingDist2"": ""2:224884"",
    ""RatingDist3"": ""3:553476"",
    ""RatingDist4"": ""4:808278"",
    ""RatingDist5"": ""5:891037""
 }
```


# Acknowledgements
**Citations**
We thank Google Developers and ML Developer Programs for sponsoring this competition.
Thanks to Nari Yoon, Hee Jung, Soonson Kwaon for the guidance and support.
- **TensorFlow User Group Hajipur**
#MLOlympiad 
#AppliedML
`#TFUGHajipur` `#TFUG`
----------------------
# Evaluation

# Evaluation Metrics

The evaluation metric for this competition is [Mean F1-Score](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/F-score). The F1 score, commonly used in information retrieval, measures accuracy using the statistics precision ""p"" and recall ""r"". Submissions are evaluated on MeanFScore, which at Kaggle is actually a **micro-averaged F1-score**.

The F1 metric weights recall and precision equally, and a good retrieval algorithm will maximize both precision and recall simultaneously. Thus, moderately good performance on both will be favored over extremely good performance on one and poor performance on the other.
----------------------
# Frequently Asked Questions

###  What is ML Olympiad?
An associated Kaggle Community Competitions hosted by Google ML communities, supported by Google Developers. (ML GDEs, TFUGs, or 3rd party ML communities host ML community competitions on Kaggle, and ML Developer Programs team sends rewards to hosts of registered competitions.)

### What is Kaggle Community Competitions?
Kaggle¡¯s community running competitions. The feature was announced in 2022, as an extended form of ¡°InClass competitions¡±. It lets anyone can create and host a competition at no cost.
https://www.kaggle.com/c/about/community

### Are there any restrictions?
- Google doesn¡¯t support competitions in Crimea, North Korea, Quebec, the so-called Donetsk People's Republic, and Luhansk People¡¯s Republic, and where prohibited by law. This program follows Google Coding Competitions Terms, see 1. Eligibility section on competition regulations for more details.


### Old Timeline
- **Start Date** - January 29, 2023
- **Entry Deadline** - Same as the Final Submission Deadline
- **Final Submission Deadline** - February 22, 2023

###New Timeline
- **Entry Deadline** - Same as the Final Submission Deadline
- **Final Submission Deadline** - February 28, 2023

All deadlines are at 11:59 PM UTC on a corresponding day unless otherwise noted. The competition organizers reserve the right to update the contest timeline if necessary.





