6613,precision-heartbeat-detection,"# Description

Join us in this exciting machine learning competition aimed at predicting the risk of heart disease using SCG data. With the help of advanced algorithms and techniques, you will have the opportunity to make a real impact in this field.
![](https://www.googleapis.com/download/storage/v1/b/kaggle-user-content/o/inbox%2F13166594%2F296069d924bf05aa6328becf0b76f78a%2Fusing%20scg.jpg?generation=1676228066409385&alt=media =800x400)

Data scientists, machine learning experts, and healthcare professionals are invited to participate in this challenge. Use your skills to analyze the largest dataset of SCG records and develop predictive models that will help doctors and patients better understand and prevent heart disease. This competition is the perfect opportunity to showcase your skills and make a difference in the lives of millions of people.

So what are you waiting for? Sign up now and help us tackle one of the biggest health challenges of our time. Your contributions could save lives and lead to more effective treatments for heart disease.
Start your journey to a healthier future today!
----------------------
# Heart Desease Early Detection 

![](https://www.googleapis.com/download/storage/v1/b/kaggle-user-content/o/inbox%2F13166594%2F77a025834a1df8327db30cb7ada1afe4%2Fheart.jpg?generation=1676228609536694&alt=media)
The early detection of heart disease is critical for preventing serious health complications and reducing the risk of death. By detecting heart disease in its early stages, individuals can take steps to manage their condition and make lifestyle changes to reduce their risk of future problems.

Some of the benefits of early detection of heart disease include:

Early treatment: If a heart disease is detected early, treatment can be started promptly, which can help to slow its progression and reduce the risk of serious complications.

Reduced risk of heart attack: Early detection of heart disease can help to identify individuals who are at high risk of a heart attack. This can help them take steps to prevent a heart attack from occurring, such as making lifestyle changes, taking medications, or undergoing procedures to open blocked arteries.

Improved outcomes: When heart disease is detected early, the prognosis is generally better than if it's detected later. Early treatment can help to preserve heart function and prevent serious health problems from developing.

Better quality of life: By detecting heart disease early, individuals can make changes to improve their overall health and well-being, which can lead to a better quality of life.

In conclusion, early detection of heart disease is essential for reducing the risk of serious health complications and improving health outcomes. It's recommended to have regular check-ups with a healthcare provider, maintain a healthy lifestyle, and seek prompt medical attention if you experience any symptoms that could indicate a heart issue.
----------------------
# Seismocardiography (SCG)

Seismocardiography (SCG) is a non-invasive technique for recording the mechanical vibrations generated by the heart. It involves placing a special sensor, called an accelerometer, on the chest to measure the vibrations generated by the beating heart. These vibrations are then recorded and analyzed to determine the heart rate and rhythm, and to assess the mechanical function of the heart. SCG has been used in various medical and research applications, such as the evaluation of heart disease, the study of heart mechanics, and the development of cardiac prostheses. The SCG method is a simple and cost-effective alternative to traditional ECG and echocardiography, and has the potential to provide important information about cardiac function in a variety of settings.

Accurate detection of heartbeats in SCG signals is a critical aspect of cardiac care. In order to effectively diagnose and treat heart disease, it is important to have a precise understanding of a patient's cardiac function.
![](https://www.googleapis.com/download/storage/v1/b/kaggle-user-content/o/inbox%2F13166594%2Fd279eb3958a0b8a9ef4ddefe8900c4bd%2Fscg1.jpg?generation=1676228008921527&alt=media)

One of the biggest challenges in SCG analysis is the accurate detection of heartbeats. This requires separating the SCG signal into individual heartbeats, and accurately measuring various parameters, such as heart rate, rhythm, and morphology. However, this task can be difficult due to various factors, including the presence of noise and artifacts in the SCG signal, as well as the variability in SCG waveform between patients.","# Dataset Description

The dataset contains SCG signal segments. Part of the segments contains the ""Ventricular ejection"" phase of the cardiac cycle.
![](https://www.googleapis.com/download/storage/v1/b/kaggle-user-content/o/inbox%2F13166594%2F9d87b9e36d2e615e8feafa3f0854ae62%2Fezgif.com-gif-maker.gif?generation=1676222906021707&alt=media)

![](https://www.googleapis.com/download/storage/v1/b/kaggle-user-content/o/inbox%2F13166594%2F10b15a7d90931f0b98fd7e2f8bbf11da%2Fezgif.com-gif-maker%20(1).gif?generation=1676222968754946&alt=media)

## Files

*   **train.csv** - the training set
*   **test.csv** - the test set


## Columns

*   `Id` -id of sample 
*   `Category`?
*   other columns - segments normalized data",False,True
