6692,math80600a-w23,"# Description

In this competition (homework 2), you are requested to solve the classify papers based on their title and abstract into 19 categories. See here for the official HW2 description.

## Pipeline
You can do whatever you want on the training data (train.csv), and then make the predictions for the test data (test.csv). See the sample submission ('sample.csv') for what your submission should look like.

## More Hints on Training Techniques
You can practice all the techniques you learned in class. Other strategies you can use to improve the performance:

- Split your training data into train, validation, and test sections so that you can evaluate your model before testing it on test.csv with Kaggle.
- Data augmentation.
- Cross-validation and hyperparameter tuning.
   - Learning rate decay.
   - Early stopping on the validation set.
- Model ensemble.
----------------------
# Evaluation

For this homework, we will evaluate your score based on your results and also your codes. To submit your codes, please fill in [the Google forum](https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSfcK31V4E16aSN1G26BHqcdmn2qGcPLO7RAlJRvbU_blrUz8g/viewform?usp=sf_link), and provide the link in the section ``The link of your Colab code assignment''. You can put your code on dropbox/gist/google drive..., but don't forget to enable TAs to access your codes.

