6696,spr-x-ray-age,"# Description

# Attention: the competition deadline was rescheduled to 1 day before. See the [Timeline](https://www.kaggle.com/competitions/spr-x-ray-age/overview/timeline) for more details.

The [Radiology and Diagnostic Imaging Society of S?o Paulo (SPR)](http://www.spr.org.br), with [Amazon Web Services](https://aws.amazon.com/), is organizing the Artificial Intelligence Challenge to determine gender and age using chest X-rays for the first time. And all healthcare professionals and data scientists worldwide are invited to participate.

The challenge is to create a model capable of predicting the patient's gender and age group through chest X-rays. To ensure the success of this activity, SPR invited institutions to collaborate with the donation of tens of thousands of images; this data allows participants to create artificial intelligence algorithms to indicate the gender and age of the patient.

This action aims to encourage initiatives that present in advance potential identification errors that could harm the patient, in addition to promoting scientific and educational activities for the Radiology and Diagnostic Imaging community.

The first 50 participants who submit solutions to the leaderboard will earn $30 credits to use on any AWS service - the participant can only use this credit on their AWS account.

The top three winners of the competition will be acknowledged during Jornada Paulista de Radiologia (JPR) 2023. All participants are invited to [register ](https://jpr2023.org.br/inscricao/congressista) and participate in JPR.

## About SPR

For 54 years, SPR has promoted scientific updating and continuing education within the highest principles of professionalism.

With an eye on the future, the organization is often looking to bring dynamism to its work and great prominence to everyone in its community, aiming to be well-recognized nationally and intentionally.

SPR is responsible for the S?o Paulo Radiological Meeting (JPR), its most significant event, and is also considered the biggest congress of the specialty in Latin America.

JPR2023 will take place in the Transamerica Expo Center in S?o Paulo - SP, on April 27-30.


**********************************************************************

### This is the age prediction competition. The page for the gender prediction competition is [this](https://www.kaggle.com/competitions/spr-x-ray-gender/). Both competitions use the same dataset and the same dataset partition. Winners might or might not be the same for both competitions.

----------------------
# Evaluation

The evaluation metric for this competition is the mean absolute error ([MAE](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mean_absolute_error))


## Submission Format

**For every image in the dataset**, submission files should contain two columns: `imageId` and `age`. 

Age should be a number of years old.

The file should contain a header and have the following format:
```
imageId,age
1,23
```

----------------------
# Timeline

Start of the competition - Feb 28, 2023

### Submission deadline - Apr 26, 2023 23:59 UTC (20:59 BRT)


Disclosure of results during [JPR 2023](http://www.jpr2023.org.br) - Apr 27-29, 2023
