6725,ml-olympiad-bahrain-ncsc,"# Description

# Who is GDG Manama?

GDG Manama is a community-led group that is part of the global Google Developer Groups (GDG) network. The group is based in Manama, Bahrain, and is dedicated to promoting and supporting the local developer community.

GDG Manama hosts regular events, workshops, and meetups that bring together developers, entrepreneurs, and technology enthusiasts to share knowledge and expertise on a wide range of topics related to software development, cloud computing, machine learning, and more.

So if you are a developer, entrepreneur, or technology enthusiast based in Bahrain or the surrounding region, be sure to check out GDG Manama and join the community of like-minded individuals who are passionate about using technology to drive positive change in the world.


# Introduction

Welcome to the phishing classification competition hosted by GDG Manama on Kaggle!

This competition challenges participants to build powerful machine-learning models that can accurately distinguish between phishing webpages and legitimate webpages based on a set of features extracted from these webpages.

The dataset for this competition consists of 48 features extracted from 5000 phishing webpages and legitimate webpages. The webpages were downloaded from different sources, including PhishTank, OpenPhish, Alexa, and Common Crawl. 

To participate in this competition, participants will use this dataset to train and validate their models, with the goal of building models that can accurately classify webpages as phishing or legitimate. The evaluation metric for this competition will be the F1 score, which is a harmonic mean of precision and recall.

To ensure that the competition is fair and unbiased, participants will be given access to a standardized dataset and evaluation metric. The top performers will be awarded prizes and recognition, and their models may even be used in real-world applications to combat phishing attacks.

So if you are passionate about machine learning and are interested in contributing to the fight against phishing attacks, join the phishing classification competition hosted by GDG Manama and compete with other talented data scientists!



# Participant Confirmation:

By participating in this competition, you agree to the following:

Abide by the competition rules and guidelines set forth by GDG Manama and Kaggle.
Only use the provided dataset and refrain from using external data sources or pre-trained models.
Use ethical and fair practices when building and training models, and avoid any form of data manipulation or bias.
Agree to have your models and submissions evaluated and potentially used in real-world applications.
Agree to have your name and affiliation published in the competition leaderboard and any related publicity materials.
Refrain from sharing your submission code with others or attempting to hack or compromise the competition platform in any way.
Accept that the decision of the competition judges is final and cannot be challenged or disputed.
Agree to indemnify and hold harmless GDG Manama, Kaggle, and any related sponsors from any claims, damages, or liabilities arising from your participation in the competition.

## Acknowledgements

Synthetic Version of the [original dataset](https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/h3cgnj8hft/1)

Original Dataset Source: 
> Tan, Choon Lin (2018), ¡°Phishing Dataset for Machine Learning: Feature Evaluation¡±, Mendeley Data, V1, doi: 10.17632/h3cgnj8hft.1
----------------------
# Evaluation

* Welcome to the evaluation page for the phishing classification competition hosted by GDG Manama!

* The goal of this competition is to build powerful machine-learning models that can accurately distinguish between phishing webpages and legitimate webpages based on a set of features extracted from these webpages.

* The evaluation metric for this competition is the F1 score, which is a harmonic mean of precision and recall.

* You will submit your predictions for a test dataset consisting of 1000 webpages, which will be used to calculate your F1 score.

* Note that your submissions will be evaluated based on their F1 score, which is a weighted average of precision and recall.

* A perfect F1 score is 1.0, while a score of 0.0 indicates poor performance.

* At the end of the competition, the top performers will be awarded prizes and recognition, and their models may even be used in real-world applications to combat phishing attacks.

* Good luck, and thank you for participating in the phishing classification competition!","# Dataset Description

The dataset for this competition consists of 48 features extracted from 5000 phishing webpages and legitimate webpages. To participate in this competition, participants will use this dataset to train and validate their models using the `train_data.csv` and `val_data.csv`, with the goal of building models that can accurately classify webpages as phishing or legitimate. The evaluation metric for this competition will be the F1 score, which is a harmonic mean of precision and recall.



## Files

*   **train_data.csv** - the training set
*   **val_data.csv** - the validation set
*   **test_data.csv** - the test set
*   **sample_submission.csv** - a sample submission file in the correct format

> **Note**: Make sure that your submission is in the same format as the sample submission


## Columns


| Column Name                      | Description                                                                               |
|---------------------------------|-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|
| id                              | A unique identifier for each observation.                                                |
| NumDots                         | The number of dots in the URL.                                                            |
| SubdomainLevel                  | The number of subdomains in the URL.                                                      |
| PathLevel                       | The number of levels in the URL path.                                                      |
| UrlLength                       | The length of the URL.                                                                     |
| NumDash                         | The number of dashes in the URL.                                                           |
| NumDashInHostname               | The number of dashes in the URL hostname.                                                  |
| AtSymbol                        | Whether or not the URL contains an '@' symbol.                                             |
| TildeSymbol                     | Whether or not the URL contains a '~' symbol.                                              |
| NumUnderscore                   | The number of underscores in the URL.                                                      |
| NumPercent                      | The number of percentage signs in the URL.                                                 |
| NumQueryComponents              | The number of components in the URL query string.                                          |
| NumAmpersand                    | The number of ampersands in the URL.                                                       |
| NumHash                         | The number of hash symbols in the URL.                                                     |
| NumNumericChars                 | The number of numeric characters in the URL.                                               |
| NoHttps                         | Whether or not the URL uses HTTPS.                                                         |
| RandomString                    | Whether or not the URL contains a random string.                                           |
| IpAddress                       | Whether or not the URL contains an IP address.                                             |
| DomainInSubdomains              | Whether or not the URL domain is contained in the subdomains.                              |
| DomainInPaths                   | Whether or not the URL domain is contained in the path.                                    |
| HttpsInHostname                 | Whether or not the URL hostname contains HTTPS.                                            |
| HostnameLength                  | The length of the URL hostname.                                                            |
| PathLength                      | The length of the URL path.                                                                |
| QueryLength                     | The length of the URL query string.                                                        |
| DoubleSlashInPath               | Whether or not the URL path contains two consecutive slashes.                              |
| NumSensitiveWords               | The number of sensitive words in the URL.                                                  |
| EmbeddedBrandName               | Whether or not the URL contains an embedded brand name.                                    |
| PctExtHyperlinks                | The percentage of external hyperlinks in the HTML code.                                    |
| PctExtResourceUrls              | The percentage of external resources in the HTML code.                                     |
| ExtFavicon                      | Whether or not the HTML code contains an external favicon.                                 |
| InsecureForms                   | Whether or not the HTML code contains insecure forms.                                      |
| RelativeFormAction              | Whether or not the HTML code contains a relative form action.                              |
| ExtFormAction                   | Whether or not the HTML code contains an external form action.                             |
| AbnormalFormAction              | Whether or not the form action in the HTML code is abnormal.                               |
| PctNullSelfRedirectHyperlinks   | The percentage of self-redirecting hyperlinks that point to null.                          |
| FrequentDomainNameMismatch      | Whether or not there is a frequent domain name mismatch in the self-redirecting hyperlinks. |
| FakeLinkInStatusBar             | Whether or not the HTML code contains a fake link in the status bar.                        |
| RightClickDisabled              | Whether or not right-clicking is disabled on the HTML page.                                 |
| PopUpWindow                     | Whether or not the HTML code contains a pop-up window.                                      |
| SubmitInfoToEmail               | Whether or not the info get submitted into the email |",False,True
