6831,mrs-spring-2023-battery-prediction-challenge,"# Description

## Welcome to the MRS Spring 2023 MD00 Symposium! We have a Battery Prediction Challenge for you. 

This afternoon, you were given the usage data of 108 old batteries, where a ""remaining usage life (RUL)"" value, until when the batteries will retire, was labelled for each battery. Your task was to predict the RUL for 19 unknown old batteries based on their featurized usage data.

## Enter the Competition
- *Kaggle Leaderboard*: submit your predicted RUL for 19 old batteries in the test dataset on Kaggle, your submission will be ranked by MAE ([mean absolute error](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mean_absolute_error#:~:text=In%20statistics%2C%20mean%20absolute%20error,an%20alternative%20technique%20of%20measurement.)). 

## Deadline of submission on Kaggle: 
**4.30 pm PDT, Monday, April 10, 2022 **

## Acknowledgements
We thank authors of [this paper](https://www.nature.com/articles/s41560-019-0356-8) for providing the dataset, Dr. Amalie Trewatha and Dr. Steven Torrisi for helping with the demo notebook.
----------------------
# Evaluation

The evaluation metric for Kaggle Leaderboard is the [[mean absolute error]((https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mean_absolute_error#:~:text=In%20statistics%2C%20mean%20absolute%20error,an%20alternative%20technique%20of%20measurement.)]) between predicted and the ground truth remaining useful lifetime (RUL) for the 19 batteries in the test dataset.

**What should I submit?**
To enter the Kaggle Leaderboard: your submission file (.csv) should contain two columns: Cell ID and Predicted Remaining Useful Life","# Dataset Description

## Training and test dataset

- train_data.csv contains 108 batteries, each with seven features and a remaining useful life (prediction target) labeled.
- test_data.csv contains 19 batteries not in the train_data.csv, each with seven features provided.
- example_submission.csv contains an example submission file in the correct format.

Please submit a csv file on Kaggle that contains two columns: 19 Cells IDs in the test dataset, and your predicted remaining useful life (RUL) for each battery.",False,True
