6888,nwds-xswing,"# Description

# Expected Swing Community Competition 
Using MLB Statcast data from Baseball Savant, use the selected columns of data to predict whether a pitch will result in a swing. 

The competition lasts until May 21st at 11:59pm US Eastern Time and winners will be announced on stream on May 22nd. 

For a chance at a free sub (for you or someone else) please:
1. Post your notebook to the ""Code"" section 
2. In your notebook, please state at the top or the bottom who you would like the sub to go to (i.e. Please gift the sub to nickwan_datasci) 
3. If you place in the top 5, I will gift the account you listed a sub. 
4. The top winner with a posted notebook will also get an additional prize! 

Check out the stream here: 
https://twitch.tv/nickwan_datasci  

Join the discord to talk about data science and sports analytics here:  
https://discord.gg/GR5p4ZY

----------------------
# Evaluation

The competition will evaluate submissions based on log loss. If you are interested in sharing your notebook and walking through your code with Nick on stream, leave a message in the discord, on the discussion board, or submit your notebook! 

The competition lasts until May 21st at 11:59pm US Eastern Time and winners will be announced on stream on May 22nd.

Check out the stream here:
https://twitch.tv/nickwan_datasci

Join the discord to talk about data science and sports analytics here:
https://discord.gg/GR5p4ZY","# Dataset Description

This dataset includes only pitches and excludes any pickoff, steals, or caught stealing events. A ""swing"" is one of the following labels in the `description` column: 
`'foul', 'swinging_strike','hit_into_play', 'foul_tip','swinging_strike_blocked'`

This dataset is from 2020-2022 MLB season.  

The data comes from MLB Statcast via Baseball Savant. Please reference the Baseball Savant Statcast Search CSV documentation for a data dictionary: 
https://baseballsavant.mlb.com/csv-docs  

Some columns are unique to this competition. These are: 
- pitch_uid: a unique ID for each pitch in the dataset 
- attack_zone: these are based off of Baseball Savant's ""Attack Zones"" 
- swing: whether a pitch produced a swing event 

Note: It is possible to cheat fairly simply. Please do not cheat! There are no financial prizes, cheating is pointless! 

# The benchmark sample solution 
The sample solution is a simple weighted average between the batter and pitcher. The pitcher average is a mean using pitcher, pitch type, batter side, pitcher throw hand, the and attack zone. The batter average is the same thing except instead of pitcher, batter is used. If there is no data for a batter or a pitcher, an average without batter or pitcher ID is used. The weighted average is 60% batter and 40% pitcher -- this is under an arbitrary assumption that the batter chooses to swing and therefore should command a little more weight than the pitcher.",False,True
6889,af-ii-2023-i-object-localization,"# Description

Han sido contratados por una gran startup del sector agr¨ªcola para desarrollar un modelo predictivo que tiene que determinar la localizaci¨®n y tipo de diferentes vegetales que aparecen en una imagen. Se le proporciona un conjunto de datos que contiene im¨¢genes y sus anotaciones correspondientes. Se garantiza que cada imagen contiene solo un objeto de tres clases posibles, su modelo debe detectar qu¨¦ tipo de objeto es y d¨®nde se encuentra.

----------------------
# Evaluation

## Evaluaci¨®n 

- **CNN personalizado:**

Cree un modelo de red neuronal convolucional personalizado como backbone (features extractor) y entr¨¦nelo desde cero (1,5 puntos)

- **Predicci¨®n del cuadro delimitador (Bounding box):**

Implemente una cabeza de regresi¨®n que se alimenta con las caracter¨ªsticas extra¨ªdas del backbone convolucional. (1 punto)

- **Clasificaci¨®n de objetos:**

Implementar una cabeza de clasificaci¨®n que se alimenta con las caracter¨ªsticas extra¨ªdas del backbone convolucional (1 punto)

- **Transferir aprendizaje (Transfer learning):**

Usar dos modelos preentrenados como backbones y conectar los creados previamente cabezas de clasificaci¨®n y regresi¨®n para recibir entradas de ellas. (1 punto)

- **Aumento de datos (Data Augmentation):**

Compara el uso de diferentes t¨¦cnicas de aumento de datos para ver su impacto en el desempe?o de ambas tareas (clasificaci¨®n y regresi¨®n) (0,5 puntos)

- **Competencia**

Adicionalmente, al tratarse de una competencia, seg¨²n la posici¨®n en la misma se otorgar¨¢n puntos de bonificaci¨®n de la siguiente manera:

* Primer grupo: 1 punto
* Segundo grupo: 0.6 puntos
* Tercer grupo: 0.3 puntos

Tengan en cuenta que deben seguir un protocolo correcto de evaluaci¨®n para evitar la fuga de datos de los conjuntos de prueba en los pasos de procesamiento de datos. Los errores ser¨¢n sancionados (-0,5 puntos cada uno). 
La m¨¦trica de evaluaci¨®n para esta competencia es el [coeficiente de dados] (https://www.kaggle.com/code/yerramvarun/understanding-dice-coefficient/notebook) para la tarea de regresi¨®n de cuadro delimitador y [accuracy](https://developers.google.com/machine-learning/crash-course/classification/accuracy) para la tarea de clasificaci¨®n de objetos. 

## Submission 

**Para cada conjunto en el conjunto de datos**, los submission deben contener las siguientes columnas: 
* `nombre de archivo`, el nombre de archivo de la imagen 
* `clase`, la clase predicha","# Dataset Description

## Files

*   **train.csv** - the training set
*   **test.csv** - the test set
*   **sample_submission.csv** - a sample submission file in the correct format
*  **images.zip** - images folder",False,True
