- Multi-class accuracy is a performance metric used in machine learning to measure the accuracy of a multi-class classification model. It is calculated by dividing the number of correctly classified instances by the total number of instances in the dataset.

>The formula for multi-class accuracy is : accuracy = (number of correctly classified instances) / (total number of instances)

- Multi-class accuracy is an important metric because it provides a measure of how well a model is performing overall in correctly classifying instances into multiple classes.","# Dataset Description

