6916,datathon23-machine-learning-competition,"# Description

This challenge serves as an ML competition for the ""Datathon'23 Machine Learning Competition"" held by the IBA Data Science Society.

Participants are expected to build models that can accurately predict energy consumption for the industry based on the provided data.

Can you predict the load type for the industry?
By solving this competition, you will be able to apply and enhance your data science skills.
----------------------
# Evaluation

The evaluation metric for this competition is [Accuracy]
(https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Accuracy_and_precision#In_binary_classification). The accuracy is the proportion of correct predictions (both true positives and true negatives) among the total number of predictions.","# Dataset Description

You are provided with dataset about energy (electricity) usage of manufacturing industry. The information gathered is from the DAEWOO Steel Co. Ltd in Gwangyang, South Korea. It produces several types of coils, steel plates, and iron plates. The information on electricity consumption is held in a cloud-based system.
The task is to predict the variable Load_Type of energy in a industry.

## Files

