6960,text-overlap-prediction,"# Description

![](https://www.googleapis.com/download/storage/v1/b/kaggle-user-content/o/inbox%2F12312654%2Fec48542309bb23cf41a8706db2bda50b%2FDribbble%20shot%20-%206.png?generation=1683912883517734&alt=media)

#Problem Statement
You are given an Image of 1080x1080 px and in this, there is a human structure and some text in it.
Your task is to create a model which can detect that in a given input image the text of an image overlap the human structure or not, if there is an overlap then it is a bad image and if there is no overlap of text then it is a good image.


## Solution
Use any Python framework, libraries, or models or create and define your own model using our training data set.

- Top 10 submissions will be evaluated using other test data set and if they found cheating then their submission will be deleted

## Acknowledgements
We thank Ayush Gupta for providing this problem statement.
----------------------
# Evaluation

#Goal
The goal of this competition is to take an image and determine whether there is text overlapping or not.
For every image in the test set, you should predict the correct label.

#Metric
This competition is evaluated on the categorization accuracy of your predictions (the percentage of images you get correct).

#Submission File Format
The file should contain a header and have the following format:
```
ImageId, TextOverlap
1, True
2, False
3, True
4, False
5, False
etc..
```","# Dataset Description

## Files
There are 3 items in the data.
- **sample_submission.csv** - the format in which the answer should be submitted
- **testing data**  - folder which has 20 images and one needs to predict the text overlapping over these images and submit as **sample_submission.csv** format
- **training data** - the folder which has 180 images for model training 

## About Images
- Image Dimension - **1080 x 1080**
- Width - **1080 pixels**
- Height - **1080 pixels**
- Horizontal Resolution - **72 dpi**
- Vertical Resolution - **72 dpi**
- Bit depth - **24** 

##Submission File Format

###Columns
*   `ImageId` - Id/Name of the test image
*   `TextOverlap`?- whether there is text overlap or not.
- True  for text overlap
- False for no text overlap

```
ImageId, TextOverlap
Instagram post - 1.jpg, True
Instagram post - 2.jpg, False
Instagram post - 3.jpg, True
Instagram post - 4.jpg, False
Instagram post - 5.jpg, False
etc..
```",False,True
