6974,sas-viya-for-learners-challenge-2023,"# Description

# **Introduction**
The SAS Viya for Learners Challenge hosted online through Kaggle InClass is geared towards students who are looking to get into and engage with machine learning problems. Students will walk through the data science process and learn how to build machine learning models on a simulated business problem, with a chance to prove their skills on the live leader board.

SAS Viya for Learners is a full suite of cloud-based software that supports the entire analytics life cycle ¨C from data, to discovery, to deployment ¨C and it also lets you code in SAS, Python or R. Machine learning is about using a combination of programming for model building, as well as visual, interactive interfaces to be able to explore data and test assumptions quickly.

## **To Enter The Challenge:**
- In order to participate in the challenge, you need to register for access to the SAS Viya for Learners environment
- Please click on the Rules tab and accept the competition rules in order to participate.

# **Table of Contents**
1.  The Challenge Problem
2.  Challenge Structure & Getting Started
3.  SAS Viya Resources
4.  Contact & Acknowledgements

# **The Challenge Problem**
The bank_train data set is a sample taken from a large financial services firm accounts. Accounts in the data represent consumers of home equity lines of credit, automobile loans, and other types of short-term to medium-term credit instruments. The challenge involves analysing the latest campaign for the firm. The campaign is used to denote all marketing efforts that provide information about and motivate the contracting (purchase) of the bank¡¯s financial services products. The purpose of the project is to train a model which can be used to predict if a customer of the bank will purchase an insurance product from the bank for the current campaign.

# **Challenge Structure**

### **Getting Started and Entering**
To start developing the ML models for this challenge on SAS Viya for Learners, all participants need access to the environment. If you came here from the landing page, you should have an email with a provided credentials for you to access the environment. If you are signing up through Kaggle, please refer to the SAS Viya For Learners Registration section on the left for more details.

Once you have access to the environment, please refer to the [Data](https://www.kaggle.com/competitions/sas-viya-for-learners-challenge-2023/data) section to understand and walk-through the data that will be used for the challenge.

### **Rules**
Please refer to the Evaluation and the Submission Requirements sections for more details.

# **SAS Viya Resources**
To get you started, please refer to the Notebooks section of the Kaggle Competition page. In this Notebook section, are two programming templates in Python and R that walk-through a machine learning pipeline and build a simple model to get you started with the challenge.

For resources on how to use the SAS Viya graphical user interfaces, please refer to the SAS Viya for Learners Resources Portal.

# **Contact & Acknowledgements**
Please use the Discussion and Notebooks section for discussion on the challenge
Feel free to reach out to the SAS Academic team for any further questions (Academic@oz.sas.com)
Thanks for playing!
----------------------
# Evaluation And Submission Requirements

# Submission to Kaggle


## Submission Requirements

All submissions require the following components to be eligible:
- A CSV containing your model predictions on the test set labelled as submission.csv. This submission.csv is entered through the Kaggle competition page.
- Model code of your SAS model (built using SAS code, or the Python/R APIs). This is your model score code (.sas or .sas + ASTORE) and must be emailed to Academic@oz.sas.com
- Please also link your training notebook as part of your submission!

## Submission CSV Evaluation

All entries are evaluated on a final submission CSV file that contains two columns, ID and Predicted. 'ID' represents the unique Account ID of the testing set and 'Status' is the prediction whether they accept the offer (1) or not (0).

``` ID, Status P_033, 1 P_034, 0 ```

The scoring metric for the Submission CSV is the Categorization Accuracy.

## SAS Model Code

Along with your submission CSV, you must submit and provide accompanying model files so your submission can be replicated and you demonstrated that you used the SAS Viya procedures to build your model. The model score code, which is either a .sas file or a combination of .sas &amp; ASTORE. These are scored representations of the model used to score new data. These files can be emailed to Academic@oz.sas.com with an email titled ""SAS Viya for Learners Submission ###"" where ### is your Kaggle user or your team-name.
----------------------
# Prizes

## **Prizes**

Participants get a chance to hone their skills and receive:

**1) SAS Badge for their resume that can also be displayed on LinkedIn. These are digital badges through Acclaim and are a way to display your skills with your LinkedIn network and prospective employers looking for SAS skills.**
There will be two badges offered:

- A Participant's Badge for entering the challenge and making an eligible submission.
![Participants Badge](https://www.googleapis.com/download/storage/v1/b/kaggle-user-content/o/inbox%2F11084107%2F895f5a6f413c05f67b9793034003435a%2Finbox_1570418_2e74bf1c45d23b8ede6da5f9c5998d28_ParticipantBadge.png?generation=1686109383610333&alt=media)

- A Winner's Badge for the final Top 3 participants on the Leaderboard at the end of the challenge.
![Winner's Badge](https://www.googleapis.com/download/storage/v1/b/kaggle-user-content/o/inbox%2F11084107%2Ff984513a267cd8dd66c52e93c8347db3%2Finbox_1570418_c14af378f7d501afe09cf97fda8550e6_WinnerBadge.png?generation=1686109402287353&alt=media)
An email will be sent to the Top 3 Winners on the Leaderboard from the SAS Academic Team (Academic@oz.sas.com) on Monday **ADD DATE**.

**2) 3-month voluntary internship for only the Top 3 eligible individual entries on the Leaderboard with SAS Institute Australia. SAS Institute is a global leader in analytics, with an award-winning culture, which during this time you will:**

- Work alongside senior engineers to assess and troubleshoot issues currently being reported by customers.

- Recreate customer issues in test environments using our SAS software, hands on use of SAS environments.

- Understand process of raising issues internally through to achieving fixes and achieving acceptable outcomes for customers.

- Internship period is for 3 months in total and must be taken in from 12th of January 2026, either full time or part-time.

- The recipient must also take the following 2 certifications before the commencement:
https://www.sas.com/en_au/certification/credentials/foundation-tools/viya-programming-associate.html
https://www.sas.com/en_au/certification/credentials/foundation-tools/programming-fundamentals.html

- Upskill by learning base SAS which will set you up to gain your SAS Base Programming certification https://www.sas.com/en_au/certification/credentials/foundation-tools/base-programming-specialist.html which is to be completed at the completion of the internship

- The internship is a voluntary 3-month program with the primary focus of providing firsthand knowledge and exposure into the real working environment to help you develop your career in analytics.

## **Prize Eligibility**
As stated in the Prizes section, you will be awarded:

**1) A Digital SAS Badge - the Top 3 individual entries on the Leaderboard will receive a Winners Badge for submitting an eligible entry (in accordance with the Timeline and Rules stated on the Kaggle competition page) and a Participants badge for all others.**
- To be eligible to receive the Winner's badge,?your Kaggle account must be registered with an Australian university student email.

**2) 3-month voluntary internship for only the Top 3 eligible individual entries on the Leaderboard with SAS Institute Australia**
- To ensure the SAS experience, the internship will be conducted in a hybrid format where applicable. If any of the Top 3 individual entries are located in either Sydney, Melbourne, Brisbane or Canberra, they are welcome into the SAS local office. The internship will be conducted remotely from the convenience of your own home for those outside of these states.
----------------------
# Timeline

## Competition Timeline & Dates
- 8AM Friday 14th July to 16th July, 2023 - A scheduled maintenance on the platform will be conducted. Accessibility will be limited - We do not recommend accessing the platform during this timeframe.
- 8AM Monday 17th July, 2023 - Challenge begins. The test dataset will be revealed on the Kaggle page and activated on the environment. Participants can then submit to the Leaderboard. Notebook and modelling templates will also be shared to help get participants started.
- 6PM Friday 21st July, 2023 - Competition ends and submission deadline

All deadlines will be AEST (UTC+10) based unless otherwise noted.

If there are any technical issues please use the SAS Chatbox or email sasviyaforlearners@sas.com. 
----------------------
# SAS Viya For Learners Registration

## Registration
In order to to participate in the challenge, you need to register for access to the SAS Viya for Learners environment. This environment is a 24/7, cloud-based environment where you will have access to the SAS Viya analytics platform in order to build models for the challenge.

To register, please visit the following link and sign-up for access:
https://www.sas.com/en_au/events/2023/sas-viya-for-learners-challenge.html

After applying, you should receive an email notice. Please follow the instructions specified in the email notice to navigate into the SAS Viya for Learners environment.
----------------------
# SAS Viya For Learners Resources Portal

## Resources
For the SAS Viya for Learners Challenge, we have created a customised learning portal containing resources to learn how to use the SAS Viya platform.

To access the portal:
1. Go to [support.sas.com/myelearn](support.sas.com/myelearn) and log in to your profile. If you do not currently have a profile, please create one using a link provided on support.sas.com/myelearn.
2. Once you've logged in to your My Training page, locate the ""To Activate a New Product"" box on the right side of the screen.
3. Enter the activation code, ***FS00879186899*** and click Submit.
4. Review and accept the license agreement.
5. You should now see the training in your list of active courses
6. Click on the portal link to access the SAS Viya for Learners resources.

Once you have performed this initial activation, visit [support.sas.com/myelearn](support.sas.com/myelearn) or select My Training from any page on the SAS training web site and log in to your profile to access the portal.

## Kaggle Introduction
Follow the ""Step-by-Step Guide to Using Viya for Learners for 2023 Kaggle Challenge"" to familiarise yourself with using the Viya platform.","# Dataset Description

