7050,practice-hackathon,"# Description

This competition is a **Practice Hackathon** as part of **Machine Learning.AI 2023**, a primer course on Data Science and Machine Learning,  conducted by IITG.ai club.

**IITG.ai** is a platform for the AI community of IITG to discuss, learn and collaborate on advancements in the field of AI. We have created a culture of contributing to and improving AI's dynamic, fast-changing world.

Here is a handy link to Kaggle's [competition documentation](https://www.kaggle.com/docs/competitions), which includes, among other things, instructions on [submitting predictions](https://www.kaggle.com/docs/competitions#making-a-submission).

Before starting make sure you go through the [Rules](https://www.kaggle.com/competitions/practice-hackathon/rules) to understand the format of the leaderboard and know about the rules regarding submissions.

Also, we have provided a **[starter notebook](https://www.kaggle.com/code/sreeharic/ml-ai-week-4-starter-notebook)** to get an idea of how to approach this competition. 

To understand how your submissions are scored on the leaderboard, go through the evaluation tab, we have provided details on the metrics used to score your submission.

The score given to you on the course leaderboard for this hackathon will be dependent on your score on the private leaderboard, we will also require **notebook submissions from all participants**. The course leaderboard scores will depend significantly on the **quality of your work** you show, not just your private LB score.
----------------------
# Evaluation

The evaluation metric for this competition is [RMSE](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Root-mean-square_deviation) Score. The RMSE score, is a frequently used measure of the differences between values (sample or population values) predicted by a model or an estimator and the values observed.

![](https://www.googleapis.com/download/storage/v1/b/kaggle-user-content/o/inbox%2F9048870%2F672cade07cd543fae332233362f139fe%2Frmse.png?generation=1686638513551031&amp;alt=media)

