<h1>Train Set:</h1>
The train set is the dataset provided to participants for developing and training their models. It typically contains a set of input features and corresponding target variables or labels. Participants use this data to build and optimize their machine learning models. The train set is often larger than the test set to provide enough data for effective model training.

<h1>Test Set:</h1>
The test set is another dataset provided to participants, but it does not include the target variables or labels. Participants use their trained models to make predictions on this dataset, and then submit those predictions to Kaggle for evaluation. The test set mimics real-world data that the model will encounter after deployment, allowing participants to assess their model's generalization capabilities.

<h1>Sample Submission:</h1>
The sample submission file is a template provided by Kaggle, representing the format in which participants should submit their predictions. It usually includes a unique identifier for each data point in the test set and a corresponding column for the predicted target variable. Participants need to fill in the predictions in this file using their trained models.

<h1>What about cross-validation:</h1>
It is optional. You can split the train set yourself for cross-validation.","# Dataset Description

