Welcome to the ""Predicting Stock Market Price Movement"" competition! 

In this challenge, you will tackle the exciting task of predicting the movement of stock market prices using an **extremely imbalanced dataset.**

The stock market is known for its dynamic and unpredictable nature, making accurate predictions a valuable skill. However, the **imbalanced** nature of this dataset presents an additional challenge, as the occurrence of price movements is heavily skewed towards one class. This competition aims to push the boundaries of predictive modeling by addressing this real-world scenario.

You will be provided with a comprehensive dataset containing historical price and market indicators for various stocks. The dataset encompasses both bullish and bearish movements, with a significant imbalance in favor of **one of three classes**. Your goal is to build a robust machine learning model that can effectively identify and predict these movements, demonstrating a strong understanding of class imbalance handling techniques.

**Good luck, and may the best model prevail!**
----------------------
# Evaluation


The evaluation metric for this competition is Mean F1-Score.

If you will write a notebook, please mention F1-Scores for each class.

